/* GARP SCR 学習目標（LO）別 練習問題（第4〜7章・全51LO×各3問）。自作。事実はIPCC・UNFCCC・BCBS・NGFS・TCFD・ISSB・GHG Protocol・PCAF・ICMA・LMA・ESMA等の公開一次資料で裏取り。GARP の教材本文・模擬試験・章末問題は使っていない */
const SCR_LO47_DATA = [
  {"f":"SCR:Ch4 政策・ガバナンス","q":"[LO 4.1] Which sequence places these milestones of international climate policy in the correct chronological order?","h":"国連条約→京都議定書→パリ協定→グラスゴー気候合意の順です。","c":["The UNFCCC was adopted (1992), then the Kyoto Protocol (1997), then the Paris Agreement (2015), then the Glasgow Climate Pact (2021).","The Kyoto Protocol was adopted (1997), then the UNFCCC (1992), then the Paris Agreement (2015), then the Glasgow Climate Pact (2021).","The UNFCCC was adopted (1992), then the Paris Agreement (2015), then the Kyoto Protocol (2017), then the Glasgow Climate Pact (2021).","The Paris Agreement was adopted (2015), then the UNFCCC (2017), then the Kyoto Protocol (2019), then the Glasgow Climate Pact (2021)."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 国際気候政策は、1992年の枠組条約→1997年の京都議定書→2015年のパリ協定→2021年のグラスゴー合意と進んだ。<br><br><b>解説</b> 1992年（リオ地球サミット）にUNFCCCが採択され、1994年に発効した。京都議定書は1997年にCOP3で採択され、先進国に数値目標を課した。パリ協定は2015年のCOP21で採択され、2016年に発効した。グラスゴー気候合意は2021年のCOP26の成果文書で、1.5℃目標の追求や、排出削減対策のとられていない石炭火力の段階的削減に言及した。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 枠組条約より前に京都議定書が来る並びや、京都議定書がパリ協定の後に採択されたとする並びは、年号が合わない。<br><br><b>日本との対応</b> 日本は京都議定書（COP3）の議長国で、1990年比6%削減（2008〜2012年）を約束した。<br><br>【出典】UNFCCC, History of the Convention, https://unfccc.int/process/the-convention/history-of-the-convention ／ UNFCCC, Kyoto Protocol, https://unfccc.int/kyoto_protocol ／ 環境省, 京都議定書の概要（COP3議長国・日本の目標）, https://www.env.go.jp/council/06earth/y060-22/mat01_2.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch4 政策・ガバナンス","q":"[LO 4.1] Which statement about the Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change (IPCC) and its role in the evolution of climate policy is correct?","h":"IPCCは科学を評価する機関で、政策の決定や処方は行いません。","c":["It was set up in 1988 by the WMO and UNEP to assess the scientific literature, and its reports inform UNFCCC negotiations without prescribing policy.","It was set up in 1997 under the Kyoto Protocol to verify national inventories, and it can impose penalties on Parties that miss their targets.","It was set up in 1992 at the Rio summit as the UNFCCC negotiating body, and its assessment reports set the binding targets for each country.","It was set up in 1988 by the WMO and UNEP to run its own satellites and ground stations, and it recommends the specific policy each government must adopt."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> IPCCは1988年にWMOとUNEPが設置した科学評価の機関で、報告書は交渉の科学的根拠になるが政策は処方しない。<br><br><b>解説</b> IPCCは自ら観測や研究を行わず、公刊された科学文献を評価する。1990年の第1次評価報告書は、枠組条約の交渉開始を後押しした。評価報告書は「政策に関連するが、政策を処方しない（policy-relevant, not policy-prescriptive）」ことが原則。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 京都議定書の下で排出量を検証・制裁する機関ではなく、交渉機関でもない。独自の衛星・観測網を持つわけでもない。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, History of the IPCC, https://www.ipcc.ch/about/history/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch4 政策・ガバナンス","q":"[LO 4.1] Which statement best captures a key shift in approach between the Kyoto Protocol (1997) and the Paris Agreement (2015)?","h":"トップダウンの数値割当から、各国が決める貢献を積み上げる方式への転換です。","c":["Voluntary pledges from developed countries gave way to quantified, legally binding targets for every Party, enforced by financial penalties set by a compliance committee, with targets reviewed only once a decade.","Quantified, legally binding targets for developed (Annex I) countries gave way to nationally determined contributions from nearly all Parties, reviewed through a five-yearly global stocktake.","A focus on mitigation by developing countries gave way to a focus on adaptation by developed countries, with no mitigation commitments remaining for any Party.","Market-based mechanisms were introduced under Kyoto and then removed under Paris, which relies only on national regulation with no role for international carbon markets."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 京都は先進国への割当、パリは全締約国の自主的貢献と5年ごとの見直しが特徴。<br><br><b>解説</b> 京都議定書は附属書I国（先進国）に法的拘束力のある数値目標を課した。パリ協定は、ほぼ全ての国が自ら決める貢献（NDC）を提出し、5年ごとに更新・前進させる枠組みで、グローバル・ストックテイクで全体の進捗を点検する。なお京都にも排出量取引・CDMなどの市場メカニズムがあり、パリ協定は6条で市場・非市場の協力を位置づけている。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> パリの遵守委員会は促進的・非懲罰的で、金銭罰を科さない。市場メカニズムは京都でも導入され、パリで廃止されたわけではない。<br><br><b>日本との対応</b> 日本は2025年2月に新NDC（2013年度比で2035年度60%・2040年度73%削減）を提出した。<br><br>【出典】UNFCCC, The Paris Agreement, https://unfccc.int/process-and-meetings/the-paris-agreement ／ UNFCCC, Kyoto Protocol, https://unfccc.int/kyoto_protocol ／ 環境省, 日本のNDC, https://www.env.go.jp/earth/earth/ondanka/ndc.html"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch4 政策・ガバナンス","q":"[LO 4.2] Which statement correctly distinguishes annual, cumulative and per-capita CO2 emissions across major emitters in recent years?","h":"「年間」「累積」「1人当たり」で順位が変わる点がポイントです。","c":["India is the largest annual emitter, China has the largest cumulative historical emissions, and Indian per-capita emissions are several times those of the United States.","The United States is the largest annual emitter, the European Union has the largest cumulative historical emissions, and per-capita emissions are similar in all large economies.","China is the largest annual emitter, the United States has the largest cumulative historical emissions, and US per-capita emissions are several times India's.","China is the largest annual emitter and the largest cumulative emitter, and its per-capita emissions are the lowest among all major economies including India."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 年間では中国が最大、累積では米国が最大、1人当たりでは米国がインドの数倍。<br><br><b>解説</b> Global Carbon Budgetなどの推計では、中国が年間CO2排出の最大国で、米国が累積排出量の最大国である。1人当たり排出量は米国が中国やEUより高く、インドは世界平均を下回る。「どの指標で見るか」で責任の見え方が変わることが、共通だが差異ある責任（CBDR）の議論の背景にある。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> インドは年間でも累積でも最大ではなく、1人当たりも低い。中国の1人当たりはインドより高い。<br><br>【出典】Our World in Data, CO2 emissions, https://ourworldindata.org/co2-emissions"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch4 政策・ガバナンス","q":"[LO 4.2] According to the IPCC AR6 Working Group III Summary for Policymakers (2022), which comparison of 2019 per-capita greenhouse gas emissions is accurate?","h":"最貧国の1人当たり排出量は世界平均の4分の1程度です。","c":["Least Developed Countries emitted about 6.1 tCO2e per capita, compared with a global average of about 6.9 tCO2e per capita.","Least Developed Countries emitted about 1.7 tCO2e per capita, compared with a global average of about 6.9 tCO2e per capita.","Least Developed Countries emitted about 3.3 tCO2e per capita, compared with a global average of about 6.9 tCO2e per capita.","Least Developed Countries emitted about 9.5 tCO2e per capita, compared with a global average of about 6.9 tCO2e per capita."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 2019年の1人当たりは、後発開発途上国が約1.7tCO2e、世界平均が約6.9tCO2e。<br><br><b>解説</b> IPCC AR6 WGIII SPMは、後発開発途上国（LDC）と小島嶼開発途上国（SIDS）の1人当たり排出量が世界平均より大幅に低いと述べる（LDC 1.7、SIDS 4.6、世界平均 6.9 tCO2e/人、CO2-LULUCFを除く）。LDCが世界の排出に占める割合も約3.3%にとどまる。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 3.3は「世界排出に占めるLDCの割合（%）」の数字との取り違え。6.1や9.5は世界平均に近いか上回る値で、報告書の内容と合わない。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, AR6 WGIII Summary for Policymakers, 2022, https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg3/chapter/summary-for-policymakers/ ／ IPCC, AR6 Synthesis Report: Summary for Policymakers, 2023, https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/syr/summary-for-policymakers/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch4 政策・ガバナンス","q":"[LO 4.2] A country imports steel produced abroad. How does consumption-based accounting differ from territorial (production-based) accounting for the emissions embedded in that steel?","h":"製造した国か、最終的に消費した国かで、排出の帰属先が変わります。","c":["Consumption-based accounting attributes the embedded emissions to the exporting country, whereas territorial accounting attributes them to the country where the steel is finally used.","Consumption-based accounting excludes emissions from traded goods altogether, whereas territorial accounting counts them in both the exporting and the importing country.","Consumption-based accounting attributes the embedded emissions to the importing country, whereas territorial accounting attributes them to the country where the steel was made.","Consumption-based accounting attributes the emissions to the country of the steelmaker's headquarters, whereas territorial accounting splits them evenly between the two trading partners."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 消費ベースは消費国に、領土ベース（生産ベース）は生産国に帰属させる。<br><br><b>解説</b> 各国のGHGインベントリ（UNFCCC報告）は領土内で排出された量を数える領土ベースである。消費ベースは貿易品に体化された排出を最終消費国に付け替える。そのため輸入依存の先進国（EU・米国・日本など）では消費ベースの数字が領土ベースより大きくなり、輸出国（中国など）では小さくなる傾向がある。CBAMは、この「貿易を通じた排出の移転（カーボンリーケージ）」への政策対応の一つ。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 消費ベースが貿易品を除外する、本社所在地で帰属させる、といった定義は存在しない。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, AR6 WGIII Chapter 2, https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg3/chapter/chapter-2/ ／ Our World in Data, https://ourworldindata.org/consumption-based-co2"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch4 政策・ガバナンス","q":"[LO 4.3] Under the Kyoto Protocol's first commitment period, what collective target did Annex I Parties accept?","h":"京都議定書の第1約束期間の全体目標の数字を問う問題です。","c":["A reduction of at least 15% below 1990 levels, averaged over the period 2005-2010.","A reduction of at least 5% below 2005 levels, averaged over the period 2008-2012.","A reduction of at least 5% below 1990 levels, averaged over the period 2008-2012.","A reduction of at least 10% below 1990 levels, averaged over the period 2013-2017."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 附属書I国全体で、2008〜2012年の平均を1990年比で少なくとも5%削減。<br><br><b>解説</b> 京都議定書（1997年採択、2005年発効）は、先進国等の附属書I国全体で、第1約束期間（2008〜2012年）に1990年比で少なくとも5%削減することを定めた。国別には差があり、EU 8%、米国 7%（批准せず）、日本 6%などの数値が割り当てられた。2012年のドーハ改正で第2約束期間（2013〜2020年）が設けられたが、日本・ロシア・カナダなどは参加しなかった。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 基準年を2005年とする、期間を別にとる、削減率を変えるといった変形は、いずれも議定書の記述と合わない。<br><br><b>日本との対応</b> 日本の約束は6%削減で、森林吸収源と京都メカニズムを活用して達成した。<br><br>【出典】UNFCCC, What is the Kyoto Protocol?, https://unfccc.int/kyoto_protocol ／ 環境省, 京都議定書の概要（COP3議長国・日本の目標）, https://www.env.go.jp/council/06earth/y060-22/mat01_2.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch4 政策・ガバナンス","q":"[LO 4.3] Which statement correctly describes a legally binding obligation of Parties under the Paris Agreement (Article 4)?","h":"拘束力があるのは、NDCの作成・提出・維持という手続きの義務です。","c":["Each Party must achieve the quantified target in its NDC by 2030, and a compliance committee imposes financial penalties on Parties that fall short of it.","Each Party must cut emissions by an equal percentage relative to 2005 levels, and the percentage is set centrally by the UNFCCC Secretariat for every country.","Each Party must submit one NDC at the time of ratification and has no obligation to update it, because later cycles are optional under the Agreement.","Each Party must prepare, communicate and maintain successive NDCs and pursue domestic mitigation measures, although achieving the NDC outcome itself is not legally binding."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> NDCを作り、出し、維持する義務は拘束力があるが、目標の達成そのものは拘束力がない。<br><br><b>解説</b> パリ協定4条は、締約国がNDCを作成・通報・維持し、その目的を達成するための国内対策をとるとする。NDCは5年ごとに通報し、後続のNDCは従前より前進（progression）を示す。達成そのものは法的拘束力がなく、実施・遵守委員会は促進的で非懲罰的。「手続きは拘束、成果は非拘束」がパリの設計。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 全締約国一律の削減率の割当や罰金、更新不要といった内容はパリ協定にない。<br><br>【出典】UNFCCC, The Paris Agreement, https://unfccc.int/process-and-meetings/the-paris-agreement"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch4 政策・ガバナンス","q":"[LO 4.3] Which pairing of a UN climate conference and its outcome is correct?","h":"COP28の成果の説明として正しいものを選ぶ問題です。","c":["COP26 (Glasgow, 2021): adopted the Paris Agreement and set the 1.5°C temperature limit for the first time in a UN climate decision.","COP27 (Sharm el-Sheikh, 2022): agreed binding national coal phase-out dates for all Annex I countries with penalties for missing them, enforced from 2025 by a newly created UN compliance body.","COP28 (Dubai, 2023): concluded the first global stocktake and called for transitioning away from fossil fuels in energy systems in a just, orderly and equitable manner.","COP21 (Paris, 2015): created the loss and damage fund and capitalised it with the first pledges from developed countries."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> COP28は初のグローバル・ストックテイクを完了し、エネルギー分野での化石燃料からの移行に言及した。<br><br><b>解説</b> COP28（2023年、ドバイ）のUAEコンセンサスは、初のグローバル・ストックテイクの成果として、公正・秩序ある衡平な形でエネルギーシステムにおける化石燃料からの脱却（transitioning away）を進めることや、2030年までの再エネ設備容量3倍・省エネ改善率2倍に言及した。パリ協定の採択はCOP21（2015年）、損失と損害基金の設立合意はCOP27（2022年）、基金の運用開始決定はCOP28。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> パリ協定の採択はCOP26ではなくCOP21。石炭の拘束的な廃止期限が決まったことはない。損失と損害基金の合意はCOP27。<br><br>【出典】UNFCCC, Global Stocktake, https://unfccc.int/topics/global-stocktake ／ UNFCCC, COP28 outcomes, https://unfccc.int/cop28"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch4 政策・ガバナンス","q":"[LO 4.4] Compared with an emissions trading system (ETS), which statement correctly describes a carbon tax?","h":"税は価格の確実性、ETSは排出量の確実性を与えます。","c":["A carbon tax gives emissions certainty but not price certainty, because the regulator fixes the total quantity and the market sets the tax rate.","A carbon tax gives both price and emissions certainty, because the tax rate is fixed and every emitter must reduce by the same percentage.","A carbon tax gives neither price nor emissions certainty, because its rate is renegotiated each year between each emitter and the regulator.","A carbon tax gives price certainty but not emissions certainty, because the quantity of abatement depends on how firms respond to the tax."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 炭素税は価格が固定され、削減量は企業の反応次第で決まる。<br><br><b>解説</b> 炭素税は課税額（価格）を政府が決めるため企業の見通しが立ちやすいが、総排出量は企業の対応に依存して不確実。ETSは総量（キャップ）を固定し、価格が市場で決まる。この「価格か数量か」のトレードオフが両者の基本的な違い。ETSは価格変動が大きくなり得るため、EU ETSは市場安定化リザーブ（MSR）などの調整措置を持つ。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 税とETSの確実性を入れ替えた記述や、両方が確実とする記述は誤り。<br><br><b>日本との対応</b> 日本ではGX-ETS（排出量取引制度）が、2026年度から直接排出量が年10万tCO2以上の事業者に義務化され、排出枠は一定の基準で無償割当される。<br><br>【出典】IPCC AR6 WGIII Chapter 13, https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg3/chapter/chapter-13/ ／ 経済産業省, GX-ETS（排出量取引制度）リーフレット, https://www.meti.go.jp/policy/energy_environment/global_warming/ets_leaflet.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch4 政策・ガバナンス","q":"[LO 4.4] What is the primary purpose of the EU Carbon Border Adjustment Mechanism (CBAM)?","h":"国内の炭素価格との差による『漏れ』を防ぐ仕組みです。","c":["To impose a global carbon tax on all traded goods, with the proceeds collected by the United Nations and distributed to developing countries, replacing all national carbon taxes from 2030.","To address carbon leakage by requiring importers of covered goods, such as steel, cement and aluminium, to surrender certificates reflecting the EU carbon price.","To refund EU ETS costs to European exporters of covered goods, so that they can compete in markets without a carbon price.","To prohibit imports of covered goods from any country that has not joined the Paris Agreement, regardless of the goods' embedded emissions."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> CBAMは、輸入品に域内と同等の炭素価格負担を求めてカーボンリーケージを防ぐ。<br><br><b>解説</b> CBAMは、EU ETSの対象品目に近い輸入品（鉄鋼・セメント・アルミニウム・肥料・電力・水素など）の輸入者に、体化排出量に応じたCBAM証書の購入・償却を求め、域内外の炭素コスト差を調整する。2023年10月から移行期間（報告のみ）、2026年から本格適用（証書の償却）となる。EU ETSの無償割当は段階的に廃止される。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> CBAMはEUの制度であり、国連が徴収する世界炭素税ではない。輸出還付や輸入禁止の仕組みでもない。<br><br>【出典】European Commission, CBAM, https://taxation-customs.ec.europa.eu/carbon-border-adjustment-mechanism_en"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch4 政策・ガバナンス","q":"[LO 4.4] Which statement describes a commonly cited drawback of carbon pricing and a typical policy response?","h":"低所得層の負担が相対的に重くなる点（逆進性）が代表的な論点です。","c":["Carbon pricing is regressive only for the richest households, because they own more vehicles, so governments exempt low-income groups from every energy price signal.","Carbon pricing can be regressive because poorer households spend a larger share of income on energy, so governments may recycle revenue as dividends or targeted transfers.","Carbon pricing cannot generate public revenue, because every allowance or tax payment must be returned to emitters, so no distributional measure is ever needed.","Carbon pricing always lowers energy bills for all households, because efficiency gains exceed the price rise, so redistribution is unnecessary in every case."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 炭素価格は逆進的になり得るため、収入の還元や移転で緩和する。<br><br><b>解説</b> 所得に占めるエネルギー支出の割合は低所得世帯ほど高く、炭素価格の負担は逆進的になり得る。対応として、税収の配当（カナダの炭素手数料の還付など）、低所得層への給付、削減投資への再配分が挙げられる。炭素価格は税収・オークション収入を生むため、その使途（収入中立か、減税か、投資か）が受容性を左右する。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 歳入が生じない、全世帯の光熱費が必ず下がる、といった記述は事実に合わない。<br><br><b>日本との対応</b> 日本では、GX推進法により、化石燃料の輸入事業者等に輸入する化石燃料のCO2量に応じて課す化石燃料賦課金が、2028年度から導入される（同法第11条）。<br><br>【出典】IPCC AR6 WGIII Chapter 13, https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg3/chapter/chapter-13/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch4 政策・ガバナンス","q":"[LO 4.5] A fuel regulation requires fuel suppliers to cut the average carbon intensity (gCO2e per MJ) of the fuels they sell by a rising percentage each year, with tradable credits and deficits. Which policy is this?","h":"燃料の炭素強度に年々厳しくなる基準を課す、運輸部門の政策です。","c":["A feed-in tariff, a guaranteed long-term price paid to producers of renewable transport fuels.","A renewable portfolio standard, a quota for the share of renewables in electricity sales.","A low carbon fuel standard, a performance standard for transport fuels such as California's LCFS.","A cap on vehicle registrations, a limit on the number of new cars sold in each year."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 燃料の炭素強度の基準を課し、クレジットで過不足を調整するのが低炭素燃料基準（LCFS）。<br><br><b>解説</b> LCFSは、燃料サプライヤーに対し、燃料ライフサイクルの炭素強度を毎年引き下げる基準を課す。基準より低い燃料はクレジットを生み、高い燃料は不足分（デフィシット）を生じ、取引で調整できる。カリフォルニア州（2011年開始）が代表例で、輸送燃料にエタノール・バイオディーゼル・電力・水素なども含む。RPSは電力、FITは電力の買取価格を定める政策。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> FITとRPSは電力部門の政策。登録台数の上限は燃料の炭素強度とは無関係。<br><br>【出典】California Air Resources Board, Low Carbon Fuel Standard, https://ww2.arb.ca.gov/our-work/programs/low-carbon-fuel-standard/about"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch4 政策・ガバナンス","q":"[LO 4.5] A government guarantees that renewable electricity generators will sell their output to the grid for 20 years at a fixed rate per kWh. Which power-sector policy is this?","h":"長期固定価格での買取を保証する、再エネ導入の代表的な制度です。","c":["A feed-in tariff, which guarantees a long-term price and grid access to eligible renewable generators.","A cap-and-trade scheme, which sets a total allowance limit and lets emitters trade permits among themselves.","A carbon tax, which charges a fixed amount per tonne of CO2 emitted by each fossil-fuel generator.","A capacity market, which pays plants to stay available to the grid without regard to their fuel source."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 買取価格と期間を保証して再エネを促すのが固定価格買取制度（FIT）。<br><br><b>解説</b> FIT（feed-in tariff）は、再エネ発電事業者に長期の固定価格と系統接続を保証し、投資リスクを下げて導入を促す。ドイツが先駆けで、各国に広がった。近年はコスト低下を受け、入札（リバースオークション）や市場連動のFIP（フィード・イン・プレミアム）への移行が進む。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> キャップ&トレードや炭素税は排出に価格をつける政策で、再エネの買取保証ではない。容量市場は供給力の確保を目的とする。<br><br><b>日本との対応</b> 日本のFIT制度は2012年7月に開始し、2022年度からFIP制度も導入された。<br><br>【出典】IPCC AR6 WGIII Chapter 6, https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg3/chapter/chapter-6/ ／ 経済産業省 資源エネルギー庁, FIT制度, https://www.enecho.meti.go.jp/category/saving_and_new/saiene/kaitori/index.html"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch4 政策・ガバナンス","q":"[LO 4.5] Which of the following is a command-and-control (regulatory standard) policy rather than a market-based instrument in the power sector?","h":"排出量や価格ではなく、設備ごとの上限を直接定める規制を選びます。","c":["An emissions performance standard that bars new power plants from emitting more than a set number of gCO2 per kWh.","An emissions trading system that lets utilities buy and sell allowances under a declining cap on total emissions.","A carbon tax that raises the generation cost of fossil plants in proportion to the tonnes of CO2 they emit.","A reverse auction that awards long-term contracts to the renewable projects offering the lowest price per MWh."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 設備ごとの排出上限（排出基準）は規制的手法で、他は価格・市場を使う手法。<br><br><b>解説</b> 排出パフォーマンス基準（EPS）は、発電所のkWh当たり排出量に上限を設ける直接規制で、英国は2013年エネルギー法で新設の化石火力に排出基準を設けた。ETS・炭素税・入札は価格シグナルや市場メカニズムで行動を促す経済的手法。規制は確実性が高い反面、費用効率が劣る場合がある。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> ETSは総量を定めて取引を認め、炭素税は価格を課し、入札は価格競争で事業者を選ぶので、いずれも市場ベース。<br><br>【出典】IPCC AR6 WGIII Chapter 6, https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg3/chapter/chapter-6/ ／ UK Government, Emissions Performance Standard, https://www.legislation.gov.uk/ukpga/2013/32/contents"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch4 政策・ガバナンス","q":"[LO 4.6] A manufacturer buys steam from a utility's district heating network for use in its plant. Under the GHG Protocol, how is the emissions associated with that purchased steam classified?","h":"購入した電気・蒸気・熱・冷熱は同じスコープです。","c":["Scope 1, because the steam is consumed at the manufacturer's own site and therefore counts as a direct emission of the company.","Scope 2, because it is indirect emissions from the generation of purchased steam, heat or cooling consumed by the company.","Scope 3, because the steam is produced by a third party and therefore always falls in the company's upstream value chain.","Excluded from all scopes, because steam is not electricity and therefore is outside the reporting boundary of the standard."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 購入した蒸気・熱・冷熱は、電力と同じくスコープ2。<br><br><b>解説</b> スコープ2は、報告企業が購入・取得した電力、蒸気、熱、冷熱の生成に伴う間接排出。消費地点が自社拠点でも排出源は他社の設備なので、スコープ1ではない。スコープ1は自社が所有・管理する排出源からの直接排出（ボイラー、社有車など）。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 購入蒸気を3や対象外とするのは誤り。電気に限らず熱も含めるのがスコープ2の定義。<br><br>【出典】WRI/WBCSD, GHG Protocol Corporate Standard, https://ghgprotocol.org/corporate-standard"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch4 政策・ガバナンス","q":"[LO 4.6] Which statement about Scope 2 reporting under the GHG Protocol Scope 2 Guidance (2015) is correct?","h":"ロケーション基準とマーケット基準の2つを報告するのが原則です。","c":["Companies with operations in markets that offer contractual instruments should report Scope 2 using both a location-based and a market-based method.","Companies should report Scope 2 using only the market-based method, because the location-based method was withdrawn when the guidance was revised.","Companies should report Scope 2 using only the location-based method, because contractual instruments such as RECs have no bearing on emissions.","Companies should report Scope 2 using whichever method gives the lower figure, and they need not disclose which method has been applied."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> スコープ2は、ロケーション基準とマーケット基準の両方を開示する（二重報告）。<br><br><b>解説</b> 2015年のスコープ2ガイダンスは、契約手段（再エネ証書、PPA、供給事業者固有の排出係数など）が利用できる市場で事業を行う企業に、ロケーション基準（グリッド平均排出係数）とマーケット基準（契約に基づく排出係数）の両方での報告を求める。2つを並べることで、購入電力の実態と再エネ調達の成果の両方を示せる。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> どちらか一方のみ、低い方のみ、という運用はガイダンスに沿わない。<br><br>【出典】WRI/WBCSD, GHG Protocol Scope 2 Guidance, https://ghgprotocol.org/scope_2_guidance"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch4 政策・ガバナンス","q":"[LO 4.6] Which of the following is an example of a downstream Scope 3 category in the GHG Protocol Corporate Value Chain (Scope 3) Standard?","h":"スコープ3は上流8カテゴリ、下流7カテゴリに分かれます。","c":["Category 1: purchased goods and services.","Category 6: business travel.","Category 7: employee commuting.","Category 11: use of sold products."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 「販売した製品の使用」は下流のカテゴリ11。<br><br><b>解説</b> スコープ3は15カテゴリで、1〜8が上流（購入した製品・サービス、資本財、燃料・エネルギー関連、輸送・流通（上流）、事業から出る廃棄物、出張、雇用者の通勤、リース資産（上流））、9〜15が下流（輸送・流通（下流）、販売した製品の加工、販売した製品の使用、販売した製品の廃棄、リース資産（下流）、フランチャイズ、投資）。投資（カテゴリ15）は金融機関にとって特に重要。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> カテゴリ1・6・7はいずれも上流のカテゴリ。<br><br>【出典】WRI/WBCSD, Corporate Value Chain (Scope 3) Accounting and Reporting Standard, https://ghgprotocol.org/corporate-value-chain-scope-3-standard"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch4 政策・ガバナンス","q":"[LO 4.7] A retailer has no supplier-specific data. It multiplies the monetary value of its purchases by sector-average emission factors derived from environmentally extended input-output models. Which Scope 3 calculation method is this, and what is a main weakness?","h":"金額×産業平均係数で見積もる方法の長所と短所を問う問題です。","c":["The spend-based method, which is quick to apply but reflects price changes and sector averages rather than the suppliers' actual emissions.","The supplier-specific method, which is quick to apply but reflects price changes and sector averages rather than the suppliers' actual emissions.","The average-data method, which is precise but requires measured emissions from each supplier for every purchased product.","The hybrid method, which is precise but ignores the monetary value of purchases and relies only on physical quantities."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 金額×EEIO係数の方法がスペンド（金額）ベース法で、実際の排出を反映しにくい。<br><br><b>解説</b> Scope 3技術ガイダンスは、データの種類として、サプライヤー固有データ、ハイブリッド、平均データ（物量×平均係数）、金額ベース（金額×EEIO係数）を区別する。金額ベース法は少ない情報で算出できるが、価格変動（インフレ）や産業平均に左右され、サプライヤーの削減努力が反映されない。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> サプライヤー固有法は実測データを用いる精度の高い方法で、平均データ法は物量に平均係数を掛ける。<br><br>【出典】WRI/WBCSD, Technical Guidance for Calculating Scope 3 Emissions, https://ghgprotocol.org/scope-3-technical-calculation-guidance"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch4 政策・ガバナンス","q":"[LO 4.7] Which statement about Scope 3 disclosure under IFRS S2 (June 2023) is correct?","h":"S2は開示を求めつつ、初年度は猶予があります。","c":["IFRS S2 does not mention Scope 3 emissions, because the standard covers only Scope 1 and Scope 2 emissions under the GHG Protocol.","IFRS S2 requires disclosure of Scope 3 emissions, but it provides transitional relief permitting an entity to omit them in its first annual reporting period.","IFRS S2 requires disclosure of Scope 3 emissions from the first reporting year, and it allows no relief for any entity in any circumstance, and the entity must also assure it externally to a reasonable level.","IFRS S2 makes Scope 3 disclosure optional for every entity permanently, and it asks only for a qualitative description of the value chain."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> IFRS S2はスコープ3の開示を求めるが、初年度は適用免除がある。<br><br><b>解説</b> IFRS S2は、スコープ1・2・3の絶対総量の開示を求め、スコープ3は測定に使ったカテゴリも示す。ただし移行措置として、初年度の年次報告期間ではスコープ3を開示しないことが認められる。スコープ3のデータ品質（サプライヤーデータの入手困難、推計の不確実性）が背景にある。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> S2はスコープ3に言及し、恒久的な任意でも一切免除なしでもない。<br><br>【出典】IFRS Foundation, IFRS S2 Climate-related Disclosures, https://www.ifrs.org/issued-standards/ifrs-sustainability-standards-navigator/ifrs-s2-climate-related-disclosures/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch4 政策・ガバナンス","q":"[LO 4.7] Why are Scope 3 emissions especially important and difficult for a bank or asset manager to account for?","h":"金融機関では、投融資に伴う排出（カテゴリ15）が大半を占めます。","c":["Most of its emissions sit in Scope 1, from branch heating and company cars, which cannot be measured because no standard method exists for them.","Most of its emissions sit in Scope 2, from the purchased electricity of trading floors, which cannot be measured without access to borrower systems.","Most of its emissions sit in Scope 3 category 6 (business travel), which depend on airline data that are never available to the reporting firm.","Most of its emissions sit in Scope 3 category 15 (investments), which depend on data from investees and borrowers that are often missing or estimated."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 金融機関の排出の大半はカテゴリ15（投資）で、投融資先のデータに依存する。<br><br><b>解説</b> 金融機関の自社排出（スコープ1・2）は小さく、投融資に伴うファイナンスド・エミッション（スコープ3カテゴリ15）が桁違いに大きい。PCAFの基準が算定方法を定めているが、投融資先の実測データがない場合は推計に頼る。データの質は、実測に近いほど高いというスコア制で示す。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> スコープ1・2は金融機関では小さく、算定方法も確立している。出張も大きくない。<br><br>【出典】PCAF, The Global GHG Accounting and Reporting Standard for the Financial Industry, https://carbonaccountingfinancials.com/standard"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch4 政策・ガバナンス","q":"[LO 4.8] Which of the following is a public policy, rather than a voluntary private-sector initiative, used to mobilise private capital for green finance?","h":"政府が信用補完で民間資金を呼び込む例を選びます。","c":["A government providing a credit guarantee that lowers the risk of private loans for building energy-efficiency retrofits.","Members of an asset-owner alliance voluntarily committing to move their portfolios to net-zero emissions by 2050.","An asset manager adopting an internal policy that excludes thermal coal producers from its actively managed funds.","A group of banks voluntarily adopting a framework to assess environmental and social risk in project finance."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 政府による信用保証は公共政策。他の3つは民間の自主的取り組み。<br><br><b>解説</b> グリーン・ファイナンスを促す公共政策には、信用保証・first-loss資本（ブレンデッド・ファイナンス）、税制優遇、補助金、ソブリン・グリーンボンド、グリーン銀行、開示規制、タクソノミーなどがある。NZAOA（資産保有者のアライアンス）、運用会社の石炭除外方針、赤道原則は民間の自主的取り組み。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> アライアンス加盟や社内の除外方針、赤道原則はいずれも民間が自ら決める枠組み。<br><br><b>日本との対応</b> 日本では、GX経済移行債（2024年2月に初回発行）で調達した資金を、GX投資の支援に充てる枠組みがある。<br><br>【出典】UNEP FI, Net-Zero Asset Owner Alliance, https://www.unepfi.org/net-zero-alliance/ ／ 財務省, GX経済移行債（クライメート・トランジション利付国債）, https://www.mof.go.jp/public_relations/finance/202405/202405c.html"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch4 政策・ガバナンス","q":"[LO 4.8] Which statement best describes the Equator Principles?","h":"プロジェクトファイナンスの環境・社会リスクを管理する自主的な枠組みです。","c":["A set of voluntary guidelines issued by ICMA that describe how an issuer should label and report on a green use-of-proceeds bond.","A binding EU regulation that requires every fund manager to disclose how sustainability risks are integrated into investment decisions, and national authorities fine funds that fail to comply.","A United Nations-convened alliance of insurers that commits members to underwrite only net-zero aligned risks from 2030.","A voluntary risk management framework adopted by financial institutions to determine, assess and manage environmental and social risk, mainly in project finance."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 赤道原則は、金融機関が環境・社会リスクを評価・管理する自主的な枠組み。<br><br><b>解説</b> 赤道原則（2003年策定、EP4は2020年）は、プロジェクトファイナンスなどで、金融機関が環境・社会リスクを特定・評価・管理するための自主的な基準。IFCのパフォーマンス基準を参照し、採択した金融機関（EPFI）は、自社の内部ルールに組み込む。EP4では気候変動リスクの評価や、先住民の権利への配慮が強化された。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> グリーンボンド原則はICMA、SFDRはEU規則、保険分野の国連原則はPSIで、赤道原則とは別。<br><br>【出典】Equator Principles Association, About the Equator Principles, https://equator-principles.com/about-the-equator-principles/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch4 政策・ガバナンス","q":"[LO 4.8] Which statement about the European Green Bond Standard (Regulation (EU) 2023/2631) is correct?","h":"EU域内でグリーンボンドの『使い道』を分類基準に結びつけた自主的な基準です。","c":["It is a mandatory standard that every bond issued in the EU must meet, and it allows proceeds to fund any activity of an issuer with a net-zero target, and each issuer must fund a public green register at its own cost.","It is a voluntary standard that exempts issuers from external review, because the issuer's own board certifies that proceeds were used as promised.","It is a voluntary standard under which proceeds of a bond designated a European Green Bond must fund Taxonomy-aligned activities, with external review of the allocation reports.","It is a mandatory standard that applies only to sovereign issuers, and it requires proceeds to be spent on activities in the issuing Member State."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 欧州グリーンボンドは自主的な基準で、資金使途はタクソノミー適合活動、外部レビューが必要。<br><br><b>解説</b> EU GBS（規則2023/2631、2024年12月21日適用開始）は、「European Green Bond」の名称を使う債券に、調達資金を原則としてEUタクソノミー適合の活動に充てること、発行前のファクトシートと発行後の配分報告・インパクト報告、ESMAに登録された外部レビュー機関による確認を求める。任意の基準だが、民間発行体も使える。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 全ての債券に義務づける基準ではなく、外部レビューも不可欠。ソブリン限定でもない。<br><br>【出典】European Commission, European Green Bond Standard, https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2023/2631/oj"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch4 政策・ガバナンス","q":"[LO 4.9] Under the EU Taxonomy Regulation, which set of conditions must an economic activity meet to qualify as environmentally sustainable?","h":"実質的貢献・DNSH・最低限のセーフガード・技術的スクリーニング基準の4つです。","c":["It makes a substantial contribution to climate change mitigation only, has a net-zero target for 2050, meets minimum safeguards and has an external second-party opinion.","It makes a contribution to at least three of six environmental objectives, causes limited harm to the others, and is certified by a national supervisory authority each year, and the certification is published in a national register.","It reduces the issuer's greenhouse gas intensity by at least 30% a year, does no harm to biodiversity only, and is listed on a regulated EU exchange.","It makes a substantial contribution to at least one of six environmental objectives, does no significant harm to the others, meets minimum safeguards and complies with technical screening criteria."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 6つの環境目標のいずれかに実質的に貢献し、他に重大な害を与えず、最低限のセーフガードを満たし、基準に適合する。<br><br><b>解説</b> EUタクソノミー規則（2020/852）は、気候変動の緩和、適応、水・海洋資源、循環経済、汚染防止、生物多様性の6つの環境目標のうち少なくとも1つに実質的に貢献し、他の目標に重大な害を与えず（DNSH）、人権・労働など最低限のセーフガードを満たし、技術的スクリーニング基準に適合することを求める。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 3つ以上への貢献、毎年30%削減、上場要件などはタクソノミーの要件にない。<br><br>【出典】European Commission, EU taxonomy for sustainable activities, https://finance.ec.europa.eu/sustainable-finance/tools-and-standards/eu-taxonomy-sustainable-activities_en"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch4 政策・ガバナンス","q":"[LO 4.9] Which of the following is a recognised challenge of green taxonomies?","h":"各国の分類が揃わず、国をまたぐ運用に手間がかかる点が代表的です。","c":["Taxonomies are always identical across jurisdictions by law, so the main challenge is that no issuer can choose a different standard.","Taxonomies never use quantitative thresholds, so the main challenge is that every activity is classified only through narrative judgement.","Taxonomies are kept private by regulators, so the main challenge is that no investor can see which activities qualify as green.","Differences between jurisdictions' taxonomies create interoperability problems and compliance costs for cross-border issuers and investors."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 各国のタクソノミーの違いが相互運用性とコンプライアンス負担を生む。<br><br><b>解説</b> EU、中国、ASEAN、英国、日本の関連指針など、各国・地域のタクソノミーは対象活動や基準が異なり、国をまたぐ資金調達や投資家の判断で相互運用性が課題になる。IPSFが策定したコモン・グラウンド・タクソノミー（EUと中国の共通部分）はその対応の一つ。ほかの課題として、データ要件の重さ、トランジション活動の扱い、グリーンウォッシュ対策との関係がある。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> タクソノミーは公開され、定量基準を持つものが多く、各国で同一でもない。<br><br>【出典】IPSF, Common Ground Taxonomy, https://finance.ec.europa.eu/sustainable-finance/international-platform-sustainable-finance_en"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch4 政策・ガバナンス","q":"[LO 4.9] Which description of a 'transitional activity' under Article 10(2) of the EU Taxonomy Regulation is correct?","h":"低炭素の代替手段がまだない活動で、最善水準かつロックインしないことが条件です。","c":["An activity with no technologically and economically feasible low-carbon alternative, whose emissions match the sector's best performance and that does not lock in carbon-intensive assets.","Any activity of a company with a published net-zero target, regardless of the activity's current emissions or of available low-carbon alternatives, provided that the target is published on the company's website and verified by its own auditor.","An activity that is already fully climate neutral and that directly enables other activities to make a substantial contribution to climate goals.","A temporary activity that qualifies as green only until 2030, after which it is automatically reclassified without any further assessment."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 移行活動は、代替手段がなく、業界最善の排出水準で、ロックインを起こさない活動。<br><br><b>解説</b> EUタクソノミー10条2項の移行活動（transitional activity）は、2050年までの気候中立への移行を支えるが、技術的・経済的に実行可能な低炭素の代替手段がまだなく、排出水準が業種内の最善の性能に対応し、低炭素の代替手段の開発を妨げず、炭素集約型資産のロックインを招かない活動をいう。他の活動の貢献を可能にする活動は「実現活動（enabling）」で、16条に別に定義される。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> ネットゼロ目標の有無だけで決まるのではなく、2030年での自動再分類もない。<br><br>【出典】Regulation (EU) 2020/852, Articles 10 and 16, https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2020/852/oj"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch4 政策・ガバナンス","q":"[LO 4.10] Which statement correctly describes the Bank of England's 2021 Climate Biennial Exploratory Scenario (CBES)?","h":"30年の探索的演習で、資本要件の設定が目的ではありません。","c":["It was a pass-or-fail test using one severe one-year scenario, and banks that failed it were required to raise capital buffers immediately, with the failing banks named in a public ranking.","It covered only insurers over a five-year horizon, and its results were used to set a mandatory climate capital add-on for each insurer.","It was an exploratory exercise using three scenarios (early, late and no additional action) over a 30-year horizon, and it was not used to set capital requirements.","It used a single orderly-transition scenario for banks over a ten-year horizon, and the results were published as firm-level pass rates."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> CBESは、3シナリオ・30年の探索的演習で、資本要件を決めるためのものではない。<br><br><b>解説</b> CBES（2021年に実施、2022年5月に結果公表）は、英国の主要銀行・保険会社を対象に、早期対応（Early Action）、後手の対応（Late Action）、追加対策なし（No Additional Action）の3シナリオを2050年までの30年間で検討した。目的は、金融システムの脆弱性の理解と企業の能力把握で、資本要件の設定には使わない。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 1年の合否テストや、保険会社限定、1シナリオという記述は事実に合わない。<br><br>【出典】Bank of England, Results of the 2021 Climate Biennial Exploratory Scenario, https://www.bankofengland.co.uk/stress-testing/2022/results-of-the-2021-climate-biennial-exploratory-scenario"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch4 政策・ガバナンス","q":"[LO 4.10] How many principles are contained in the Basel Committee's 'Principles for the effective management and supervision of climate-related financial risks' (2022), and how are they split?","h":"18原則で、銀行向けと監督当局向けの2群に分かれます。","c":["18 principles in total: 6 addressed to banks and 12 addressed to supervisors.","10 principles in total: 5 addressed to banks and 5 addressed to supervisors.","24 principles in total: 12 addressed to banks and 12 addressed to supervisors.","18 principles in total: 12 addressed to banks and 6 addressed to supervisors."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 全部で18原則で、銀行向けが12、監督当局向けが6。<br><br><b>解説</b> バーゼル銀行監督委員会が2022年6月に公表した原則は、銀行向けの12原則（ガバナンス、リスク管理プロセス、資本・流動性等）と、監督当局向けの6原則（監督の枠組み、権限・手段等）からなる。自主的に、比例性を考慮して実施される。気候リスクを新しいリスク種別でなく既存リスクのドライバーとして捉えるのが基本的な立場。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 数や割り振りを変えた選択肢は誤り。<br><br>【出典】BCBS, Principles for the effective management and supervision of climate-related financial risks, 2022, https://www.bis.org/bcbs/publ/d532.htm ／ BIS, Basel Committee issues principles for the effective management and supervision of climate-related financial risks (press release), 2022, https://www.bis.org/press/p220615.htm"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch4 政策・ガバナンス","q":"[LO 4.10] Which best describes the ECB's Guide on climate-related and environmental risks (November 2020)?","h":"13の監督上の期待を示し、監督対話やSREPに反映されます。","c":["It sets a binding climate capital add-on of 3% of CET1 for banks with fossil-fuel exposures, which applies from the date of publication, and which supervisors reviewed annually through a dedicated stress test.","It requires banks to reach net-zero financed emissions by 2050 as a condition of keeping their licence, with no flexibility in timing.","It forbids banks from lending to any fossil-fuel company from 2025, with supervisors verifying compliance in an annual stress test.","It sets out 13 supervisory expectations for banks on business model, governance, risk management and disclosure, which feed into supervisory dialogue and the SREP."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> ECBのガイドは、13の期待を示し、監督対話とSREPに反映される。<br><br><b>解説</b> ECBのガイドは、銀行がビジネスモデルと戦略、ガバナンスとリスク選好、リスク管理、開示の4領域で満たすべき13の監督上の期待を示す。2022年のテーマ別レビュー・気候ストレステストで進捗を点検し。ECBは新たな資本の上乗せを法的に義務づけたわけではない。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> CET1の上乗せ、ネットゼロ義務、化石燃料への融資の禁止は、ガイドに含まれない。<br><br>【出典】ECB Banking Supervision, Guide on climate-related and environmental risks, 2020, https://www.bankingsupervision.europa.eu/ecb/pub/pdf/ssm.202011finalguideonclimate-relatedandenvironmentalrisks~58213f6564.en.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch4 政策・ガバナンス","q":"[LO 4.11] Which grouping consists of asset owners, was convened by UNEP FI and the PRI, and commits members to transition their investment portfolios to net-zero GHG emissions by 2050?","h":"「資産保有者」のグループかどうかが決め手です。","c":["The Net-Zero Banking Alliance (NZBA).","The Net Zero Asset Managers initiative (NZAM).","Climate Action 100+ (CA100+).","The Net-Zero Asset Owner Alliance (NZAOA)."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 資産保有者のアライアンスがNZAOA。<br><br><b>解説</b> NZAOAは、2019年9月の国連気候行動サミットで発足した、年金基金・保険会社などの資産保有者のグループで、UNEP FIとPRIが事務局的に招集する。投資ポートフォリオを2050年までにネットゼロに移行することを約束する。NZBAは銀行、NZAMは資産運用会社のグループで、CA100+は主要排出企業へのエンゲージメントを行う投資家イニシアティブ。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> NZBA（銀行）、NZAM（運用会社）、CA100+（エンゲージメント）は、会員の属性や活動が異なる。<br><br>【出典】UNEP FI, Net-Zero Asset Owner Alliance, https://www.unepfi.org/net-zero-alliance/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch4 政策・ガバナンス","q":"[LO 4.11] Which statement best describes Climate Action 100+?","h":"最大の排出企業に働きかける投資家主導のイニシアティブです。","c":["An investor-led initiative, launched in 2017, that engages the world's largest corporate greenhouse gas emitters on governance, emissions cuts and disclosure.","A group of central banks, launched in 2017, that sets the capital charges banks must apply to loans to the world's largest emitters, and that publishes the resulting charges on a public website each year.","A voluntary standard-setter, launched in 2017, that certifies corporate emissions targets as consistent with a 1.5°C pathway.","An intergovernmental fund, launched in 2017, that finances coal plant closures in the world's largest emitting countries."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> CA100+は、大口排出企業に対するエンゲージメントを行う投資家イニシアティブ。<br><br><b>解説</b> Climate Action 100+は、2017年12月に発足した投資家主導のイニシアティブで、世界の主要排出企業（フォーカス企業）に、ガバナンスの強化、排出削減、気候関連の財務開示の改善を求めて対話する。中央銀行の枠組みはNGFS、排出目標の検証はSBTiが担う。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 資本賦課の設定や石炭火力の閉鎖資金は、CA100+の活動ではない。<br><br>【出典】Climate Action 100+, About, https://www.climateaction100.org/about/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch4 政策・ガバナンス","q":"[LO 4.11] Which initiative is correctly matched with its focus?","h":"RE100は、事業で使う電力を再エネ100%にする企業の取り組みです。","c":["RE100: companies committing to source 100% renewable electricity, led by The Climate Group in partnership with CDP.","SBTi: a certification body that issues carbon offsets for companies that wish to claim neutrality, and that audits the buyers' purchase records annually.","CDP: a regulator that sets mandatory climate disclosure rules for all companies listed in Europe.","PCAF: an NGO that sets sector-level lending caps for banks financing high-emitting industries."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> RE100は、使用電力を100%再エネにする企業のイニシアティブ。<br><br><b>解説</b> RE100は、The Climate GroupがCDPと共同で運営する、事業で使う電力を100%再生可能エネルギーにする目標を掲げる企業の取り組み。SBTiは企業の削減目標が科学に整合するか検証する（オフセットは発行しない）。CDPは非営利の環境情報開示システムで規制当局ではない。PCAFは、金融機関の投融資に伴う排出量の算定基準を作る業界連携。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> SBTiはオフセットを発行せず、CDPは規制機関ではなく、PCAFは融資上限を定めない。<br><br>【出典】RE100, About us, https://www.there100.org/about-us"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch4 政策・ガバナンス","q":"[LO 4.12] According to the IPBES Global Assessment (2019), which list correctly gives the five direct drivers of biodiversity loss?","h":"陸と海の利用変化が最大の要因です。","c":["Changes in land and sea use, population growth, climate change, pollution and invasive alien species.","Direct exploitation of organisms, technological innovation, climate change, pollution and invasive alien species.","Changes in land and sea use, direct exploitation of organisms, climate change, income inequality and invasive alien species.","Changes in land and sea use, direct exploitation of organisms, climate change, pollution and invasive alien species."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 5つの直接要因は、土地・海の利用変化、生物の直接採取、気候変動、汚染、外来種。<br><br><b>解説</b> IPBES（生物多様性及び生態系サービスに関する政府間科学政策プラットフォーム）の2019年の地球規模評価は、生物多様性の損失の直接要因として、陸と海の利用変化（最大）、生物の直接採取（乱獲）、気候変動、汚染、外来種の5つを挙げる。人口増加や技術革新などは、間接要因に当たる。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 人口増加、技術革新、所得格差は間接要因で、直接要因ではない。<br><br>【出典】IPBES, Global Assessment Report on Biodiversity and Ecosystem Services, 2019, https://www.ipbes.net/global-assessment"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch4 政策・ガバナンス","q":"[LO 4.12] Under the IPBES classification, how is the pollination of crops by wild insects best categorised among ecosystem services (nature's contributions to people)?","h":"作物の受粉は、自然が調整する働きです。","c":["A provisioning service, because it is a physical product, such as food or fibre, that people harvest from nature.","A cultural service, because it is a non-material benefit, such as recreation or spiritual value, that people derive from nature.","A supporting service, because it is a financial return, such as a dividend, that the owner of the land receives from nature.","A regulating service, because it is a process by which nature moderates the conditions that support production."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 受粉は調整サービス。<br><br><b>解説</b> 生態系サービスは、供給（食料・水・木材）、調整（受粉、洪水の緩和、気候調整）、文化（レクリエーション、精神的価値）などに分類される（MEAの分類では支持サービスも置く）。受粉は、自然のプロセスが作物の生産条件を整える調整サービスで、金融機関にとっては、農業関連融資の「自然への依存」の例になる。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 収穫物は供給、非物質的な価値は文化。財務的な収益は生態系サービスの分類ではない。<br><br>【出典】IPBES, Global Assessment Report Summary for Policymakers (IPBES/7/10/Add.1), 2019, https://files.ipbes.net/ipbes-web-prod-public-files/ipbes_7_10_add.1_en_1.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch4 政策・ガバナンス","q":"[LO 4.12] The TNFD's final recommendations (September 2023) are structured how?","h":"TCFDの11開示に3つを加えた構成です。","c":["11 recommended disclosures across the same four pillars as the TCFD, with no new disclosures added for nature.","14 recommended disclosures across four pillars: governance, strategy, risk and impact management, and metrics and targets.","14 recommended disclosures across five pillars, adding a separate pillar for biodiversity targets.","20 recommended disclosures across four pillars, adding a financial impact test for every issuer."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> TNFDの最終提言は、4つの柱に14の開示。<br><br><b>解説</b> TNFD（自然関連財務情報開示タスクフォース）の2023年9月の最終提言は、TCFDと同じ4つの柱（ガバナンス、戦略、リスク・インパクト管理、指標と目標）に14の開示事項を置く。TCFDの11に、自然の依存・インパクトに関する開示を加えた構成。評価の手法はLEAPアプローチ。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 11開示のみ、5つの柱、20開示というのは、提言の構成と合わない。<br><br>【出典】TNFD, Recommendations of the Taskforce on Nature-related Financial Disclosures, 2023, https://tnfd.global/publication/recommendations-of-the-taskforce-on-nature-related-financial-disclosures/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch4 政策・ガバナンス","q":"[LO 4.13] Which of the following is NOT one of the six recommendations in the NGFS first comprehensive report 'A call for action' (2019)?","h":"資本の上乗せを義務づけるものは含まれていません。","c":["Integrate climate-related risks into financial stability monitoring and micro-supervision of individual banks and insurers, in line with their mandates.","Integrate sustainability factors into own-portfolio management of central banks.","Bridge data gaps and build awareness, intellectual capacity and knowledge sharing.","Require banks to hold a climate-specific capital surcharge from 2020, set by the NGFS for all member jurisdictions."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> NGFSの6提言に、気候専用の資本上乗せの義務化は含まれない。<br><br><b>解説</b> NGFSの2019年報告書の6提言は、(1)金融安定の監視とミクロ・プルーデンス監督への気候リスクの組み込み、(2)中央銀行の自己ポートフォリオ運用への組み込み、(3)データギャップの解消、(4)意識向上・知見・能力構築と技術支援、(5)堅牢で国際的に整合した開示、(6)経済活動の分類（タクソノミー）の開発支援。NGFSは資本上乗せを義務づける機関ではない。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 他の3つは、実際の提言の内容（1、2、3・4）に当たる。<br><br>【出典】NGFS, A call for action: Climate change as a source of financial risk, 2019, https://www.ngfs.net/en/first-comprehensive-report-call-action ／ NGFS, A call for action: Climate change as a source of financial risk, 2019, https://www.ngfs.net/sites/default/files/medias/documents/ngfs_first_comprehensive_report_-_17042019_0.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch4 政策・ガバナンス","q":"[LO 4.13] Which NGFS recommendation is directed at central banks' own balance sheets?","h":"中央銀行自身の運用を気候に配慮させる提言を問う問題です。","c":["Require commercial banks to divest every fossil-fuel exposure from the assets that they hold on behalf of their customers.","Fix a global carbon price that central banks collect from the emitters in their jurisdictions and recycle to households.","Prohibit central banks from holding any government bond issued by a country that has not set a net-zero target.","Integrate sustainability factors into the management of central banks' own portfolios, such as pension funds and own-account assets."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 中央銀行の自己ポートフォリオにサステナビリティ要因を組み込むことが、提言2。<br><br><b>解説</b> NGFSの提言2は、中央銀行が、自身の運用（年金基金、自己勘定資産、外貨準備など）にサステナビリティ要因を組み込むことを求める。中央銀行が率先して範を示す意味を持つ。化石燃料の全面売却や炭素価格の設定、国債の保有禁止は提言に含まれない。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 炭素価格の設定は財政当局の権限で、中央銀行の提言には入っていない。<br><br>【出典】NGFS, A call for action, 2019, https://www.ngfs.net/en/first-comprehensive-report-call-action ／ NGFS, A call for action: Climate change as a source of financial risk, 2019, https://www.ngfs.net/sites/default/files/medias/documents/ngfs_first_comprehensive_report_-_17042019_0.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch4 政策・ガバナンス","q":"[LO 4.13] The NGFS 2019 report recommends supporting a taxonomy of economic activities. What problem does this recommendation address?","h":"『何がグリーンか』という共通理解の欠如への対応です。","c":["The lack of a global carbon price, which prevents central banks from setting the policy rate in line with the carbon content of consumption, which therefore must be set by central banks themselves.","The lack of legal powers for central banks to ban lending to fossil-fuel companies, which prevents any form of transition from occurring.","The lack of a common understanding of which economic activities are green and which are not, which hampers consistent risk assessment and capital allocation.","The lack of insurance for coastal property, which prevents banks from lending against real estate in any area exposed to flooding."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 提言6は、グリーンな活動の共通理解を作り、リスク評価と資金配分を整合させる。<br><br><b>解説</b> NGFSは、何がグリーン・ブラウンかについての共通理解が欠けると、金融機関のリスク評価・投資判断が不整合になるとして、政策当局にタクソノミーの開発支援を求める。炭素価格の不在や融資禁止の権限といった問題を扱う提言ではない。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 炭素価格やローン禁止、保険の不足は、提言6の問題意識とは別の論点。<br><br>【出典】NGFS, A call for action, 2019, https://www.ngfs.net/en/first-comprehensive-report-call-action ／ NGFS, A call for action: Climate change as a source of financial risk, 2019, https://www.ngfs.net/sites/default/files/medias/documents/ngfs_first_comprehensive_report_-_17042019_0.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch4 政策・ガバナンス","q":"[LO 4.14] How does the NGFS first comprehensive report 'A call for action' (2019) describe its six recommendations?","h":"6つの提言は拘束力がなく、1〜4は中央銀行・監督当局向け、5〜6は政策当局向けです。","c":["They are binding rules adopted by all NGFS members, addressed to commercial banks and insurers, with penalties for non-compliance set by the NGFS Secretariat.","They are non-binding recommendations, of which the first two are addressed to policymakers and the remaining four to commercial banks and insurers.","They are non-binding recommendations reflecting members' best practices: the first four are aimed at central banks and supervisors, and the last two at policymakers.","They are legally binding obligations under the Paris Agreement, of which the first four apply to developed countries and the last two to developing countries."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> NGFSの6提言は拘束力のないベストプラクティスで、1〜4は中央銀行・監督当局向け、5〜6は政策当局向け。<br><br><b>解説</b> NGFS第1次包括報告書（2019年4月）は、金融セクターがパリ協定の目的の達成に果たす役割を促すため、拘束力のない6つの提言を示した。提言1〜4（リスクの金融安定監視・ミクロ監督への組み込み、自己ポートフォリオ運用への組み込み、データギャップの解消、意識向上・能力構築）は中央銀行・監督当局の取り組み向け、提言5〜6（堅牢で国際的に整合した開示、経済活動のタクソノミーの開発支援）は、中央銀行・監督当局の直接の権限の外にあり、政策当局に向けたもの。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 拘束力のある規則や罰則、パリ協定上の法的義務とする記述は、報告書の性格（非拘束・メンバーのベストプラクティス）と合わない。宛先を入れ替えた記述も誤り。<br><br>【出典】NGFS, A call for action: Climate change as a source of financial risk, 2019, https://www.ngfs.net/sites/default/files/medias/documents/ngfs_first_comprehensive_report_-_17042019_0.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch4 政策・ガバナンス","q":"[LO 4.14] Why does the NGFS argue that central banks and supervisors have a role in addressing climate change?","h":"気候変動が金融リスクの源泉であり、金融の安定と健全性の責務に含まれるためです。","c":["Because climate change is a source of financial risk, so ensuring the resilience of the financial system to it falls within their mandates for financial stability and prudential supervision.","Because the Paris Agreement legally obliges central banks to buy green assets, so the central banks must tilt their asset purchases accordingly, starting from the next reporting period under supervision by the UNFCCC.","Because central banks' primary mandate is to set national carbon prices, so they must therefore take the lead in the design of carbon taxes.","Because central banks regulate the emissions of non-financial firms, so they must set sector emission limits for their economies."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 気候変動は金融リスクの源泉で、金融安定・健全性の責務の範囲。<br><br><b>解説</b> NGFSは、気候変動が金融リスクの源泉であり、中央銀行・監督当局が責務（物価の安定、金融システムの安定、ミクロ・プルーデンス）の範囲内でリスクの把握・管理を進めるべきとする。パリ協定は中央銀行にグリーン資産の購入を義務づけておらず、炭素価格の設定や排出規制は中央銀行の役割でもない。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 購入義務、炭素価格の設定、排出規制はいずれも中央銀行の役割ではない。<br><br>【出典】NGFS, A call for action, 2019, https://www.ngfs.net/en/first-comprehensive-report-call-action ／ NGFS, A call for action: Climate change as a source of financial risk, 2019, https://www.ngfs.net/sites/default/files/medias/documents/ngfs_first_comprehensive_report_-_17042019_0.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch4 政策・ガバナンス","q":"[LO 4.14] At COP29 (Baku, 2024), what was agreed as the New Collective Quantified Goal (NCQG) on climate finance?","h":"2035年までに年3,000億ドルで、1.3兆ドルへの拡大を呼びかけました。","c":["At least USD 100 billion per year by 2030 for developing countries, within a call to scale up to USD 1.3 trillion per year by 2050.","At least USD 300 billion per year by 2035 for developing countries, within a call to scale up to USD 1.3 trillion per year from all sources.","At least USD 30 billion per year by 2035 for developing countries, within a call to scale up to USD 3 trillion per year from all sources.","At least USD 500 billion per year by 2030 for developing countries, within a call to scale up to USD 5 trillion per year by 2035."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> COP29のNCQGは、2035年までに年3,000億ドル、1.3兆ドルへの拡大を呼びかけ。<br><br><b>解説</b> COP29で合意されたNCQGは、先進国が主導して、2035年までに少なくとも年3,000億ドルを開発途上国に提供するとし、あらゆる公的・民間の資金源から年1.3兆ドルへの拡大に向けて取り組むよう、全てのアクターに呼びかけた。従前の目標は2020年までに年1,000億ドル（コペンハーゲン合意・カンクン合意）。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 年1,000億ドルは従前の目標。金額・年・拡大目標が一致しない他の選択肢は誤り。<br><br>【出典】UNFCCC, COP29 outcomes on climate finance, https://unfccc.int/cop29 ／ UNFCCC, Decision CMA.6 (New collective quantified goal on climate finance), 2024, https://unfccc.int/sites/default/files/resource/CMA_11(a)_NCQG.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch4 政策・ガバナンス","q":"[LO 4.15] Which list correctly gives the five accounting and reporting principles of the GHG Protocol Corporate Standard?","h":"関連性・完全性・一貫性・透明性・正確性の5つです。","c":["Relevance, completeness, consistency, transparency and accuracy.","Relevance, materiality, comparability, transparency and assurance.","Completeness, consistency, conservatism, timeliness and accuracy.","Relevance, verifiability, comparability, simplicity and accuracy."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 5原則は、関連性・完全性・一貫性・透明性・正確性。<br><br><b>解説</b> GHGプロトコル（企業算定・報告基準）の5原則は、関連性（利用者の意思決定に資する）、完全性（境界内の全排出源を網羅）、一貫性（比較可能な方法）、透明性（根拠を開示）、正確性（系統的な偏りと不確実性を抑える）。他の選択肢は、会計・保証基準の用語が混ざったもの。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 保守性、検証可能性、簡潔性、重要性、保証などは、5原則に含まれない。<br><br>【出典】WRI/WBCSD, GHG Protocol Corporate Standard, Chapter 1, https://ghgprotocol.org/corporate-standard"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch4 政策・ガバナンス","q":"[LO 4.15] A company changes its emission-calculation method for Scope 1 without disclosing the change and without restating earlier years. Which GHG Protocol principle is most directly compromised?","h":"年を超えて比較できる方法の継続が崩れています。","c":["Completeness, because every emission source inside the chosen boundary must be covered, which a method change automatically breaks.","Consistency, because meaningful comparisons of emissions over time require consistent methodologies or transparently documented changes.","Relevance, because the method must be selected by the users of the report, which the company did not consult in advance.","Accuracy, because any change in method automatically makes the earlier inventory wrong, so that no comparison could ever be valid."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 算定方法を無断で変えると、年次比較ができなくなる＝一貫性の原則に反する。<br><br><b>解説</b> 一貫性の原則は、時系列での意味のある比較のために、一貫した方法を使い、方法の変更や、その他の要因の変更を文書化することを求める。方法を変えたことを開示しなければ、透明性にも反する。完全性は網羅性、関連性は利用者のニーズ、正確性は偏りの抑制に関する原則で、本ケースの主論点ではない。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 完全性・関連性・正確性は、方法の変更の開示・遡及とは別の論点。<br><br>【出典】WRI/WBCSD, GHG Protocol Corporate Standard, Chapter 1, https://ghgprotocol.org/corporate-standard"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch4 政策・ガバナンス","q":"[LO 4.15] Under the GHG Protocol Corporate Standard, which event would normally require a company to recalculate its base-year emissions?","h":"構造的な変更は再計算し、有機的な増減は再計算しません。","c":["A 12% increase in output at existing facilities that causes emissions to rise in line with production.","The acquisition of a business whose emissions are significant relative to the company's base-year emissions.","The commissioning of a new plant that the company built itself to meet growing demand for its products.","A fall in sales caused by weak demand, which leads the company to run its existing plants at lower output."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 買収などの構造変化は基準年の再計算が必要で、有機的な増減は不要。<br><br><b>解説</b> GHGプロトコルは、構造変更（合併・買収・売却、アウトソーシング・インソーシング）、算定方法や排出係数の変更、誤りの発見が重要な水準に達した場合に、基準年排出量の再計算を求める。生産量の増減や自社新設などの有機的成長・縮小では再計算しない。一貫性ある比較のため。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 生産増、自社新設、需要減による稼働低下は有機的な変化で、再計算は不要。<br><br>【出典】WRI/WBCSD, GHG Protocol Corporate Standard, Chapter 5, https://ghgprotocol.org/corporate-standard"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch4 政策・ガバナンス","q":"[LO 4.16] A company holds 40% of a joint venture (JV), has operational control but not financial control, and the JV emits 1,000 tCO2e of direct emissions. How are the JV's direct emissions reported in the company's Scope 1 under each consolidation approach?","h":"連結のアプローチごとに、報告する割合が変わります。","c":["Operational control: 400 tCO2e; equity share: 1,000 tCO2e; financial control: 400 tCO2e.","Operational control: 0 tCO2e; equity share: 400 tCO2e; financial control: 1,000 tCO2e.","Operational control: 1,000 tCO2e; equity share: 1,000 tCO2e; financial control: 400 tCO2e.","Operational control: 1,000 tCO2e; equity share: 400 tCO2e; financial control: 0 tCO2e."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 運用支配なら100%、持分比率なら40%、財務支配がなければ0。<br><br><b>解説</b> GHGプロトコルの連結アプローチは、持分比率（出資割合）、財務支配、運用支配の3つ。運用支配では、支配するJVの排出を100%算入する。持分比率では40%。財務支配では、財務支配がなければ算入せず、スコープ3（カテゴリ15・投資）で扱う。どのアプローチを使うかを選び、一貫して適用・開示する。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 運用支配が持分比率に、財務支配が運用支配に入れ替わった組み合わせは誤り。<br><br>【出典】WRI/WBCSD, GHG Protocol Corporate Standard, Chapter 3, https://ghgprotocol.org/corporate-standard"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch4 政策・ガバナンス","q":"[LO 4.16] Under the GHG Protocol Corporate Standard, which emissions must a company include in its operational boundary and which are optional?","h":"スコープ1と2は必須、スコープ3は任意（企業基準）です。","c":["Scope 1 is required, while Scope 2 and Scope 3 are both optional reporting categories.","Scope 1 and Scope 2 are required, while Scope 3 is an optional reporting category.","Scope 1 and Scope 3 are required, while Scope 2 is an optional reporting category.","Scope 1, Scope 2 and Scope 3 are all required, with no exclusion permitted in any case."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 企業基準では、スコープ1・2が必須で、スコープ3は任意。<br><br><b>解説</b> Corporate Standard（改訂版、2004）は、運用上の境界のうち、スコープ1とスコープ2は必須とし、スコープ3は任意の報告カテゴリとする。企業バリューチェーン（スコープ3）基準は、スコープ3の全カテゴリを算定し、除外は理由を開示することを求める。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> スコープ2が任意とする、スコープ3を必須とする選択肢は、基準の記述と合わない。<br><br>【出典】WRI/WBCSD, GHG Protocol Corporate Standard, Chapter 4, https://ghgprotocol.org/corporate-standard"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch4 政策・ガバナンス","q":"[LO 4.16] A company decides to exclude two Scope 3 categories from its Scope 3 inventory. What does the GHG Protocol Corporate Value Chain (Scope 3) Standard require?","h":"除外した場合は、開示して理由を説明します。","c":["It must keep the excluded categories confidential, because disclosure of omissions could mislead users about the inventory, and may be reported only to the regulator.","It must exclude all remaining categories as well, because partial reporting is not permitted under the standard.","It must disclose and justify the exclusion of any Scope 3 category, and it should explain why the exclusion does not undermine the inventory's relevance.","It must replace the excluded categories with an offset purchase, because the standard requires a net figure for Scope 3."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 除外したカテゴリは開示し、正当化する。<br><br><b>解説</b> Scope 3基準は、企業に15カテゴリ全体の排出の算定を求め、除外するカテゴリは理由とともに開示することを求める。完全性の原則に沿う。除外を非公表にしたり、他のカテゴリもまとめて除外したり、オフセットで代替したりすることを求める規定はない。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 非公表、全除外、オフセット代替は、基準の要求ではない。<br><br>【出典】WRI/WBCSD, Corporate Value Chain (Scope 3) Standard, Chapter 6, https://ghgprotocol.org/corporate-value-chain-scope-3-standard"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch5 グリーンファイナンス","q":"[LO 5.1] Which statement best describes the relationship between sustainable finance, green finance and climate finance?","h":"広い順に、サステナブル→グリーン→気候の入れ子になっています。","c":["Sustainable finance covers environmental, social and governance objectives; green finance is its environmental subset; climate finance is the part of that subset that addresses climate mitigation and adaptation.","Climate finance is the broadest concept; green finance is its social subset; sustainable finance is the part of that subset that addresses climate mitigation and adaptation.","Green finance covers environmental, social and governance objectives; sustainable finance is its environmental subset; climate finance is the part of that subset that addresses climate mitigation and adaptation.","The three terms are interchangeable synonyms that describe the same set of instruments, so none of them can be treated as a subset of another one."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> サステナブル・ファイナンス＞グリーン・ファイナンス＞気候ファイナンスという入れ子。<br><br><b>解説</b> サステナブル・ファイナンスは、環境・社会・ガバナンス（ESG）の目的を持つ金融全般。グリーン・ファイナンスはそのうち環境面（気候、生物多様性、汚染、水など）を対象とし、気候ファイナンスは、さらにその中で気候変動の緩和と適応を対象とする。ソーシャル・ファイナンスは、サステナブルのうち社会面を扱う別の部分集合。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 気候→グリーン→サステナブルの順に広いとする選択肢は、入れ子の方向が逆。3語が同義とする記述は誤り。<br><br>【出典】Climate Policy Initiative, Global Landscape of Climate Finance 2023, https://www.climatepolicyinitiative.org/publications/global-landscape-of-climate-finance-2023/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch5 グリーンファイナンス","q":"[LO 5.1] According to the ICMA Climate Transition Finance Handbook, which set of elements should an issuer disclose to support credible transition-labelled financing?","h":"戦略とガバナンス、ビジネスモデルへの重要性、科学に基づく目標、実行の透明性の4つです。","c":["Climate transition strategy and governance; shareholder return policy; carbon credit purchases; and a third-party credit rating of the issuer.","Climate transition strategy and governance; use of proceeds; management of proceeds; and annual impact reporting on the funded projects only.","Business model environmental materiality; offset-based targets; supplier-specific emission data; and exclusive reliance on external audits.","Climate transition strategy and governance; business model environmental materiality; science-based targets and pathways; and implementation transparency."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 移行ファイナンスでは、4つの要素を開示する。<br><br><b>解説</b> ICMAのクライメート・トランジション・ファイナンス・ハンドブック（2020年、2023年改訂）は、発行体に、(1)気候移行戦略とガバナンス、(2)ビジネスモデルへの環境面の重要性、(3)科学に基づく目標と経路、(4)実施の透明性（資本支出の計画などを含む）の開示を求める。これらを示すことで、使途特定型でもSLB型でも、移行の資金調達として位置づけられる。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 配当、クレジット購入、信用格付け、使途管理は、4つの要素に含まれない。<br><br>【出典】ICMA, Climate Transition Finance Handbook, https://www.icma-group.org/sustainable-finance/the-principles-guidelines-and-handbooks/climate-transition-finance-handbook/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch5 グリーンファイナンス","q":"[LO 5.1] A developer retrofits an aging social housing block in a low-income area to cut its energy use and heating costs. How is the project best classified within sustainable finance?","h":"環境（省エネ）と社会（低所得者向け住宅）の両方に当たります。","c":["It overlaps the green (energy efficiency) and social (affordable housing) categories, so it could be eligible for a sustainability bond.","It is purely social because affordable housing is involved, so green criteria are irrelevant and a green bond could never fund it.","It is purely green because energy efficiency is involved, so social criteria are irrelevant and a social bond could never fund it.","It is neither green nor social because retrofits are ordinary capital expenditure, so no labelled instrument could finance it at all."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 省エネ（グリーン）と低所得者向け住宅（ソーシャル）の重なり。<br><br><b>解説</b> ICMAのGBPでは省エネ建築がグリーン、SBPでは低価格の住宅がソーシャルのプロジェクトカテゴリ。両面を持つプロジェクトは、サステナビリティ・ボンド（グリーンとソーシャルの組み合わせに充当）の対象になり得る。分類の「重なり」は、資金使途の整理で重要になる。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 片方のみとする、またはどちらにも当たらないとする選択肢は、プロジェクトの二面性を見落としている。<br><br>【出典】ICMA, Green Bond Principles / Social Bond Principles, https://www.icma-group.org/sustainable-finance/the-principles-guidelines-and-handbooks/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch5 グリーンファイナンス","q":"[LO 5.2] According to the IEA's World Energy Investment 2024, how did global investment in clean energy compare with investment in fossil fuels in 2024?","h":"クリーンエネルギーへの投資は、化石燃料のおよそ2倍でした。","c":["About USD 2 trillion went to clean energy technologies and infrastructure, roughly half the amount invested in fossil fuels.","About USD 2 trillion went to clean energy technologies and infrastructure, roughly twice the amount invested in fossil fuels.","About USD 0.5 trillion went to clean energy technologies and infrastructure, roughly twice the amount invested in fossil fuels.","About USD 2 trillion went to clean energy technologies and infrastructure, roughly the same as the amount invested in fossil fuels."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 2024年は、クリーンエネルギー投資が約2兆ドルで、化石燃料の約2倍。<br><br><b>解説</b> IEAのWorld Energy Investment 2024によれば、2024年の世界のエネルギー投資は約3兆ドルで、うちクリーンエネルギーが約2兆ドル、化石燃料が約1兆ドルと、クリーンエネルギーが約2倍。2015年にはほぼ同額だったが、太陽光・蓄電池・送電網への投資が拡大してきた。ただし新興国・途上国（中国を除く）への投資は不足している。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 金額や比率を変えた選択肢は、IEAの報告と一致しない。<br><br><b>日本との対応</b> 日本では、GX経済移行債による20兆円規模の先行投資支援が、この分野への資金移動を後押しする。<br><br>【出典】IEA, World Energy Investment 2024, https://www.iea.org/reports/world-energy-investment-2024 ／ 財務省, GX経済移行債（クライメート・トランジション利付国債）, https://www.mof.go.jp/public_relations/finance/202405/202405c.html"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch5 グリーンファイナンス","q":"[LO 5.2] Which statement about tracked climate finance flows is consistent with Climate Policy Initiative's Global Landscape of Climate Finance (2023)?","h":"大半が緩和に向かい、適応はごく一部です。","c":["The large majority of tracked climate finance goes to adaptation, and mitigation receives only a single-digit percentage of the total.","Mitigation and adaptation each receive about half of the tracked climate finance, so the two are balanced and need no policy action.","The large majority of tracked climate finance goes to mitigation, and adaptation receives only a single-digit percentage of the total.","Almost all tracked climate finance goes to fossil-fuel-related projects, and mitigation and adaptation receive under five percent combined."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 追跡される気候資金の大半は緩和向けで、適応は1桁％。<br><br><b>解説</b> CPIの『Global Landscape of Climate Finance 2023』は、気候資金の年間フローが、2021/22年平均で約1.3兆ドルと初めて1兆ドルを超えたと推計する。そのうち大半は緩和向けで、適応は約630億ドル規模（全体の約5%）にとどまる。適応資金の不足は、気候リスクが高い途上国の脆弱性に関わる。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 適応が大半、半々、化石燃料向けが大半という記述は、CPIの推計と合わない。<br><br>【出典】Climate Policy Initiative, Global Landscape of Climate Finance 2023, https://www.climatepolicyinitiative.org/publications/global-landscape-of-climate-finance-2023/ ／ Climate Policy Initiative, Global Landscape of Climate Finance 2023, Executive Summary, https://www.climatepolicyinitiative.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/Executive-Summary-l-Global-Landscape-of-Climate-Finance-2023.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch5 グリーンファイナンス","q":"[LO 5.2] Which statement about the geographic pattern of climate finance is consistent with CPI's Global Landscape of Climate Finance (2023)?","h":"資金は特定の3地域に集中し、中国を除く新興・途上国向けは15%程度です。","c":["Emerging markets and developing economies other than China received most tracked climate finance, while East Asia and the Pacific, the US and Canada and Western Europe together received under a fifth.","Most tracked climate finance is invested in a handful of tax havens, because investors seek jurisdictions with no climate regulation at all, and private actors provide under one percent of the total.","Most tracked climate finance is public grant funding from multilateral development banks, with private finance below one percent of the total, while adaptation finance is the largest category.","East Asia and the Pacific, the US and Canada and Western Europe together account for a large majority of tracked climate finance, while only about 15% goes to or within emerging and developing economies other than China."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 気候資金は東アジア・太平洋、米国・カナダ、西欧の3地域に約84%が集中し、中国を除く新興・途上国向けは約15%。<br><br><b>解説</b> CPIの『Global Landscape of Climate Finance 2023』によれば、2021/22年平均の気候資金（約1.3兆ドル）のうち、東アジア・太平洋、米国・カナダ、西欧の3地域が合計84%を占める。後発開発途上国（LDC）向けは3%未満（約300億ドル）、中国を除く新興・途上国向けは15%にとどまり、資金は必要額に対して不足している。民間資金は全体の49%（約6,250億ドル）。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 新興・途上国向けが大半、タックスヘイブンへの集中、公的助成が大半で民間1%未満、適応が最大という記述は、CPIの推計と合わない（適応は約630億ドルで全体の約5%）。<br><br>【出典】Climate Policy Initiative, Global Landscape of Climate Finance 2023, Executive Summary, https://www.climatepolicyinitiative.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/Executive-Summary-l-Global-Landscape-of-Climate-Finance-2023.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch5 グリーンファイナンス","q":"[LO 5.3] A bond's investors have a claim only on the revenue streams, fees or taxes of a green project, with no recourse to the issuer's other assets. Under the ICMA Green Bond Principles, which type of green bond is this?","h":"事業のキャッシュフローだけが返済の源泉となる型です。","c":["A standard green use-of-proceeds bond, which is backed by the issuer's balance sheet with full recourse.","A green securitised bond, which is backed by a pool of assets and has no use-of-proceeds requirement.","A green revenue bond, whose debt obligation is backed by the revenue streams of the green project.","A green general-purpose bond, which has no restriction on how the issuer chooses to spend the proceeds."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 収益のみが返済原資となる債券は、グリーン・レベニュー債。<br><br><b>解説</b> ICMAのGBPは、グリーンボンドを4つに分類する。スタンダード・グリーン使途特定債（発行体へのリコースあり）、グリーン・レベニュー債（プロジェクトの収入・手数料・税収に限定される）、グリーン・プロジェクト債（特定のプロジェクトのリスクを投資家が直接負う）、グリーン証券化債（資産プールが裏付け）。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> スタンダード債は発行体全体の信用で返済される。使途の制限がない債券は、GBPの対象外。<br><br>【出典】ICMA, Green Bond Principles, https://www.icma-group.org/sustainable-finance/the-principles-guidelines-and-handbooks/green-bond-principles-gbp/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch5 グリーンファイナンス","q":"[LO 5.3] Which of the following is an eligible project category under the ICMA Social Bond Principles?","h":"社会的なテーマの例を選びます。","c":["Pollution prevention and control.","Renewable energy.","Climate change adaptation.","Affordable housing."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 低価格の住宅はソーシャルのカテゴリ。<br><br><b>解説</b> SBPの例示カテゴリは、低価格の基本インフラ（上下水道、衛生、交通）、必須サービスへのアクセス（健康、教育）、低価格の住宅、雇用の創出（中小企業向け融資・マイクロファイナンスを含む）、食料の安全保障と持続可能な食料システム、社会経済的向上とエンパワーメント。再エネ、汚染防止、気候変動への適応は、GBPのグリーンのカテゴリ。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 他の3つは、GBPの環境面のカテゴリ。<br><br>【出典】ICMA, Social Bond Principles, https://www.icma-group.org/sustainable-finance/the-principles-guidelines-and-handbooks/social-bond-principles-sbp/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch5 グリーンファイナンス","q":"[LO 5.3] An investor holds a standard use-of-proceeds green bond issued by a corporate. Which statement about its credit risk is correct?","h":"グリーンのラベルは、発行体の信用リスクを変えるものではありません。","c":["It has recourse only to the green project and normally ranks below the issuer's other senior unsecured debt, so its credit risk is that of the project.","It is guaranteed by the bond's external reviewer and normally ranks above all other debt of the issuer, so its credit risk is that of the reviewer.","It has recourse to the issuer and normally ranks equally with the issuer's other senior unsecured debt, so its credit risk is that of the issuer.","It carries no credit risk because proceeds are ring-fenced in a government account, so the investor cannot lose capital on the bond."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> スタンダード型のグリーンボンドは、発行体の信用リスクを負い、他の無担保債務と同順位。<br><br><b>解説</b> スタンダード・グリーン使途特定債は、発行体にリコースがあり、通常は同じ発行体の他の無担保シニア債とパリパスで、信用リスクは発行体のもの。グリーンのラベルは調達資金の使途を示すもので、信用補完ではない。外部レビューは保証ではなく、使途の適合性についての意見。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> プロジェクトのみへのリコース、外部レビュー機関の保証、政府口座での保全は、スタンダード型の特徴ではない。<br><br>【出典】ICMA, Green Bond Principles, https://www.icma-group.org/sustainable-finance/the-principles-guidelines-and-handbooks/green-bond-principles-gbp/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch5 グリーンファイナンス","q":"[LO 5.4] Besides the four core components, what do the ICMA Green Bond Principles recommend that issuers do to support transparency?","h":"フレームワークの公表と、外部レビューの活用が推奨されています。","c":["Publish a Green Bond Framework outlining the alignment with the four components, and use external review such as a second-party opinion.","Obtain a government licence for the green label, and submit annual reports to the national securities regulator for approval.","Hold unallocated proceeds in fossil-fuel securities until a project is selected, and report only on the first anniversary of issuance.","List the bond on a green exchange segment, and have the issuer's own auditor give a binding guarantee of the bond's returns."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> グリーンボンド・フレームワークを示し、外部レビューを受けることが推奨される。<br><br><b>解説</b> GBPは、4つの中核要素（資金使途、プロジェクトの評価・選定のプロセス、調達資金の管理、レポーティング）に加え、発行体が、4要素への整合を示すグリーンボンド・フレームワークを公表することと、外部レビュー（セカンドパーティ・オピニオン、検証、認証、格付）の活用を推奨する。GBPは自主的ガイドラインで、政府の免許は不要。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 免許、化石燃料での待機運用、取引所上場の義務、リターンの保証は、GBPにない。<br><br>【出典】ICMA, Green Bond Principles, https://www.icma-group.org/sustainable-finance/the-principles-guidelines-and-handbooks/green-bond-principles-gbp/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch5 グリーンファイナンス","q":"[LO 5.4] Under the 'Management of Proceeds' component of the Green Bond Principles, which practice is expected?","h":"調達資金は、区分して追跡・管理することが求められます。","c":["The net proceeds should be credited to a sub-account or otherwise tracked, with the issuer attesting to this in a formal internal process.","The net proceeds should be paid directly to the bond's external reviewer, which then selects and funds the eligible projects for the issuer.","The net proceeds should be placed into the issuer's general account with no tracking, because green status depends only on the label at issuance.","The net proceeds should be distributed to investors as a coupon rebate, because the green label does not require any use of the funds."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 調達資金は、サブ口座などで区分・追跡し、発行体が内部プロセスで確認する。<br><br><b>解説</b> GBPの「調達資金の管理」は、純調達資金を、サブ口座に入金する、サブポートフォリオに移す、またはその他の適切な方法で追跡し、発行体が正式な内部プロセスで確認することを求める。未充当資金の残高は、一時的な運用先を開示する。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 外部レビュー機関への送金、追跡なしの一般口座、クーポンの割戻しは、原則にない。<br><br>【出典】ICMA, Green Bond Principles, https://www.icma-group.org/sustainable-finance/the-principles-guidelines-and-handbooks/green-bond-principles-gbp/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch5 グリーンファイナンス","q":"[LO 5.4] Which description of the 'Reporting' component of the Green Bond Principles is correct?","h":"資金の充当状況とインパクトを、少なくとも年1回報告します。","c":["Issuers should report once at issuance and then only if requested by an investor, including a statement on the validity of the green label.","Issuers should report every five years to a regulator and then should not publish any information about the use of proceeds to the public.","Issuers should report quarterly on the bond's trading price, including a list of the secondary-market buyers and the pricing of the green label, with reports audited by an external credit rating agency.","Issuers should report at least annually until full allocation and then on material developments, including a list of projects, amounts allocated and expected impact."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 充当が終わるまで少なくとも年1回、その後も重要な変化があれば報告する。<br><br><b>解説</b> GBPのレポーティングは、資金の充当に関する最新情報を、全額が充当されるまで少なくとも年1回、その後は重要な進展があった場合にも、更新して利用可能にすることを求める。プロジェクトの一覧、充当額、期待されるインパクト（定性、可能なら定量の指標）を含む。ICMAは、インパクト報告のハーモナイズされた枠組みも公表している。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 発行時のみ、5年ごと、価格や買い手の報告は、原則にない。<br><br>【出典】ICMA, Green Bond Principles, https://www.icma-group.org/sustainable-finance/the-principles-guidelines-and-handbooks/green-bond-principles-gbp/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch5 グリーンファイナンス","q":"[LO 5.5] Which organisations jointly publish the Green Loan Principles and Social Loan Principles?","h":"ローン市場の業界団体が策定した自主的な原則です。","c":["The International Capital Market Association (ICMA), the Climate Bonds Initiative (CBI) and the International Monetary Fund (IMF).","The Loan Market Association (LMA), the Asia Pacific Loan Market Association (APLMA) and the Loan Syndications and Trading Association (LSTA).","The European Commission, the European Central Bank and the European Securities and Markets Authority (ESMA).","The Basel Committee on Banking Supervision (BCBS), the Financial Stability Board (FSB) and the International Organization of Securities Commissions (IOSCO)."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> LMA・APLMA・LSTAの3団体が、ローン原則を共同で策定している。<br><br><b>解説</b> グリーンローン原則（GLP、2018年）、ソーシャルローン原則（SLP、2021年）、サステナビリティ・リンク・ローン原則（SLLP）は、LMA、APLMA、LSTAが策定する自主的ガイドライン。債券のGBP・SBPはICMAが策定している。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> ICMAは債券、EU当局やバーゼル委員会は規制・監督の機関で、ローン原則の策定者ではない。<br><br>【出典】LMA, Sustainable lending, https://www.lma.eu.com/sustainable-lending"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch5 グリーンファイナンス","q":"[LO 5.5] A company draws a revolving credit facility for general corporate purposes. The margin falls if the company cuts its emissions intensity below set targets. How should this facility be classified?","h":"使途は限定されず、条件が目標の達成度に連動しています。","c":["A sustainability-linked loan, because its pricing is linked to sustainability performance and the proceeds are not restricted to specific green projects.","A green loan, because any loan that rewards emissions cuts must have its proceeds restricted to eligible green projects under the principles.","A social loan, because any loan with a pricing link must target a defined population that is to benefit from the funded activity.","A conventional loan, because only use-of-proceeds structures can be labelled under the loan market principles in any circumstance."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 使途が限定されず、金利が目標達成に連動するローンは、サステナビリティ・リンク・ローン。<br><br><b>解説</b> SLLは、借り手のサステナビリティ・パフォーマンスの目標（SPTs）の達成度に応じて経済条件（金利のマージンなど）が変わるローンで、使途は限定されない。グリーンローン・ソーシャルローンは、使途特定型。SLLPは、KPIの選定、SPTsの設定、ローンの特性、報告、検証を中核要素とする。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> グリーンローンやソーシャルローンは使途を限定する。SLLは、使途特定でなくてもラベルの対象になる。<br><br>【出典】LMA/APLMA/LSTA, Sustainability-Linked Loan Principles, https://www.lma.eu.com/sustainable-lending"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch5 グリーンファイナンス","q":"[LO 5.5] Which of the following would be eligible for a social loan under the Social Loan Principles?","h":"特定の対象層に社会的な便益をもたらす資金使途を選びます。","c":["A loan that finances a commercial office tower in a prime business district, with reporting on leasable floor area.","A loan that finances an upgrade of luxury hotel rooms in a tourist region, with reporting on the average room rate.","A loan that finances low-cost clinics in underserved rural communities, with reporting on the patients served.","A loan that finances corporate share buybacks for a listed company, with reporting on the earnings per share."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 対象層に明確な社会的便益がある使途が、ソーシャルローンの対象。<br><br><b>解説</b> SLPは、特定の対象層（target population）に対して明確な社会的便益をもたらすプロジェクトに資金を充てるローンを指す。必須サービス（医療・教育）へのアクセスがその例。4つの中核要素（使途、プロジェクト評価と選定、資金管理、報告）はGLPと共通。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 商業ビル、高級ホテル、自社株買いは、対象層への社会的便益がない。<br><br>【出典】LMA/APLMA/LSTA, Social Loan Principles, https://www.lma.eu.com/sustainable-lending"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch5 グリーンファイナンス","q":"[LO 5.6] Which list correctly gives the five core components of the ICMA Sustainability-Linked Bond Principles?","h":"KPI・SPT・債券の特性・報告・検証の5つです。","c":["Selection of KPIs; calibration of Sustainability Performance Targets; bond characteristics; reporting; and verification.","Use of proceeds; process for project evaluation; management of proceeds; reporting; and external review, each set by the listing exchange.","Selection of KPIs; use of proceeds; bond characteristics; investor engagement; and a credit rating.","Calibration of targets; use of proceeds; coupon step-down; collateral package; and external review."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> SLBPの5要素は、KPI、SPT、債券の特性、報告、検証。<br><br><b>解説</b> SLBPは、KPIの選定、サステナビリティ・パフォーマンス・ターゲット（SPT）の設定、債券の特性（ステップアップなどの財務的な変化）、報告、検証を中核要素とする。使途特定ではないため、GBPの4要素（使途、選定、管理、報告）とは異なる。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 使途や資金管理を含む選択肢は、GBPの要素と混ざっている。<br><br>【出典】ICMA, Sustainability-Linked Bond Principles, https://www.icma-group.org/sustainable-finance/the-principles-guidelines-and-handbooks/sustainability-linked-bond-principles-slbp/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch5 グリーンファイナンス","q":"[LO 5.6] According to the SLBP, which characteristic should a Key Performance Indicator (KPI) have?","h":"発行体の事業にとって中核的で重要な指標であることが求められます。","c":["It should be unrelated to the issuer's core business, so that any conflict between financial and sustainability objectives is avoided altogether.","It should be relevant, core and material to the issuer's overall business, and be measurable on a consistent methodological basis and externally verifiable.","It should be reported in a way that cannot be benchmarked, because external comparison would reduce the issuer's flexibility in target setting.","It should be an absolute financial measure such as net income, because only financial KPIs can be linked to the coupon of a bond."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> KPIは、事業にとって中核的・重要で、一貫した方法で測定でき、外部検証が可能であること。<br><br><b>解説</b> SLBPは、KPIを、発行体の事業全体にとって関連性が高く、中核的で重要なものとし、一貫した方法で測定可能、外部検証可能で、可能であればベンチマークできるものとする。事業と無関係な指標を選ぶと、実質的な改善につながらず、グリーンウォッシュの懸念を招く。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 事業と無関係、比較不能、財務指標のみ、といった条件はSLBPの要件にない。<br><br>【出典】ICMA, Sustainability-Linked Bond Principles, https://www.icma-group.org/sustainable-finance/the-principles-guidelines-and-handbooks/sustainability-linked-bond-principles-slbp/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch5 グリーンファイナンス","q":"[LO 5.6] How should Sustainability Performance Targets (SPTs) be calibrated under the SLBP?","h":"通常の延長線を超える、野心的な目標が求められます。","c":["They should equal the issuer's current performance, so that the target is certain to be met and the coupon is never stepped up.","They should be set after maturity of the bond, so that the issuer can choose the level once its results are already known.","They should represent a material improvement over a business-as-usual trajectory and be benchmarked against peers or science where possible.","They should be chosen by the underwriter without disclosure, so that investors cannot compare them with other issuers' targets."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> SPTは、BAUを超える大幅な改善を示し、同業や科学と比較して設定する。<br><br><b>解説</b> SLBPは、SPTsを、発行体のBAUの軌道を超えた重要な改善を示し、可能であれば、同業他社や科学（パリ協定整合など）で比較して設定することを求める。目標が弱いとSLBの信頼性が損なわれる。目標・時期・ステップアップの条件は、発行前に明確にする。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 現状維持、満期後の設定、非開示の目標は、SLBPに反する。<br><br>【出典】ICMA, Sustainability-Linked Bond Principles, https://www.icma-group.org/sustainable-finance/the-principles-guidelines-and-handbooks/sustainability-linked-bond-principles-slbp/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch5 グリーンファイナンス","q":"[LO 5.7] A fund excludes issuers that violate the UN Global Compact principles, the OECD Guidelines for Multinational Enterprises or ILO conventions. Which sustainable investment strategy is this?","h":"国際規範への違反の有無で選別する手法です。","c":["Best-in-class screening, which selects the top-rated issuers in each sector regardless of any norms.","Norms-based screening, which screens investments against minimum standards set by international norms.","Sustainability-themed investing, which targets assets that address one specific sustainability theme.","Impact investing, which targets measurable outcomes in addition to a financial return on the capital."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 国際規範に反する企業を除外するのが、規範ベース・スクリーニング。<br><br><b>解説</b> 規範ベース・スクリーニングは、国連グローバル・コンパクト、OECD多国籍企業行動指針、ILO条約などの国際規範の最低基準を満たさない投資先を除外する。GSIAの分類では、ネガティブ（除外）、ポジティブ/ベスト・イン・クラス、規範ベース、ESGインテグレーション、テーマ型、インパクト・コミュニティ投資、エンゲージメント・議決権行使に分かれる。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> ベスト・イン・クラスは業種内の上位選別、テーマ型は特定テーマ、インパクトは成果の測定が特徴。<br><br>【出典】GSIA, Global Sustainable Investment Review 2022, https://www.gsi-alliance.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/GSIA-Report-2022.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch5 グリーンファイナンス","q":"[LO 5.7] A fund invests only in companies that derive most of their revenue from solar, wind and battery storage. Which strategy does it follow?","h":"テーマ（再エネ・蓄電）に沿った企業に投資する手法です。","c":["Negative screening, which removes certain sectors from a broad index but keeps the remaining market weights unchanged.","Sustainability-themed investing, which allocates capital to assets contributing to a defined sustainability theme such as clean energy.","Norms-based screening, which excludes companies that breach international conventions but does not select by theme.","ESG integration, which adjusts financial forecasts for ESG factors without restricting the investable universe of the fund."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 特定のテーマに投資するのが、テーマ型。<br><br><b>解説</b> サステナビリティ・テーマ型投資は、クリーンエネルギー、水、気候変動対策などの特定テーマに貢献する資産に配分する。ネガティブ・スクリーニングや規範ベースは除外、ESGインテグレーションは分析の中での考慮が特徴。テーマ型は、特定の分野への集中リスクがある。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 他の選択肢は、除外・規範・分析の手法で、テーマで選定する手法ではない。<br><br>【出典】GSIA, Global Sustainable Investment Review 2022, https://www.gsi-alliance.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/GSIA-Report-2022.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch5 グリーンファイナンス","q":"[LO 5.7] Under ESMA's Guidelines on funds' names using ESG or sustainability-related terms (2024), what minimum share of investments must a fund meet to use such a term in its name?","h":"名称にESG用語を使う場合の最低比率を問う問題です。","c":["At least 50% of its investments must be used to meet the environmental or social characteristics or sustainable objectives, with no exclusions.","At least 65% of its investments must be used to meet the environmental or social characteristics or sustainable objectives, with exclusions optional.","At least 95% of its investments must be used to meet the environmental or social characteristics or sustainable objectives, with exclusions banned.","At least 80% of its investments must be used to meet the environmental or social characteristics or sustainable objectives, and exclusions apply."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> ESG用語を名称に使うファンドは、投資の80%以上を目的に沿って運用し、除外基準も適用する。<br><br><b>解説</b> ESMAのファンド名称ガイドライン（2024年）は、ESG関連の用語を名称に用いるファンドに、投資の少なくとも80%を、環境・社会の特性や持続可能な目的を満たすために用いることを求める。加えて、用語の種類に応じて、パリ協定適合ベンチマーク（PAB）の除外基準などを適用する。新規ファンドには2024年11月21日、既存ファンドには2025年5月21日から適用。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 50%、65%、95%や、除外の有無などの数字は、ガイドラインの内容と異なる。<br><br>【出典】ESMA, ESMA Guidelines establish harmonised criteria for use of ESG and sustainability terms in fund names, 2024, https://www.esma.europa.eu/press-news/esma-news/esma-guidelines-establish-harmonised-criteria-use-esg-and-sustainability-terms"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch5 グリーンファイナンス","q":"[LO 5.8] Which of the following is a consumer-facing sustainable finance product?","h":"個人向けの商品を選びます。","c":["A syndicated sustainability-linked loan arranged for a large utility and sold to institutional lenders.","A catastrophe bond sold to reinsurers and specialist funds to transfer natural-catastrophe risk.","A green savings deposit whose balances are allocated by the bank to finance eligible green projects.","A green project bond whose proceeds are tied to one wind farm and sold to institutional investors."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 個人向けのグリーン預金は、消費者向けの商品。<br><br><b>解説</b> 消費者向けのサステナブル・ファイナンスには、グリーン預金・リテール向けグリーンボンド、グリーン住宅ローン、EV・省エネ設備ローン、ESG投信・ETF、サステナブル保険などがある。大企業向けのシンジケートSLL、再保険向けのキャットボンド、機関投資家向けのプロジェクト債は、機関向けの商品。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 他の3つは、機関投資家・企業・再保険会社向けの商品。<br><br>【出典】一般的な商品区分の例示（特定の一次資料は未確認）"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch5 グリーンファイナンス","q":"[LO 5.8] What is Property Assessed Clean Energy (PACE) financing?","h":"物件の税と一緒に返済する、省エネ・再エネの設備資金です。","c":["A US financing model in which the cost of energy-efficiency or renewable-energy upgrades is repaid through an assessment on the property tax bill.","A UK scheme in which a government agency pays homeowners a fixed price per kWh for the electricity that they export to the grid, for a period of ten years.","A European fund label under which retail funds must invest at least 80% in companies that are aligned with the EU Taxonomy.","A Japanese insurance product in which premiums fall automatically when a household switches to a renewable electricity tariff."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> PACEは、設備投資を物件の税に上乗せして返済する、米国の仕組み。<br><br><b>解説</b> PACEは、住宅・事業用の物件のエネルギー効率や再エネ設備の工事費を、地方自治体を通じて融資し、固定資産税に上乗せする形で長期に返済する米国の仕組み。債務が物件に紐づくため、所有者が変わっても引き継がれる。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 固定価格買取の保証、ファンドのラベル、保険料の割引は、PACEの説明ではない。<br><br>【出典】US Department of Energy, Property Assessed Clean Energy Programs, https://www.energy.gov/scep/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch5 グリーンファイナンス","q":"[LO 5.8] A bank offers a mortgage whose interest rate is cut in later years if the home's energy performance certificate (EPC) rating improves. How does this differ from a standard green mortgage?","h":"条件が、実績に連動して変わる点が特徴です。","c":["Its pricing is linked to a measured performance outcome, whereas a standard green mortgage prices the loan on the home meeting a specified efficiency standard at the outset.","Its pricing is linked to the bank's own share price, whereas a standard green mortgage prices the loan on the borrower's income at the outset, with an administration fee added by the bank for each year.","Its pricing is fixed at origination for the life of the loan, whereas a standard green mortgage must be refinanced each year at a new rate.","Its pricing is unrelated to energy performance, whereas a standard green mortgage prices the loan on the lender's own credit rating."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 実績に連動する金利は、サステナビリティ連動型。グリーン住宅ローンは基準を満たす物件で条件が決まる。<br><br><b>解説</b> 消費者向けでも、サステナビリティ・リンクの考え方がある。グリーン住宅ローンは、一定の省エネ基準を満たす物件に優遇金利を適用する。実績連動型は、EPCなどの成果が改善されると条件が改善される。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 銀行の株価、毎年の借換え、格付けは、商品の設計と無関係。<br><br>【出典】EeMAP, Technical Report on Building Performance Indicators that Impact Mortgage Credit Risk, https://worldgbc.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/EeMAP-Technical-Report-on-Building-Performance-Indicators-that-Impact-Mortgage-Credit-Risk_0.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch5 グリーンファイナンス","q":"[LO 5.9] Which of the following is an example of ESG integration in credit analysis?","h":"分析・予測に、ESG要因を組み込む手法です。","c":["Refusing to buy any bond issued by a company in the tobacco sector, whatever the credit quality of that issuer may be.","Voting against the re-election of directors at the annual meeting of an equity holding that has no climate strategy.","Allocating a fixed share of the portfolio to projects that deliver a measurable social outcome alongside a financial return.","Adjusting forecast cash flows or internal credit ratings of an issuer for its exposure to carbon costs and physical climate hazards."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> キャッシュフローや格付けの見直しに気候リスクを反映するのが、ESGインテグレーション。<br><br><b>解説</b> ESGインテグレーションは、財務分析にESG要因（炭素コスト、物理的ハザードなど）を体系的・明示的に組み込む。たとえば、キャッシュフロー予測、割引率、格付け、スプレッドの調整がある。業種の除外（ネガティブ・スクリーニング）、議決権行使（エンゲージメント）、インパクト投資は別の手法。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 除外は除外型、議決権行使は積極的な株主行動、成果の測定はインパクト投資。<br><br>【出典】一般的な手法の例示（PRIの該当資料はURLが失効しており本文は未確認）"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch5 グリーンファイナンス","q":"[LO 5.9] In Berg, Koelbel and Rigobon (2022), what was identified as the largest source of divergence among ESG ratings from different providers?","h":"評価機関ごとに、同じ属性の測り方が違うことが最大の要因でした。","c":["Weight divergence: raters assign different weights to the same attributes when aggregating.","Measurement divergence: raters measure the same attribute using different indicators.","Scope divergence: raters cover a different set of attributes when constructing the rating.","Date divergence: raters publish their ratings in different calendar years for the same issuer."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 最大の要因は、測定（measurement）の違い。<br><br><b>解説</b> 論文『Aggregate Confusion』は、ESG格付けの業者間の相関が0.38〜0.71（平均約0.54）と、信用格付けの約0.99より低いことを示し、乖離の要因を、対象範囲（scope）、測定（measurement）、ウェイト（weight）に分解した。測定が約56%、範囲が約38%、ウェイトが約6%と推計された。投資家は、格付けの背後にある指標を確認する必要がある。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> ウェイトの違いは寄与が小さく、公表年の違いは要因として挙げられていない。<br><br>【出典】Berg, Koelbel & Rigobon, Aggregate Confusion, Review of Finance, 2022, https://academic.oup.com/rof/article/26/6/1315/6590532"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch5 グリーンファイナンス","q":"[LO 5.9] Under the EU rules for Paris-aligned Benchmarks (PAB), which requirement applies?","h":"基準となるユニバースに比べた削減率と、毎年の削減率を満たす必要があります。","c":["At least 30% lower GHG intensity than the investable universe, and an average self-decarbonisation of at least 7% a year.","At least 50% lower GHG intensity than the investable universe, and an average self-decarbonisation of at least 3% a year.","At least 50% lower GHG intensity than the investable universe, and an average self-decarbonisation of at least 7% a year.","At least 30% lower GHG intensity than the investable universe, and an average self-decarbonisation of at least 5% a year."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> PABは、ユニバース比でGHG集約度を50%以上低くし、毎年7%の削減を続ける。<br><br><b>解説</b> EUのベンチマーク規則（2019/2089）と委任規則（2020/1818）は、パリ協定適合ベンチマーク（PAB）に、投資ユニバース比で50%低い集約度と、年平均7%の自己脱炭素化を求める。気候移行ベンチマーク（CTB）は30%低い集約度と年7%。PABには化石燃料関連などの除外基準もある。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> CTBは30%と7%で、PABの数字と異なる。他の組み合わせは規則にない。<br><br>【出典】Regulation (EU) 2019/2089, https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2019/2089/oj"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch5 グリーンファイナンス","q":"[LO 5.10] Which action is a recognised escalation step for an investor that engages a company on its climate strategy without success?","h":"対話で改善されない場合の次の手段を選びます。","c":["Transferring its shares to the company's largest creditor without a sale at market value.","Asking the stock exchange to remove the company from all indices for a fixed period.","Appointing the company's chief executive directly, since a minority holder can name executives.","Voting against the re-election of directors, or filing or supporting a shareholder resolution."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 対話が実らない場合、取締役への反対票や株主提案へ進む。<br><br><b>解説</b> エスカレーションの手段には、協働エンゲージメント、議決権行使（取締役選任への反対）、株主提案の提出・支持、公の発言、そして最後に売却（ダイベストメント）がある。少数株主が経営者を直接指名することはできない。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 債権者への株式移転、取引所による指数からの除外、経営者の指名は、株主の権利ではない。<br><br>【出典】Climate Action 100+, About, https://www.climateaction100.org/about/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch5 グリーンファイナンス","q":"[LO 5.10] Which statement about investor influence on company sustainability strategy is correct?","h":"エンゲージメントは株を持ち続けて働きかけ、売却は影響力を手放します。","c":["Engagement requires the investor to sell its shares first, whereas divestment is a way of exercising voting rights at a general meeting.","Engagement and divestment are identical because both transfer the shares to another investor, so neither has a different effect on influence, and neither affects the company's behaviour.","Engagement seeks to change a company's behaviour while the investor remains a shareholder, whereas divestment removes the investor's capital and also its voting influence.","Engagement works only for investors that hold more than 50% of the shares, whereas divestment works only for investors with less than 5%."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> エンゲージメントは保有を続けて変化を促し、売却は資本と議決権を手放す。<br><br><b>解説</b> エンゲージメントは、株主として対話・議決権行使を通じ、企業の行動変容を促す。売却（ダイベストメント）は、保有を手放すため影響力も失う。資本コストへの影響は限定的とする研究が多く、投資家は目的に応じて使い分ける。エンゲージメントに過半数の保有は不要。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 過半数の保有が必要、先に売却が必要、両者が同一、とする記述は誤り。<br><br>【出典】Climate Action 100+, About, https://www.climateaction100.org/about/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch5 グリーンファイナンス","q":"[LO 5.10] Which description of the May 2021 ExxonMobil annual meeting is correct?","h":"アクティビスト・ファンドが、取締役を選任させた事例です。","c":["Shareholders voted to remove all ExxonMobil directors, and a new board was installed with a mandate to close the oil business within five years.","Engine No. 1 won a majority of ExxonMobil's board seats, and the company then immediately adopted a binding net-zero target for 2030.","Engine No. 1 won three seats on Shell's board, citing the company's failure to report its refining margins to investors.","Engine No. 1, an activist fund backed by large institutional investors, won three seats on ExxonMobil's board, citing the lack of a climate strategy."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 2021年5月、エンジンNo.1が、気候戦略の不備を理由にエクソンモービルの取締役を3名獲得した。<br><br><b>解説</b> 2021年5月のエクソンモービルの株主総会で、アクティビスト・ファンドのEngine No. 1が、大手機関投資家の支持も得て、取締役12名のうち3名を獲得した。気候変動対応や資本配分の見直しを求めたもので、機関投資家の議決権行使が、気候戦略に影響を与えた事例として知られる。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 全取締役の解任、過半数の獲得、シェルの取締役会は、事実と異なる。<br><br>【出典】ExxonMobil, ExxonMobil updates preliminary results on election of directors, 2021-06-02, https://corporate.exxonmobil.com/news/news-releases/2021/0602_exxonmobil-updates-preliminary-results-on-election-of-directors ／ Skadden, What the Exxon Mobil Shareholder Votes Mean, 2021, https://www.skadden.com/insights/publications/2021/06/the-informed-board/what-the-exxon-mobil-shareholder-votes-mean"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch5 グリーンファイナンス","q":"[LO 5.11] Under the SFDR (Regulation (EU) 2019/2088), which set of conditions defines a 'sustainable investment'?","h":"環境・社会の目的への貢献、DNSH、グッド・ガバナンスの3つです。","c":["An investment in any company that has published a sustainability report and that has a lower carbon intensity than the average of its sector.","An investment in an economic activity that contributes to an environmental or social objective, does not significantly harm any such objective, and is made in investee companies following good governance practices.","An investment in an EU-listed company that has signed the UN Global Compact and that has not been fined by any authority in the last three years, and that is audited by an independent sustainability assurance provider every year.","An investment in a bond labelled as green or social and that is then held by the fund until its maturity date."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 持続可能な投資は、貢献・DNSH・グッド・ガバナンスの3条件。<br><br><b>解説</b> SFDR 2条17号は、持続可能な投資を、環境目的（資源効率、CO2排出、エネルギー等）や社会目的への貢献をもつ経済活動への投資で、他の目的に重大な害を与えず（DNSH）、投資先企業がグッド・ガバナンスの慣行に従っているものと定義する。EUタクソノミーより広く、運用会社に一定の裁量がある。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> サステナビリティ報告書の有無、GCへの署名や罰金のないこと、ラベル付き債券の保有は、定義の要件ではない。<br><br>【出典】Regulation (EU) 2019/2088 (SFDR), Article 2(17), https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2019/2088/oj"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch5 グリーンファイナンス","q":"[LO 5.11] How do the ICMA Green Bond Principles differ from the EU Taxonomy in defining 'green'?","h":"プロセス重視のガイドラインと、技術的な基準に基づく分類の違いです。","c":["The GBP are a binding EU law with technical screening criteria, whereas the EU Taxonomy is a voluntary guideline on use of proceeds.","The GBP list the specific threshold in gCO2/kWh for each activity, whereas the EU Taxonomy lets issuers choose any definition of green.","The GBP and the EU Taxonomy are identical documents issued by ICMA, so they define green in precisely the same way.","The GBP are voluntary process guidelines on use of proceeds, whereas the EU Taxonomy sets technical screening criteria for qualifying activities."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> GBPは使途のプロセスの自主ガイドライン、EUタクソノミーは技術的基準をもつ分類。<br><br><b>解説</b> GBPは、何がグリーンかの具体的な技術基準を定めず、発行体が使途の適格性を示す枠組みを提供する自主的ガイドライン。EUタクソノミーは、活動ごとの技術的スクリーニング基準を持つ法定の分類。両者は補完的に使われ、EU GBSは、GBPを基盤にタクソノミー適合を求める。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> GBPはEU法ではなく、閾値を列挙するのはタクソノミー側、同一の文書でもない。<br><br>【出典】ICMA, Green Bond Principles, https://www.icma-group.org/sustainable-finance/the-principles-guidelines-and-handbooks/green-bond-principles-gbp/ ／ European Commission, EU Taxonomy, https://finance.ec.europa.eu/sustainable-finance/tools-and-standards/eu-taxonomy-sustainable-activities_en"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch5 グリーンファイナンス","q":"[LO 5.11] How did China's 2021 edition of the Green Bond Endorsed Project Catalogue change its coverage compared with the earlier catalogue?","h":"国際的な基準との整合のため、化石燃料関連の事業を外しました。","c":["It removed projects involving fossil fuels, including 'clean coal', to align more closely with international standards.","It added clean coal projects for the first time, to align with the domestic policy of coal-fired power expansion.","It limited eligibility to state-owned issuers only, to align with the central government's industrial policy.","It abolished the catalogue entirely, to leave eligible projects to each issuer's own determination."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 2021年版は、クリーンコールを含む化石燃料関連を対象から外した。<br><br><b>解説</b> 中国人民銀行、国家発展改革委員会、証監会が2021年4月に公表した『グリーンボンド支援プロジェクト目録（2021年版）』は、従前の目録に含まれていたクリーンコールなどの化石燃料関連の事業を除外し、EUタクソノミーなど国際基準との整合を進めた。グリーンボンド市場の定義が、国によって異なる例。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> クリーンコールの追加、国有企業限定、目録の廃止は、事実と異なる。<br><br>【出典】IEEFA, Carbon neutral bonds: has China set the bar too low?, 2021, https://ieefa.org/resources/carbon-neutral-bonds-has-china-set-bar-too-low ／ Argus Media, China takes fossil fuel projects off green bond list, 2021, https://www.argusmedia.com/en/news-and-insights/latest-market-news/2208896-china-takes-fossil-fuel-projects-off-green-bond-list（PBOC/NDRC/CSRCの原文は未確認）"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch5 グリーンファイナンス","q":"[LO 5.12] What is the key difference in materiality between the EU's ESRS (under the CSRD) and the ISSB's IFRS S1 and S2?","h":"ESRSは二重のマテリアリティ、ISSBは財務マテリアリティが基本です。","c":["ESRS use financial materiality only, whereas the ISSB standards require disclosure of all impacts on society whether or not they affect enterprise value.","ESRS use double materiality (impact and financial), whereas the ISSB standards focus on information material to investors' assessment of enterprise value.","ESRS and the ISSB standards use identical materiality, and both require disclosure only of the impacts on the environment and society.","ESRS use no materiality filter at all, whereas the ISSB standards allow companies to skip any topic that they find inconvenient."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> ESRSは二重のマテリアリティ、ISSBは投資家向けの財務マテリアリティ。<br><br><b>解説</b> CSRD/ESRSは、インパクト・マテリアリティ（企業が社会・環境に与える影響）と財務マテリアリティ（企業の財務への影響）の「二重のマテリアリティ」を採用する。ISSBのIFRS S1/S2は、投資家の意思決定（企業価値の評価）に関連する情報を対象とする。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 両者は同一ではなく、ESRSが財務のみ、ISSBが全ての影響、という記述は逆。<br><br>【出典】EU, Directive (EU) 2022/2464 (CSRD), https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/dir/2022/2464/oj ／ IFRS Foundation, IFRS S1, https://www.ifrs.org/issued-standards/ifrs-sustainability-standards-navigator/ifrs-s1-general-requirements/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch5 グリーンファイナンス","q":"[LO 5.12] Which international baseline did the Sustainability Standards Board of Japan (SSBJ) build on when it issued its sustainability disclosure standards in March 2025?","h":"国際的なベースライン基準に整合させました。","c":["The European Sustainability Reporting Standards (ESRS).","The TCFD recommendations only, without any ISSB standard.","IFRS S1 and IFRS S2 issued by the ISSB.","The GRI Standards issued by the Global Sustainability Standards Board."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> SSBJ基準は、ISSBのIFRS S1・S2に整合している。<br><br><b>解説</b> SSBJ（サステナビリティ基準委員会）は、2025年3月にサステナビリティ開示基準（適用基準、一般基準、気候基準）を公表した。内容は、ISSBのIFRS S1・S2に整合している。国内での適用は、金融庁の計画で、時価総額の大きい企業から段階的に義務化される見通し。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> ESRS、TCFDのみ、GRIは、SSBJ基準が土台とした基準ではない。<br><br><b>日本との対応</b> 日本の有価証券報告書には、サステナビリティ情報の記載欄が2023年3月期から設けられている。SSBJ基準は、金融庁の方針で時価総額の大きい企業から段階的に適用される（時価総額3兆円以上の企業は2027年3月期から適用の予定）。<br><br>【出典】金融庁, サステナビリティ情報の開示, https://www.fsa.go.jp/policy/kaiji/sustainability-kaiji.html"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch5 グリーンファイナンス","q":"[LO 5.12] What happened to the TCFD after its 2023 status report?","h":"TCFDは解散し、ISSBが引き継ぎました。","c":["The TCFD was converted into a government regulator, and it took over the supervision of all listed companies' climate reports.","The TCFD recommendations were withdrawn as obsolete, and no standard-setter has monitored climate disclosure since 2024.","The TCFD was disbanded, and the IFRS Foundation took over monitoring of companies' climate-related disclosures from 2024.","The TCFD was merged into the NGFS, and it took over the supervision of banks' climate stress tests from 2024."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> TCFDは2023年に役目を終え、ISSBが2024年から進捗の監視を引き継いだ。<br><br><b>解説</b> FSBのTCFDは、2017年の提言から2023年の進捗報告を最後に解散し、IFRS財団（ISSB）が2024年から企業の気候関連開示の進捗の監視を引き継いだ。IFRS S2は、TCFDの提言を取り込んでいる。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 規制機関への転換、提言の廃止、NGFSへの統合は、事実と異なる。<br><br>【出典】IFRS Foundation, TCFD, https://www.ifrs.org/sustainability/tcfd/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch5 グリーンファイナンス","q":"[LO 5.13] What were the three objectives of the European Commission's 2018 Action Plan on Financing Sustainable Growth?","h":"資金の方向づけ、リスクの主流化、透明性と長期志向の3つです。","c":["Reorient capital flows towards sustainable investment, manage financial risks stemming from climate change and other issues, and foster transparency and long-termism.","Reduce EU emissions by 55% by 2030, ban fossil-fuel financing in the EU from 2025, and introduce a single carbon price for all sectors of the economy, administered by the ECB.","Create a single EU rating agency for sovereign debt, harmonise national tax rates on green funds, and replace the euro with a green currency.","Establish a mandatory EU-wide divestment from fossil fuels, require all banks to hold climate capital buffers, and set up an EU carbon bank."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 2018年のEU行動計画は、資金の方向づけ、リスク管理、透明性と長期志向の3つを目的とした。<br><br><b>解説</b> EUの『持続可能な成長への資金供給に関する行動計画』（2018年）は、(1)持続可能な投資への資本フローの方向づけ、(2)気候変動・資源枯渇・環境劣化・社会課題から生じる金融リスクの管理、(3)金融・経済活動における透明性と長期志向の促進、を目的とする。タクソノミー、SFDR、ベンチマーク規則、開示規則などに結実した。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 他の選択肢は、行動計画の目的ではない。<br><br>【出典】European Commission, Action Plan: Financing Sustainable Growth, 2018, https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:52018DC0097"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch5 グリーンファイナンス","q":"[LO 5.13] Which set of investment labels was introduced under the UK FCA's Sustainability Disclosure Requirements (SDR) regime?","h":"四つのラベルがあります。","c":["Light Green, Mid Green, Dark Green and Net Zero Aligned.","Article 6, Article 8, Article 9 and Article 10 funds.","Sustainability Focus, Sustainability Improvers, Sustainability Impact and Sustainability Mixed Goals.","Bronze, Silver, Gold and Platinum sustainability ratings awarded by a government agency to each fund every year."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> UKのSDRは、4つの投資ラベルを導入した。<br><br><b>解説</b> 英FCAのSDR（2023年11月に最終規則）は、投資商品のラベルとして、Sustainability Focus、Sustainability Improvers、Sustainability Impact、Sustainability Mixed Goalsの4種を導入した。2024年5月31日からは、反グリーンウォッシング規則が適用されている。EUのSFDRは、条項（Article 6/8/9）ベースの開示規則で、ラベルではない。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> Light Green等は、市場での通称。SFDR 8条・9条は開示上の分類。<br><br>【出典】FCA, Sustainability Disclosure Requirements (SDR) regime, https://www.fca.org.uk/firms/climate-change-and-sustainable-finance/sustainability-disclosure-requirements-sdr-regime"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch5 グリーンファイナンス","q":"[LO 5.13] Which statement about the EU Regulation on ESG rating activities (Regulation (EU) 2024/3005) is correct?","h":"ESG評価機関に、認可と監督を課す規則です。","c":["ESG rating providers operating in the EU are banned from rating banks, with the rules applying from July 2026.","ESG rating providers operating in the EU must be authorised and are supervised by ESMA, with the rules applying from July 2026.","ESG rating providers operating in the EU need no authorisation, and each national tax authority audits the ratings every year.","ESG rating providers operating in the EU must publish identical scores, and the European Commission sets those scores centrally."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> EU域内のESG評価機関は認可制で、ESMAが監督する。<br><br><b>解説</b> EUのESG評価規則（2024/3005）は、EU域内でESG評価を提供する事業者に、ESMAの認可と継続的な監督を求め、方法論・データ源の透明性、利益相反の防止を定める。2026年7月2日から適用される。ESG評価の乖離や不透明性への対応。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 銀行の評価の禁止、認可不要、スコアの統一といった規定はない。<br><br>【出典】Regulation (EU) 2024/3005, https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/3005/oj ／ ESMA, ESG Rating Providers, https://www.esma.europa.eu/esmas-activities/investors-and-issuers/esg-rating-providers"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch6 リスクの計測と管理","q":"[LO 6.1] Which of the following best describes a macroeconomic channel through which physical climate risk can affect financial institutions?","h":"マクロの経路は、GDPや生産性など経済全体への影響です。","c":["Heat stress and damaged capital stock reduce labour productivity and potential output, which lowers growth and weakens borrowers' incomes across a region.","A single borrower's warehouse is flooded, which lowers that one borrower's inventory value and weakens the cash flow of that company alone.","A bank's own head-office data centre loses power in a storm, which interrupts that bank's payment systems and raises its operating costs.","A single insurer's catastrophe claims exceed its reserves, which forces that insurer to raise premiums on its own policyholders only."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 猛暑や資本の損傷が生産性・潜在成長率を下げる経路が、マクロの経路。<br><br><b>解説</b> 物理リスクのマクロ経済的な経路には、労働生産性の低下、資本ストックの毀損、サプライチェーンの寸断、食料・エネルギー価格の変動、財政への負担などがある。これらは、地域・国全体の所得や雇用に影響し、金融機関の信用・市場リスクに波及する。個別の企業・金融機関の被害はミクロの経路。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 1社の倉庫の浸水、自行のデータセンターの停電、1社の保険金支払は、ミクロの経路。<br><br>【出典】BCBS, Climate-related risk drivers and their transmission channels, 2021, https://www.bis.org/bcbs/publ/d517.htm"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch6 リスクの計測と管理","q":"[LO 6.1] Which of the following is an example of a transition risk driver rather than a physical risk driver?","h":"政策・技術・市場の変化から生じるのが移行リスクです。","c":["More frequent flooding of a distribution centre that interrupts deliveries and damages its stock of goods.","Heat stress that lowers the productivity of outdoor workers on a construction site during the summer months.","Sea-level rise that reduces the market value of coastal homes pledged as collateral against mortgage loans.","The introduction of a carbon price that raises production costs and reduces the margins of a cement producer."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 炭素価格の導入は移行リスクのドライバー。<br><br><b>解説</b> 移行リスクは、低炭素経済への移行に伴う政策・規制、技術、市場・消費者の嗜好、評判の変化から生じる。炭素価格はコストと利益率に影響する政策ドライバー。浸水・熱ストレス・海面上昇は物理リスクのドライバー。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 他の3つは、気象・気候の物理的な現象による物理リスク。<br><br><b>日本との対応</b> 日本では、GX-ETS（2026年度から義務化）や化石燃料賦課金（2028年度から）の導入が、企業のコストに影響する移行リスクのドライバーになり得る。<br><br>【出典】TCFD, Recommendations of the Task Force on Climate-related Financial Disclosures, 2017, https://www.fsb-tcfd.org/recommendations/ ／ 経済産業省, GX-ETS（排出量取引制度）リーフレット, https://www.meti.go.jp/policy/energy_environment/global_warming/ets_leaflet.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch6 リスクの計測と管理","q":"[LO 6.1] How does the Basel Committee (2021) characterise climate-related financial risks in relation to traditional risk categories?","h":"新しいリスク種別ではなく、既存リスクのドライバーとして捉えます。","c":["As risk drivers that materialise through existing categories such as credit, market, liquidity and operational risk, rather than as a new standalone risk type.","As a new standalone risk type with its own Pillar 1 capital charge, which replaces credit, market, liquidity and operational risk, administered by the Basel Committee.","As a risk that arises only for insurers and has no relevance to the credit or market exposures of banks.","As a risk with no financial relevance before 2050, so that banks need not consider it in their current risk management."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 気候リスクは、既存のリスクのドライバーとして現れる。<br><br><b>解説</b> バーゼル委員会（2021年）の分析は、気候関連リスクを、信用・市場・流動性・オペレーショナルといった既存のリスク種別を通じて現れるリスクドライバーと位置づけた。新たなリスクカテゴリや第1の柱の資本賦課を定めたものではない。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 独立のリスク種別、保険会社のみ、2050年までは無関係、という記述は誤り。<br><br>【出典】BCBS, Climate-related risk drivers and their transmission channels, 2021, https://www.bis.org/bcbs/publ/d517.htm"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch6 リスクの計測と管理","q":"[LO 6.2] A coastal hotel owner has a bank loan secured on the hotel. A storm damages the property and closes the hotel for months. Which effect on the bank's expected credit loss is most direct?","h":"返済力の低下と担保価値の低下の両方が効きます。","c":["The probability of default rises because income stops, and the loss given default rises because the collateral has lost value.","The probability of default falls because the owner receives insurance advice, and the loss given default falls because the hotel is repaired.","The probability of default is unchanged because storms are random events, and the loss given default is unchanged because loans are fixed.","The exposure at default falls to zero because the bank's loan is cancelled automatically when the property is damaged."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 収入が止まりPDが上がり、担保が毀損しLGDも上がる。<br><br><b>解説</b> 物理リスクは信用リスクに、借り手の収入減によるPD（デフォルト確率）の上昇、担保価値の低下によるLGD（デフォルト時損失率）の上昇を通じて現れる。保険の付保状況によっては、損失が緩和される。EAD（デフォルト時エクスポージャー）が自動的にゼロになることはない。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> PDやLGDが下がる、または変わらない、EADがゼロになる、という記述は、被災の影響と合わない。<br><br>【出典】NGFS, Guide for Supervisors: Integrating climate-related and environmental risks into prudential supervision, 2020, https://www.ngfs.net/en/guide-supervisors-integrating-climate-related-and-environmental-risks-prudential-supervision"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch6 リスクの計測と管理","q":"[LO 6.2] Which scenario is a climate-related source of liquidity risk for a bank?","h":"預金流出や、コミットメントラインの引出しが急増する場面です。","c":["After a major disaster, many depositors in the affected region withdraw funds for repairs and borrowers draw heavily on committed credit lines.","After a mild winter, a utility reports lower heating revenue and its share price falls slightly relative to its own historical average.","After a new building code, an insurer raises the premiums for new homes and the insurer's loss ratio falls for the following year.","After a long period of stable weather, a bank's counterparties repay their loans early and the bank's interest income grows."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 被災地での預金引出しと、与信枠の引出しの急増は、流動性リスク。<br><br><b>解説</b> 気候関連の流動性リスクは、大規模災害後の預金流出・コミットメントラインの引出し増、あるいは移行の急激な進行に伴う市場の流動性低下・担保価値の下落によるマージンコールなどで生じる。収益の変動や保険料の改定は、流動性ではなく収益・引受の問題。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 他の3つは、収益・引受・金利収入の変動で、資金繰りの逼迫を示すものではない。<br><br>【出典】BCBS, Climate-related financial risks: a survey on current initiatives, 2020, https://www.bis.org/bcbs/publ/d502.htm"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch6 リスクの計測と管理","q":"[LO 6.2] Which action best addresses underwriting risk for a property insurer facing rising flood claims?","h":"将来の気候変動を織り込んだ価格・引受条件の見直しです。","c":["Keep pricing based only on the last decade of claims and expand coverage into the flood-prone zones to gain market share.","Raise the assumed discount rate on reserves, so that future claims look cheaper and the required premium falls.","Stop reinsuring flood exposures, so that the insurer retains all losses and need not model future hazard changes.","Update catastrophe models for forward-looking climate conditions and adjust pricing, deductibles and aggregate limits accordingly."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 将来の気候を織り込んで、価格・免責・限度額を見直す。<br><br><b>解説</b> 引受リスクは、気象災害の頻度・強度の変化により、保険料の設定と準備金が過去の実績に基づいて不足するリスク。対応は、カタストロフィ・モデルに将来の気候条件を反映し、価格、免責額、引受限度額、再保険の設計を見直すこと。過去の実績のみに依拠した価格設定は、リスクの過小評価を招く。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 過去10年のデータのみに依存、割引率の引上げ、再保険の停止は、リスクを高める方向。<br><br>【出典】EIOPA/ECB, Policy options to reduce the climate insurance protection gap (press release), 2023, https://www.eiopa.europa.eu/eiopa-and-ecb-call-increased-uptake-climate-catastrophe-insurance-2023-04-24_en"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch6 リスクの計測と管理","q":"[LO 6.3] Why can climate risk be a source of systemic risk, rather than only a collection of idiosyncratic risks?","h":"同時に多くの機関を直撃し、分散では消せないためです。","c":["Climate shocks always hit one institution at a time, are easily diversified away, and cannot spread to other institutions through markets, so that no regulator needs to monitor them.","Climate risk is systemic only because regulators require banks to report it, and it would be irrelevant to financial stability otherwise.","Physical and transition shocks can hit many institutions at once, are hard to diversify away, and can be amplified through fire sales and withdrawal of insurance.","Climate risk is systemic only for central banks, because commercial banks and insurers hold no exposures to physical or transition risk."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 同時に多くの機関に影響し、分散が効かず、市場を通じて増幅されるから。<br><br><b>解説</b> 気候リスクは、(1)同時多発的に多くの資産・機関を直撃し得る、(2)共通の曝露により分散が効きにくい、(3)資産価格の急落（ファイアセール）や保険の撤退を通じて増幅する、(4)長期・不確実性が大きく、非線形な変化があり得る、という点で金融システムの安定を損なうシステミックなリスクになり得る。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 1行ずつ起きて分散できる、規制のためだけのリスク、中央銀行のみのリスク、という記述は誤り。<br><br>【出典】ESRB, Positively green: Measuring climate change risks to financial stability, 2020, https://www.esrb.europa.eu/pub/pdf/reports/esrb.report200608_on_Positively_green_-_Measuring_climate_change_risks_to_financial_stability~d903a83690.en.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch6 リスクの計測と管理","q":"[LO 6.3] Which report by the European Systemic Risk Board's Advisory Scientific Committee (2016) is associated with the idea that an abrupt transition could threaten financial stability?","h":"『遅すぎ、突然すぎる』と題した2016年の報告書です。","c":["'Too late, too sudden: Transition to a low-carbon economy and systemic risk'.","'Breaking the tragedy of the horizon: Climate change and financial stability'.","'Task Force on Climate-related Financial Disclosures: Recommendations'.","'A call for action: Climate change as a source of financial risk'."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> ESRBの2016年報告書は、『Too late, too sudden』。<br><br><b>解説</b> ESRB諮問科学委員会（ASC）の2016年の報告書『Too late, too sudden』は、低炭素経済への移行が遅れ、その後に急激に進むと、資産の急な再評価を通じて金融システムの安定を損ない得るとした。『Tragedy of the horizon』はカーニーの2015年の講演、TCFD提言は開示の枠組み、『A call for action』はNGFSの2019年の報告書。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 他の3つは、講演、開示提言、NGFSの報告書で、ESRBの報告書ではない。<br><br>【出典】ESRB ASC, Too late, too sudden, 2016, https://www.esrb.europa.eu/pub/pdf/asc/Reports_ASC_6_1602.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch6 リスクの計測と管理","q":"[LO 6.3] In his 2015 speech 'Breaking the tragedy of the horizon', which three categories of climate-related financial risk did Mark Carney identify?","h":"物理リスク、賠償責任リスク、移行リスクの3つです。","c":["Credit risks, market risks and operational risks.","Physical risks, sovereign risks and reputational risks.","Physical risks, liability risks and transition risks.","Liability risks, liquidity risks and model risks."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> カーニーは、物理リスク・賠償責任リスク・移行リスクの3つを挙げた。<br><br><b>解説</b> 2015年9月のカーニー（当時の英国中央銀行総裁・FSB議長）の講演は、気候変動が金融安定に及ぼすリスクを、物理的リスク（保険損害など）、賠償責任リスク（損害を受けた側が責任を追及するもの）、移行リスク（低炭素経済への調整による資産の再評価）に整理した。のちのTCFDの分類（物理・移行）の源流になった。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 他の3つは、金融機関の伝統的リスク分類や別の組み合わせで、講演の分類ではない。<br><br>【出典】Bank of England, Breaking the tragedy of the horizon, 2015, https://www.bankofengland.co.uk/speech/2015/breaking-the-tragedy-of-the-horizon-climate-change-and-financial-stability"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch6 リスクの計測と管理","q":"[LO 6.4] A loan has EAD of USD 50 million. Under a climate stress scenario, the borrower's PD rises from 2% to 4% and LGD rises from 40% to 50%. What is the stressed expected loss (EL = PD x LGD x EAD)?","h":"EL＝PD×LGD×EADに、ストレス後の数値を代入します。","c":["USD 1.0 million.","USD 0.4 million.","USD 0.8 million.","USD 2.0 million."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 4%×50%×5,000万ドル＝100万ドル。<br><br><b>解説</b> EL＝PD×LGD×EAD。ストレス後は、0.04×0.50×50百万ドル＝1.0百万ドル。ベースラインは0.02×0.40×50＝0.4百万ドル。0.8はPD4%とLGDのベースライン40%の組合せ、2.0はLGDを掛け忘れたPD×EAD。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 0.4はストレス前、0.8はLGDを更新し忘れた値、2.0はLGDを掛けていない値。<br><br>【出典】BCBS, Basel Framework CRE, https://www.bis.org/basel_framework/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch6 リスクの計測と管理","q":"[LO 6.4] What does the Liquidity Coverage Ratio (LCR) measure, and what must the ratio be under Basel III?","h":"30日間のストレスに耐える高品質流動資産の比率で、100%以上です。","c":["Available stable funding divided by required stable funding over a one-year horizon, which must be at least 100%.","Common equity tier 1 capital divided by risk-weighted assets over a one-year horizon, which must be at least 4.5%.","Tier 1 capital divided by total leverage exposure over a 30-day stress period, which must be at least 3%.","Stock of high-quality liquid assets divided by total net cash outflows over a 30-day stress period, which must be at least 100%."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> LCRは、高品質流動資産÷30日間の純資金流出額で、100%以上。<br><br><b>解説</b> バーゼルIIIのLCR（流動性カバレッジ比率）は、30日間のストレス下で、高品質流動資産（HQLA）が純資金流出額を賄えるかを測り、100%以上が求められる。NSFR（安定調達比率）は1年の資金の調達と運用の期間の整合、CET1比率は資本の質、レバレッジ比率は非リスクベースの資本比率。気候リスクは、預金流出や担保価値の低下を通じて、LCRの分母・分子に影響し得る。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> NSFR、CET1比率、レバレッジ比率は、別の指標。<br><br>【出典】BCBS, Basel III: The Liquidity Coverage Ratio and liquidity risk monitoring tools, 2013, https://www.bis.org/publ/bcbs238.htm"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch6 リスクの計測と管理","q":"[LO 6.4] An insurer's combined ratio rises from 95% to 108% after a year of severe storm losses. What does this indicate?","h":"損害率と事業費率の合計が100%を超えると、引受は赤字です。","c":["Claims and expenses were below premiums earned, so the underwriting result was a profit before any investment income.","Claims and expenses exceeded premiums earned, so the underwriting result was a loss before any investment income.","Investment income exceeded claims, so the insurer's total result was a profit regardless of its underwriting performance.","The insurer's solvency ratio rose above 108%, so the insurer holds more capital than required by its supervisor."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> コンバインド・レシオが100%超は、引受損益が赤字。<br><br><b>解説</b> コンバインド・レシオ＝(支払保険金＋事業費)÷収入保険料。100%を超えると、投資収益を除いた引受損益は赤字。95%は黒字、108%は赤字で、大規模な風水災などで悪化する。気候変動で災害の頻度・強度が上がると、引受リスクの指標として注視される。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 100%未満は黒字。投資収益は別の項目で、ソルベンシー比率とは別の指標。<br><br>【出典】EIOPA/ECB, Policy options to reduce the climate insurance protection gap (press release), 2023, https://www.eiopa.europa.eu/eiopa-and-ecb-call-increased-uptake-climate-catastrophe-insurance-2023-04-24_en"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch6 リスクの計測と管理","q":"[LO 6.5] Which is an example of how climate change creates operational risk for a financial institution?","h":"自社の事業継続の混乱が、オペレーショナルリスクです。","c":["A borrower's profits fall after a carbon price is introduced, so the bank expects higher losses on a loan to it, while its own operations continue unaffected.","Depositors in a flooded region withdraw funds quickly, so the bank must raise liquid assets to meet outflows.","An extreme-weather event disables a data centre and branch network, interrupting payments and customer service for several days.","An insurer's claims rise after hailstorms, so the insurer's loss ratio exceeds the level assumed in pricing."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> データセンターや店舗の機能停止は、オペレーショナルリスク。<br><br><b>解説</b> オペレーショナルリスクは、不適切または機能しない内部プロセス・人・システム、外部事象による損失。極端な気象でデータセンター・店舗・従業員の出勤が妨げられ、事業継続が難しくなるのは、典型例。借り手の収益悪化は信用リスク、預金流出は流動性リスク、保険金の増加は引受リスク。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 他の3つは、それぞれ信用・流動性・引受のリスク。<br><br>【出典】BCBS, Principles for the effective management and supervision of climate-related financial risks, 2022, https://www.bis.org/bcbs/publ/d532.htm"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch6 リスクの計測と管理","q":"[LO 6.5] How can the withdrawal of insurance cover in high-risk areas affect a bank's mortgage portfolio?","h":"保険が付かなくなると、物件の価値と返済力が下がります。","c":["Uninsurable properties gain market value because competition for them rises, which strengthens collateral values and lowers the loss given default.","Uninsurable properties have no effect on mortgages because the bank is the sole beneficiary of the insurance and receives all payouts.","Uninsurable properties lose market value and become harder to sell, which weakens collateral values and raises the loss given default on mortgages.","Uninsurable properties are removed from the borrower's balance sheet, which lowers the bank's exposure at default to zero immediately."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 保険が撤退した地域の物件は価値が下がり、担保価値と回収が悪化する。<br><br><b>解説</b> 保険の保護ギャップは、リスクの高い地域で、保険料の高騰や引受の拒否として現れる。保険のない物件は買い手がつきにくく、価格が下がり、担保価値が下がるため、住宅ローンのLGDが上がる。信用リスクと保険（引受）リスクが、銀行の貸出資産を通じてつながる例。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 価値が上がる、影響がない、EADがゼロになる、という記述は誤り。<br><br>【出典】EIOPA/ECB, Policy options to reduce the climate insurance protection gap (press release), 2023, https://www.eiopa.europa.eu/eiopa-and-ecb-call-increased-uptake-climate-catastrophe-insurance-2023-04-24_en"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch6 リスクの計測と管理","q":"[LO 6.5] What is meant by a 'brown discount' on a property in a bank's mortgage book?","h":"省エネ性能が低い物件が、価格や担保評価で割り引かれることです。","c":["Properties with poor energy performance may sell at a discount, because buyers anticipate retrofit costs and tighter efficiency standards.","Properties located near forests are sold at a discount, because the buyers fear that wildfires would damage the surrounding natural vegetation.","Properties with brown roofs are sold at a discount, because the colour of the roof absorbs more heat than that of lighter roofs.","Properties owned by brown-field developers are sold at a discount, because the developers have made no use of previously developed land."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 省エネ性能の低い物件が割り引かれる現象が、ブラウン・ディスカウント。<br><br><b>解説</b> エネルギー性能の低い物件は、改修コスト、将来の最低省エネ基準（EUのEPBDなど）、光熱費の高さを織り込んで、価格が割り引かれる傾向がある（反対にグリーン・プレミアム）。担保価値の低下や借り手のコスト増を通じて、住宅ローンの信用リスクに影響する。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 森林近接、屋根の色、ブラウンフィールド開発者は、ブラウン・ディスカウントの意味ではない。<br><br>【出典】EeMAP, Technical Report on Building Performance Indicators that Impact Mortgage Credit Risk, https://worldgbc.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/EeMAP-Technical-Report-on-Building-Performance-Indicators-that-Impact-Mortgage-Credit-Risk_0.pdf ／ Bank of England, The greening of lending: mortgage pricing of energy transition risk, 2023, https://www.bankofengland.co.uk/-/media/boe/files/working-paper/2023/the-greening-of-lending-mortgage-pricing-of-energy-transition-risk.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch6 リスクの計測と管理","q":"[LO 6.6] A severe drought cuts crop yields across several continents, food prices rise, inflation increases and central banks raise interest rates. Through which channel does this most directly affect financial institutions?","h":"供給ショックが物価と金利を通じて、市場リスクに波及します。","c":["Microeconomic transmission: a single borrower's factory is damaged, which reduces that firm's output and its capacity to service its loan.","Operational transmission: the bank's own branches are closed by flooding, which interrupts its payment services for several days.","Reputational transmission: customers learn that the bank has financed fossil fuels, which causes them to transfer deposits to other banks.","Macroeconomic transmission: higher inflation and interest rates reduce the market value of fixed-income holdings and raise funding costs."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 干ばつ→食料価格→インフレ→利上げは、マクロの経路で市場リスクに波及する。<br><br><b>解説</b> 気候の物理的ショックは、供給サイドのショック（農業生産の減少）を通じて物価・金利・為替といったマクロ変数を動かし、債券価格や資金調達コストなどの市場リスクに影響する。ミクロ経路は個々の企業・家計への影響で、オペレーショナル・評判の経路は別のもの。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 他の3つは、個別借り手、自社の拠点、評判の経路。<br><br>【出典】BCBS, Climate-related risk drivers and their transmission channels, 2021, https://www.bis.org/bcbs/publ/d517.htm"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch6 リスクの計測と管理","q":"[LO 6.6] Which description best illustrates an amplification (feedback) mechanism in the financial system after a disorderly transition?","h":"資産価格の下落が担保と売りを呼び、さらに下落する連鎖です。","c":["Rising prices of carbon-intensive assets attract new buyers, which further raises their prices and reduces losses for the other holders.","Falling prices of carbon-intensive assets trigger margin calls and forced sales, which push prices lower still and spread losses to other holders.","A single bank writes off a loan, and this affects only that bank because all other institutions hold fully separate and uncorrelated assets.","A regulator publishes a stress-test report, and this has no effect on any asset price because investors do not use published information."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 価格下落→追証・強制売却→さらなる下落という増幅メカニズム。<br><br><b>解説</b> 急激で無秩序な移行では、炭素集約型資産の価格が急落し、担保価値の低下、追加証拠金の請求、強制的な売却が価格をさらに下げる悪循環（ファイアセール）や、共通の保有を通じた損失の伝播が起こり得る。これがシステミックリスクの増幅メカニズムで、金融安定のリスクにつながる。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 価格上昇や影響の遮断、情報への無反応は、増幅メカニズムとは逆の記述。<br><br>【出典】ESRB, Positively green: Measuring climate change risks to financial stability, 2020, https://www.esrb.europa.eu/pub/pdf/reports/esrb.report200608_on_Positively_green_-_Measuring_climate_change_risks_to_financial_stability~d903a83690.en.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch6 リスクの計測と管理","q":"[LO 6.6] How can physical climate shocks to public finances transmit to banks (the sovereign-bank nexus)?","h":"政府の財政負担が国債価格に波及し、国債を持つ銀行に影響します。","c":["Disaster costs raise government revenue and lower sovereign spreads, which raises the value of government bonds held by banks and strengthens their capital.","Disaster costs reduce fiscal capacity and raise sovereign spreads, which lowers the value of government bonds held by banks and weakens their capital.","Disaster costs are paid by banks directly to the government, which removes all government bonds from banks' balance sheets at once.","Disaster costs have no effect on the government's finances, since climate shocks are borne exclusively by private households."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 災害の財政負担が国債のスプレッドを広げ、保有する銀行の資本に響く。<br><br><b>解説</b>  物理的な気候ショックは、災害対応の歳出増や税収減で政府の財政余力を低下させ、ソブリン・スプレッドを拡大し得る。国債を多く保有する銀行は、評価損やリスクウェイトの上昇を通じて影響を受ける（ソブリンと銀行のつながり、sovereign-bank nexus）。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 歳入の増加、銀行による直接の負担、政府への影響がないという記述は誤り。<br><br>【出典】ECB, Working Paper No 3135 (climate risk and sovereign yields), 2025, https://www.ecb.europa.eu//pub/pdf/scpwps/ecb.wp3135~024090a8b9.en.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch6 リスクの計測と管理","q":"[LO 6.7] In MSCI's Climate Value-at-Risk framework, which components make up the overall measure?","h":"政策リスク、技術機会、物理リスクの3つで構成されます。","c":["Credit risk, market risk and operational risk.","Liquidity risk, underwriting risk and reputational risk, as set out in the TCFD recommendations.","Scope 1, Scope 2 and Scope 3 emissions of the firm.","Policy risk, technology opportunities and physical risk (extreme and chronic)."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> Climate VaRは、政策リスク、技術機会、物理リスクの3要素。<br><br><b>解説</b> MSCIのClimate VaRは、移行リスク（政策リスク）、移行の機会（技術の機会）、物理リスク（極端な気象と慢性的な変化）の3つのコンポーネントからなり、将来の費用と収益を現在価値で表す。信用・市場・オペレーショナルは伝統的なリスク分類、スコープ1〜3は排出量の区分。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 他の3つの組み合わせは、Climate VaRのコンポーネントではない。<br><br>【出典】MSCI, ClimateVaR Introduction, 2020, https://www.msci.com/documents/1296102/16985724/MSCI-ClimateVaR-Introduction-Feb2020.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch6 リスクの計測と管理","q":"[LO 6.7] How does Climate VaR differ from conventional market VaR?","h":"将来を見据えた長期のシナリオ型か、過去に基づく短期の統計型かです。","c":["Climate VaR is backward-looking and based on historical prices over one day, whereas conventional VaR is scenario-based over many decades.","Climate VaR measures only the probability of a firm's default, whereas conventional VaR measures only the firm's emissions per unit of revenue, and neither is expressed in currency units.","Climate VaR is forward-looking and scenario-based over long horizons, whereas conventional VaR is a short-horizon statistical estimate based on historical price volatility.","Climate VaR is identical to conventional VaR but is reported in tonnes of CO2 equivalent instead of currency units."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> Climate VaRは将来志向の長期シナリオ型、市場VaRは過去に基づく短期の統計型。<br><br><b>解説</b> 従来のVaRは、過去の価格変動に基づいて、1〜10日程度の保有期間の損失を一定の信頼水準で推計する。Climate VaRは、気候シナリオに基づく将来の費用・収益を、長期（15年など）の現在価値で表す。確率的な損失ではなく、シナリオ条件付きの価値変化。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 過去の価格・1日の推計、デフォルト確率のみ、トン表示という記述は、Climate VaRの説明ではない。<br><br>【出典】MSCI, ClimateVaR Introduction, 2020, https://www.msci.com/documents/1296102/16985724/MSCI-ClimateVaR-Introduction-Feb2020.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch6 リスクの計測と管理","q":"[LO 6.7] Which is a recognised limitation of Climate VaR results?","h":"結果が、シナリオ・損害関数・割引率の選択に大きく左右されます。","c":["Results are identical across all providers because the method, data and assumptions are mandated by one international regulation.","Results show the exact loss that will occur in the next ten trading days with a probability of 99 percent.","Results cover only direct emissions of the issuer and ignore all policy, technology and physical risk drivers of value.","Results depend heavily on the choice of scenario, damage function and discount rate, so outputs from different providers may not be comparable."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 結果は、シナリオ・損害関数・割引率の仮定に左右され、比較しにくい。<br><br><b>解説</b> Climate VaRは、シナリオの選択、物理リスクの損害関数、割引率、政策の想定などに結果が大きく左右され、提供者間の比較が難しい。また、将来のシナリオ条件下の価値の変化であり、確率で表した損失ではない。使うときは、前提を確認する。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 統一規制による同一の結果、10営業日・99%の損失、直接排出のみ、という記述は誤り。<br><br>【出典】NGFS, Guide to climate scenario analysis for central banks and supervisors, https://www.ngfs.net/en/publications-and-statistics/publications/guide-climate-scenario-analysis-central-banks-and-supervisors"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch6 リスクの計測と管理","q":"[LO 6.8] Which data best supports a company-level physical risk assessment of a manufacturer's plants?","h":"施設の位置情報と、ハザードマップの重ね合わせが基本です。","c":["The company's total revenue for the last year divided by the number of its employees across all countries.","The company's share price for the last ten days compared with an equity index of its sector.","Facility geolocation data overlaid on hazard maps for flooding, heat and storms, drawn from climate models.","The name of the company's auditor and the date of the last annual general meeting of shareholders."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 施設の位置情報とハザードマップを重ねるのが、物理リスク評価の基本。<br><br><b>解説</b> 企業レベルの物理リスクは、工場・倉庫・サプライヤーなどの資産の位置情報と、洪水・高温・暴風・干ばつなどのハザードデータ（気候モデル由来）を重ね合わせて評価する。さらに、事業の依存度、保険の付保状況などを考慮する。売上高/従業員、株価、監査人は、物理リスクの指標ではない。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 財務比率や株価、監査人の情報は、ハザードへの曝露を示すデータではない。<br><br>【出典】TCFD, Recommendations (fsb-tcfd.org), https://www.fsb-tcfd.org/recommendations/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch6 リスクの計測と管理","q":"[LO 6.8] What does the Transition Pathway Initiative (TPI) assess?","h":"経営の質と、炭素パフォーマンスの二つの視点で企業を評価します。","c":["The credit ratings of sovereign issuers, which are then compared with those of their central banks.","The quality of companies' management of climate risks (rated in levels) and their carbon performance compared with Paris-aligned benchmarks.","The physical hazard exposure of individual buildings, which is then used to price property insurance.","The share price volatility of listed companies, which is then used to set the margin on equity derivatives, and by regulators to set the capital buffers."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> TPIは、気候リスクへの経営の質と、炭素パフォーマンスを評価する。<br><br><b>解説</b> TPI（Transition Pathway Initiative）は、ロンドン大学グランサム研究所などが運営する、企業の気候移行への備えを評価する枠組みで、経営の質（段階評価）と、将来の炭素パフォーマンス（パリ協定整合のベンチマークとの比較）の2軸で評価する。無償で利用でき、投資家のエンゲージメントに使われる。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 他の3つは、ソブリン格付け、建物の物理リスク、株価変動の分析で、TPIの内容ではない。<br><br>【出典】Transition Pathway Initiative, Methodology and Indicators Report, 2017, https://www.transitionpathwayinitiative.org/publications/uploads/2017-methodology-and-indicators-report.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch6 リスクの計測と管理","q":"[LO 6.8] Which is a recognised data challenge in measuring a company's transition risk?","h":"推計値と実測値の差や、データの欠落が課題です。","c":["All companies report audited Scope 3 emissions using one mandatory method, so there are no data gaps for any issuer.","Emission data are always available in real time at the asset level, so there is no need to estimate any value.","Third-party modelled emissions can differ materially from company-reported figures, and coverage is thin for private and smaller firms.","Estimated and reported emissions are always identical, because vendors only copy the figures published by the company, with no estimation by the vendor."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 推計値と企業の報告値には差があり、未上場・中小企業のデータは薄い。<br><br><b>解説</b> 移行リスクの測定では、企業の開示する排出量に空白や不整合があり、データ提供会社の推計値が報告値と大きく異なる場合がある。スコープ3の算定は特に不確実で、未上場企業・中小企業のカバレッジが小さい。データの出典（報告か推計か）を区別して使う必要がある。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 全社の監査済みスコープ3、リアルタイムの資産別データ、推計と報告の一致は、現実と合わない。<br><br>【出典】PCAF, The Global GHG Accounting and Reporting Standard, https://carbonaccountingfinancials.com/standard"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch6 リスクの計測と管理","q":"[LO 6.9] What does an implied temperature rise (ITR) metric for a portfolio estimate?","h":"ポートフォリオの排出や目標が、世界全体に当てはまった場合の気温上昇です。","c":["The temperature of the buildings owned by the companies in the portfolio, measured in degrees Celsius at the present time.","The warming that would result if the whole economy had the same emissions trajectory or ambition as the companies in the portfolio.","The rise in the portfolio's market value if global temperatures were to increase by one degree over the next year.","The number of days per year on which the portfolio's holdings are exposed to a temperature above 35 degrees."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> ITRは、ポートフォリオの軌道が世界全体に適用された場合の気温上昇を推計する。<br><br><b>解説</b> ITR（想定気温上昇）は、投資先企業の排出量や目標を、カーボンバジェットと比較して、「世界全体がこのポートフォリオと同じ排出の道筋をたどったら何℃上がるか」を示す。将来志向だが、方法論・データ・仮定により結果が大きく異なる。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 建物の温度、時価の上昇、高温日数は、ITRの定義ではない。<br><br>【出典】TCFD, Measuring Portfolio Alignment: Technical Supplement, 2021（転載版）, https://skbi.smu.edu.sg/sites/skbi.smu.edu.sg/files/cgs/library/Measuring%20Portfolio%20Alignment%20Technical%20Supplement.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch6 リスクの計測と管理","q":"[LO 6.9] Which description of PACTA (Paris Agreement Capital Transition Assessment) is correct?","h":"生産計画をシナリオと比べて、整合度を見る手法です。","c":["It measures only the past Scope 1 emissions of each company and divides them by revenue for the previous year.","It compares the forward-looking production plans of companies in a portfolio with climate scenario pathways for key sectors.","It is an insurance product that pays out when a portfolio's market value falls below a defined floor after a flood.","It is a national law that obliges banks to reduce their lending to fossil-fuel sectors by a fixed percentage each year."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> PACTAは、企業の生産計画を気候シナリオの経路と比較する。<br><br><b>解説</b> PACTA（Paris Agreement Capital Transition Assessment）は、発電、石油・ガス、石炭、自動車、セメント、鉄鋼などの重要セクターの企業の将来の生産計画を、気候シナリオの経路と比較して、ポートフォリオの整合度を評価するオープンソースの手法。排出量の過去実績だけを見る指標より、将来志向。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 過去のスコープ1のみ、保険商品、法律、という記述はPACTAの内容ではない。<br><br>【出典】RMI, PACTA for Investors Methodology Document V1.0, 2022, https://pacta.rmi.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/12/PACTA-for-Investors-Methodology-Document_V1.0.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch6 リスクの計測と管理","q":"[LO 6.9] A bank lends USD 20 million to a company with EVIC of USD 400 million and annual Scope 1 and 2 emissions of 100,000 tCO2e. Using the PCAF approach for listed companies, what are the financed emissions attributable to the loan?","h":"帰属割合は、融資残高÷EVICです。","c":["2,000 tCO2e.","20,000 tCO2e.","5,000 tCO2e.","500 tCO2e."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 帰属割合は20÷400＝5%で、10万×5%＝5,000tCO2e。<br><br><b>解説</b> PCAFでは、上場企業向け融資の帰属割合を、融資残高÷EVIC（企業価値、現金を含む）で求め、企業の排出量に掛ける。20/400＝5%、100,000×5%＝5,000 tCO2e。2,000は2%、20,000は20%、500は0.5%に相当する値で、いずれも帰属割合の計算が合わない。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 他の値は、帰属割合を誤った場合の値。<br><br>【出典】PCAF, The Global GHG Accounting and Reporting Standard for the Financial Industry, https://carbonaccountingfinancials.com/standard"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch6 リスクの計測と管理","q":"[LO 6.10] In the three lines model applied to climate risk, which allocation of responsibilities is correct?","h":"第1線が管理し、第2線が監視・牽制し、第3線が独立に保証します。","c":["The first line gives independent assurance on climate risk, the second line owns and manages it, and internal audit sets the risk appetite.","The first line only reports to regulators, the second line trades the exposures, and internal audit takes the exposures onto its own books.","The first line owns and manages climate risk, the second line oversees and challenges it independently, and internal audit provides independent assurance.","The board owns and manages all climate risk directly, and the three lines are replaced by one central climate committee."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 第1線が管理、第2線が独立に監視・牽制、第3線の内部監査が保証。<br><br><b>解説</b> 3線モデルでは、第1線（事業部門）がリスクを所有・管理し、第2線（リスク管理・コンプライアンス）が独立に監視・牽制し、第3線（内部監査）が独立の保証を与える。気候リスクも既存のERMの中で、この役割分担に沿って管理する。取締役会は、リスク選好を設定し、監督する。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 役割を入れ替えた記述、内部監査が保有する、取締役会が全てを管理する、は誤り。<br><br>【出典】IIA, The IIA's Three Lines Model, 2020, https://www.theiia.org/globalassets/documents/resources/the-iias-three-lines-model-an-update-of-the-three-lines-of-defense-july-2020/three-lines-model-updated-english.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch6 リスクの計測と管理","q":"[LO 6.10] Which is a way to embed climate risk into a bank's risk appetite framework?","h":"リスク選好に、気候の指標と上限・トリガーを設定します。","c":["Keep climate risk out of the risk appetite statement, and review it only when a physical event has already caused a loss.","Set a single net profit target for the bank, and treat climate risk as a matter for the marketing department.","Set limits or triggers on exposure to high-emitting sectors or on financed-emission intensity, and monitor them in regular risk reports.","Delegate all climate decisions to an external vendor, and accept the vendor's score without further review."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> リスク選好に、セクター別の上限や排出強度のトリガーを設定し、定期的に監視する。<br><br><b>解説</b> 気候リスクをERMに統合するには、リスク選好の記述（RAS）に、高排出セクターへのエクスポージャーの上限、ファイナンスド・エミッションの強度、シナリオ分析の結果などの指標とトリガーを設定し、リスクレポートで定期的に監視する。被害発生後の対応や、外部の評価の丸受けは、リスク管理とはいえない。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> リスク選好に含めない、利益目標のみ、外部ベンダーへの全面的な委任は、適切な統合ではない。<br><br>【出典】BCBS, Principles for the effective management and supervision of climate-related financial risks, 2022, https://www.bis.org/bcbs/publ/d532.htm"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch6 リスクの計測と管理","q":"[LO 6.10] How should a typical 3-to-5-year planning horizon be adapted to manage climate risk in ERM?","h":"短期の計画を、長期のシナリオ分析で補います。","c":["Shorten the planning horizon to three months, because climate impacts are fully visible only in quarterly financial statements.","Supplement the planning horizon with longer-horizon scenario analysis and stress tests, because many climate impacts materialise over decades.","Ignore horizons beyond the current financial year, because uncertainty makes any long-term analysis meaningless for decisions.","Use only the last twenty years of historical data, because the future climate will be the same as the average of the past."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 数年の計画期間を、数十年スケールのシナリオ分析で補う。<br><br><b>解説</b> 気候リスクの多くは数十年にわたり顕在化し、過去のデータだけでは将来を捉えにくい。そのため、通常の3〜5年の計画期間に加え、2030年・2050年などの長期のシナリオ分析・ストレステストで補う。ただし、長期の分析は不確実性が大きく、前提を示して使う。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 3か月への短縮、当年度のみ、過去20年のみ、という方法は、長期リスクを捉えられない。<br><br>【出典】TCFD, Guidance on Scenario Analysis for Non-Financial Companies, 2020, https://www.fsb.org/wp-content/uploads/P291020-3.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch6 リスクの計測と管理","q":"[LO 6.11] What is an advantage and a limitation of Weighted Average Carbon Intensity (WACI) as a portfolio metric?","h":"投資家の持分に依存せずに計算できる反面、少数の高排出企業に敏感です。","c":["It reflects the investor's ownership share of each company's absolute emissions, but it cannot be calculated for any asset class other than listed equity.","It is unaffected by changes in revenue and by outliers, but it requires the investor to know every company's enterprise value including cash.","It captures forward-looking transition plans of each company, but it requires the investor to hold at least 50 percent of the shares.","It does not depend on the investor's ownership share of each company and is simple to calculate, but it can be dominated by a few high-intensity holdings."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> WACIは持分不要で簡便だが、高排出の少数銘柄に左右される。<br><br><b>解説</b> WACI（加重平均炭素集約度）は、保有ウェイトで企業の炭素集約度（排出量÷売上高）を加重平均する。投資家の持分（EVIC）が不要で、他の資産クラスにも使える利点がある。一方、少数の高集約度の銘柄に左右されやすく、売上高の変動の影響を受け、後ろ向きの指標である。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 持分を反映するのは総排出量・フットプリント。WACIは将来計画を捉えない。<br><br>【出典】TCFD, Implementing the Recommendations of the TCFD, 2021, https://assets.bbhub.io/company/sites/60/2021/07/2021-TCFD-Implementing_Guidance.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch6 リスクの計測と管理","q":"[LO 6.11] Why can a portfolio's carbon footprint (tCO2e per USD million invested) change even when the physical emissions of its holdings do not?","h":"分母が株価・時価に連動するためです。","c":["Because the denominator and attribution use market-based values such as EVIC, so share price movements change the metric without changing the real emissions.","Because the metric is calculated only once in a lifetime, so any later change is a rounding difference of the original figure.","Because the metric uses the investor's tax rate, so a change in the tax law alters the number that is reported.","Because the metric ignores the investor's holdings, so it moves only with changes in the emissions of the issuers' competitors, measured over the same calendar year."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 時価（EVIC）に連動するため、株価で数字が動く。<br><br><b>解説</b> カーボン・フットプリントは、投資家の持分（保有額÷EVIC）で帰属させた排出量を、ポートフォリオの価値で割る。EVICや時価総額は株価で変動するため、実際の排出が変わらなくても、数値が動く。このノイズが、時系列比較での留意点。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 生涯に一度の計算、税率、他社の排出、という記述は誤り。<br><br>【出典】TCFD, Implementing the Recommendations of the TCFD, 2021, https://assets.bbhub.io/company/sites/60/2021/07/2021-TCFD-Implementing_Guidance.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch6 リスクの計測と管理","q":"[LO 6.11] Which limitation applies to all of the TCFD-recommended carbon footprint and exposure metrics?","h":"後ろ向きで、スコープ1・2が中心です。","c":["They are forward-looking and fully based on Scope 3 emissions, so they cannot be calculated for any past period, and are updated daily by each company in real time.","They are expressed only in currency units, so they cannot be compared with any emissions-based target.","They are backward-looking and mostly based on Scope 1 and 2 emissions, so they do not capture forward-looking transition risk or Scope 3.","They are available only for private companies, so listed issuers cannot be assessed by them."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> いずれも後ろ向きで、スコープ1・2が中心。将来の移行リスクやスコープ3は捉えにくい。<br><br><b>解説</b> TCFDが挙げる炭素関連の指標（総炭素排出量、カーボン・フットプリント、炭素集約度、WACI）は、過去の排出実績に基づく後ろ向きの指標で、多くはスコープ1・2が中心。将来の移行計画、技術の転換、スコープ3の影響を捉えにくい。TCFDは、これらを出発点とし、将来志向の指標で補うことを推奨した。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 将来志向、通貨単位、非上場のみ、という記述は誤り。<br><br>【出典】TCFD, Implementing the Recommendations of the TCFD, 2021, https://assets.bbhub.io/company/sites/60/2021/07/2021-TCFD-Implementing_Guidance.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch6 リスクの計測と管理","q":"[LO 6.12] An investor holds USD 5 million of Company X (EVIC USD 250 million, Scope 1+2 emissions 120,000 tCO2e) and USD 15 million of Company Y (EVIC USD 300 million, Scope 1+2 emissions 40,000 tCO2e). What are the total carbon emissions attributable to these two holdings?","h":"保有額÷EVICで帰属割合を出し、排出量に掛けて足します。","c":["160,000 tCO2e.","2,200 tCO2e.","8,800 tCO2e.","4,400 tCO2e."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> X：2%×12万＝2,400、Y：5%×4万＝2,000、合計4,400tCO2e。<br><br><b>解説</b> 総炭素排出量は、Σ(保有額÷EVIC×排出量)。X：5÷250＝2%、120,000×2%＝2,400。Y：15÷300＝5%、40,000×5%＝2,000。合計4,400 tCO2e。160,000は帰属割合を掛けない排出量の単純合計、2,200は半分、8,800は2倍の値。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 他の値は、帰属割合の計算を誤った場合の値。<br><br>【出典】TCFD, Implementing the Recommendations of the TCFD, 2021, https://assets.bbhub.io/company/sites/60/2021/07/2021-TCFD-Implementing_Guidance.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch6 リスクの計測と管理","q":"[LO 6.12] A portfolio has three holdings with weights of 50%, 30% and 20%. Their carbon intensities (Scope 1+2 emissions per USD million of revenue) are 500, 300 and 50 tCO2e/USD million respectively. What is the portfolio's WACI?","h":"保有ウェイトで加重平均します。","c":["283 tCO2e/USD million.","350 tCO2e/USD million.","850 tCO2e/USD million.","215 tCO2e/USD million."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 0.5×500＋0.3×300＋0.2×50＝350。<br><br><b>解説</b> WACI＝Σ(ウェイト×炭素集約度)＝0.5×500＋0.3×300＋0.2×50＝250＋90＋10＝350。283は単純平均、850は単なる合計、215はウェイトの順番を逆にした場合の値。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 単純平均は保有ウェイトを無視、合計は平均になっていない、215はウェイトの割当ての誤り。<br><br>【出典】TCFD, Implementing the Recommendations of the TCFD, 2021, https://assets.bbhub.io/company/sites/60/2021/07/2021-TCFD-Implementing_Guidance.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch6 リスクの計測と管理","q":"[LO 6.12] A USD 40 million portfolio holds USD 4 million of Company P (EVIC USD 200 million, emissions 50,000 tCO2e), USD 6 million of Company Q (EVIC USD 120 million, emissions 36,000 tCO2e), and other holdings whose attributable emissions total 1,200 tCO2e. What is the portfolio's carbon footprint?","h":"総排出量を、ポートフォリオの価値（100万ドル）で割ります。","c":["100 tCO2e per USD million invested.","4,000 tCO2e per USD million invested.","40 tCO2e per USD million invested.","400 tCO2e per USD million invested."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 帰属排出量は1,000＋1,800＋1,200＝4,000、÷40百万ドル＝100。<br><br><b>解説</b> P：4÷200＝2%、50,000×2%＝1,000。Q：6÷120＝5%、36,000×5%＝1,800。その他1,200。合計4,000 tCO2e。カーボン・フットプリント＝4,000÷40＝100 tCO2e/百万ドル。4,000は総排出量そのもの、40と400は割る数字の誤り。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 4,000は割り算の忘れ、40・400は桁や分母の誤り。<br><br>【出典】TCFD, Implementing the Recommendations of the TCFD, 2021, https://assets.bbhub.io/company/sites/60/2021/07/2021-TCFD-Implementing_Guidance.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch7 気候モデルとシナリオ分析","q":"[LO 7.1] Which statement about climate scenarios is correct?","h":"シナリオは予測ではなく、もっともらしい将来像です。","c":["Scenarios are precise forecasts of the single most likely future, and each one is assigned a probability that sums to 100%.","Scenarios are internally consistent, plausible pathways rather than forecasts, and they are generally not assigned probabilities.","Scenarios are legal targets that every company must meet, and a failure to meet them triggers a penalty by the regulator.","Scenarios are historical records of past weather, and they cannot be used to explore future policy or technology changes."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> シナリオは、整合的でもっともらしい将来像で、予測ではなく確率も付けない。<br><br><b>解説</b> 気候シナリオは、政策・技術・社会経済の仮定に基づく、内的に整合した「もっともらしい」将来の経路。予測（forecast）とは異なり、確率は通常付けない。不確実な将来に対する戦略やリスクの頑健性を検討するための道具。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 単一の最も可能性の高い予測、法的な目標、過去の気象記録、という記述は誤り。<br><br>【出典】TCFD, Technical Supplement: The Use of Scenario Analysis in Disclosure of Climate-Related Risks and Opportunities, 2017, https://fsb.org/uploads/Technical-Supplement-1.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch7 気候モデルとシナリオ分析","q":"[LO 7.1] Which set lists core components of a climate scenario analysis exercise?","h":"前提とナラティブ、定量的な経路、時間軸、事業への落とし込みです。","c":["A narrative with policy, technology and socioeconomic assumptions; quantitative pathways from models; a time horizon; and translation into business or financial impacts.","A list of past losses; a single historical year; a fixed exchange rate; and translation into an accounting restatement of earlier years, with sign-off by the external auditor.","A government licence; a prohibition on external data; a prescribed discount rate; and translation into a regulatory capital charge.","A set of marketing messages; a brand name; a product list; and translation into a customer survey of satisfaction."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> ナラティブと仮定、モデルによる定量経路、時間軸、財務への翻訳が構成要素。<br><br><b>解説</b> シナリオ分析は、(1)政策・技術・社会経済などの仮定とナラティブ、(2)統合評価モデルや気候モデルによる定量的な経路、(3)時間軸（2030・2050など）、(4)結果の事業・財務への影響への翻訳、を要素とする。結果は、戦略の頑健性や資本計画に使う。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 過去の損失、免許、マーケティングは、シナリオ分析の要素ではない。<br><br>【出典】TCFD, Technical Supplement: The Use of Scenario Analysis in Disclosure of Climate-Related Risks and Opportunities, 2017, https://fsb.org/uploads/Technical-Supplement-1.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch7 気候モデルとシナリオ分析","q":"[LO 7.1] What does IFRS S2 require an entity to do regarding climate-related scenario analysis?","h":"気候レジリエンスを評価するために、自社に見合う分析を使います。","c":["Use a single scenario prescribed by the ISSB for all entities to assess their climate resilience, and keep the results confidential.","Use climate-related scenario analysis that is commensurate with its circumstances to assess its climate resilience, and disclose how it was done.","Use scenario analysis only if the entity is a bank, and disclose it only if the regulator requests it in a written notice.","Use scenario analysis only for physical risk, and omit transition risk from the assessment of its climate resilience."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> IFRS S2は、自社の状況に見合う気候シナリオ分析で、レジリエンスを評価し開示することを求める。<br><br><b>解説</b> IFRS S2は、企業の戦略と事業モデルの気候レジリエンスの評価に、企業の状況に見合った（commensurate）気候関連シナリオ分析を用いることを求め、手法・入力・前提・結果などの開示を求める。使えるデータ・技術が限られる企業に対応して、適用は比例的。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> ISSBが単一のシナリオを指定する、銀行のみ、物理リスクのみ、という記述は誤り。<br><br>【出典】IFRS Foundation, IFRS S2 Climate-related Disclosures, https://www.ifrs.org/issued-standards/ifrs-sustainability-standards-navigator/ifrs-s2-climate-related-disclosures/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch7 気候モデルとシナリオ分析","q":"[LO 7.2] According to the IPCC AR6 Synthesis Report (2023), when must global net-zero CO2 emissions be reached to limit warming to 1.5°C (>50%) with no or limited overshoot, and to 2°C (>67%)?","h":"1.5℃は2050年代初め、2℃は2070年代初めです。","c":["Around the early 2050s for 1.5°C and around the early 2070s for 2°C.","Around the early 2070s for 1.5°C and around the early 2050s for 2°C.","Around the early 2030s for 1.5°C and around the early 2040s for 2°C.","Around the early 2080s for 1.5°C and around the early 2090s for 2°C."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 1.5℃では2050年代初め、2℃では2070年代初めにCO2排出正味ゼロ。<br><br><b>解説</b> IPCC AR6統合報告書（2023）は、1.5℃（50%超、オーバーシュートなしまたは限定的）の経路では、世界のCO2排出が2050年代初めに正味ゼロとなり、2℃（67%超）の経路では2070年代初めに正味ゼロとなるとした。温室効果ガス全体では、1.5℃の経路で2070年代初めに正味ゼロとなる。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 年代が入れ替わった、または大きくずれた選択肢は、報告書の内容と合わない。<br><br><b>日本との対応</b> 日本は2020年10月に2050年カーボンニュートラルを宣言した。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, AR6 Synthesis Report: Summary for Policymakers, 2023, https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/syr/ ／ IPCC, AR6 Synthesis Report: Summary for Policymakers, 2023, https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/syr/summary-for-policymakers/ ／ Carbon Brief, Analysis: What the new IPCC report says about how to limit warming to 1.5C or 2C, https://www.carbonbrief.org/analysis-what-the-new-ipcc-report-says-about-how-to-limit-warming-to-1-5c-or-2c/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch7 気候モデルとシナリオ分析","q":"[LO 7.2] Which of the following is classified as a novel (engineered) carbon dioxide removal method rather than a conventional land-based method?","h":"工学的な除去手法を選びます。","c":["Afforestation of previously unforested land.","Direct air carbon capture and storage (DACCS).","Reforestation of recently cleared forest land.","Soil carbon sequestration through improved crop and grazing management."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> DACCSは新しい（工学的な）CDRで、造林・再造林・土壌炭素貯留は従来の陸域の手法。<br><br><b>解説</b> CDRは、従来型の陸域の手法（新規造林・再造林、土壌炭素貯留、森林管理など）と、新しい手法（大気中からのCO2直接回収・貯留（DACCS）、BECCS、風化促進、バイオ炭など）に分けられる。新しい手法は、コストやスケールが課題。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 造林、再造林、土壌炭素貯留は、いずれも従来型。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, AR6 WGIII Chapter 12, https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg3/chapter/chapter-12/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch7 気候モデルとシナリオ分析","q":"[LO 7.2] A fossil-fuel power plant is fitted with CCS that captures 90% of its CO2 emissions. How should this be classified?","h":"大気中のCO2を除去するのではなく、排出を減らす手法です。","c":["It is an emissions reduction, not carbon dioxide removal, because it prevents CO2 from entering the atmosphere rather than removing it from the atmosphere.","It is carbon dioxide removal, because any capture of CO2 at a source removes CO2 from the atmosphere.","It is carbon dioxide removal only if the captured CO2 is sold as a product for use in drinks.","It is neither an emissions reduction nor a removal, because CCS leaves the plant's emissions unchanged, so it is excluded from all emissions accounting by the GHG Protocol and by the IPCC inventory guidelines."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> CCSは排出削減で、CDRは大気中からの除去。<br><br><b>解説</b> 化石燃料の発電所に付けるCCSは、排出の約90%を回収して大気への放出を防ぐ「排出削減」。CDRは、すでに大気中にあるCO2を人為的に除去して貯留する。BECCS（バイオマス＋CCS）やDACCSは、正味で大気から除去できる場合にCDRとなる。ネットゼロでは、残余排出をCDRで相殺する。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> CCSをCDRと同一視する、排出を変えないとする、といった記述は誤り。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, AR6 WGIII Chapter 12, https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg3/chapter/chapter-12/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch7 気候モデルとシナリオ分析","q":"[LO 7.3] In IPCC AR6 scenarios, what does the label 'SSP5-8.5' mean?","h":"SSP5の社会経済ナラティブと、約8.5W/m2の放射強制力の組合せです。","c":["The sustainability socioeconomic pathway (SSP1) combined with a radiative forcing of about 8.5 W/m2 by 2100.","The fossil-fuelled development socioeconomic pathway (SSP5) combined with a radiative forcing of about 8.5 W/m2 by 2100.","The fossil-fuelled development socioeconomic pathway (SSP5) combined with a temperature rise of exactly 8.5°C by 2100.","The regional rivalry socioeconomic pathway (SSP3) combined with a radiative forcing of about 8.5 W/m2 by 2100."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> SSP5-8.5＝化石燃料依存の発展と、2100年に約8.5W/m2の放射強制力。<br><br><b>解説</b> AR6のシナリオは、SSP（共有社会経済経路）の番号と、2100年頃の放射強制力（W/m2）を組み合わせて表す。SSP1：持続可能性、SSP2：中庸、SSP3：地域対立、SSP4：不平等、SSP5：化石燃料依存の発展。SSP5-8.5は、排出量が最も多い高排出のシナリオ。8.5は気温ではなく、W/m2。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> SSP1・SSP3との取り違え、8.5を気温（℃）とする誤りに注意。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, AR6 WGI Chapter 1, https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg1/chapter/chapter-1/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch7 気候モデルとシナリオ分析","q":"[LO 7.3] Which description of SSP3 ('regional rivalry') is correct?","h":"緩和と適応の両方が難しい世界のシナリオです。","c":["A world with low challenges to both mitigation and adaptation, with strong global cooperation, rapid growth and low population in all regions, with equal incomes across countries.","A world with low challenges to mitigation and high challenges to adaptation, with a rapid global shift to renewable energy and equal incomes.","A world with high challenges to both mitigation and adaptation, with resurgent nationalism, slow economic growth and rapid population growth in developing regions.","A world with high challenges to mitigation only, with fossil-fuel-intensive growth and strong institutions that make adaptation easy."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> SSP3は、地域対立で、緩和・適応の両方の課題が大きい。<br><br><b>解説</b> SSP3（Regional Rivalry、A Rocky Road）は、ナショナリズムの再燃、国際協力の停滞、低成長、途上国での人口増加が特徴で、緩和と適応の双方の課題が高い。SSP1は両方の課題が低く、SSP5は緩和の課題が高いが適応の課題は低い。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 他の選択肢は、SSP1・SSP5などの特徴を混ぜたもの。<br><br>【出典】O'Neill et al., The roads ahead: Narratives for shared socioeconomic pathways, Global Environmental Change, 2017, https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0959378015000060"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch7 気候モデルとシナリオ分析","q":"[LO 7.3] Why does IPCC AR6 combine SSPs with radiative forcing levels (e.g., SSP2-4.5)?","h":"放射強制力だけでは社会経済の道筋が決まらないためです。","c":["Because a forcing level alone fixes the exact policy mix, so combining it with an SSP is only a labelling convention and carries no other meaning, which means that policies are chosen by governments.","Because an SSP alone specifies the forcing in W/m2, so combining it with a forcing level is a duplication that is kept for historical reasons.","Because a forcing level alone does not specify the socioeconomic route, so combining it with an SSP allows different societal routes to the same forcing to be explored.","Because forcing levels and SSPs are produced by different regulators, so a combination is required by law for any climate disclosure."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 同じ強制力に至る社会経済の道筋が複数あるため、SSPと組み合わせる。<br><br><b>解説</b> RCPは濃度・放射強制力の経路だけを示し、社会経済の前提は指定しない。SSPは社会経済のナラティブを与える。AR6は、この2つを組み合わせたSSP-RCP（SSP1-1.9、SSP1-2.6、SSP2-4.5、SSP3-7.0、SSP5-8.5など）で、同じ放射強制力に至る複数の社会経済経路を検討できるようにした。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> RCPが政策の組合せを決める、SSPが強制力を決める、法的な要請、という記述は誤り。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, AR6 WGI Chapter 1, https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg1/chapter/chapter-1/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch7 気候モデルとシナリオ分析","q":"[LO 7.4] Which statement about the IEA Net Zero Emissions by 2050 (NZE) scenario is correct?","h":"2050年のネットゼロと、1.5℃の約50%の確率に対応する経路です。","c":["It shows a pathway to net-zero energy-sector CO2 emissions by 2070 that gives roughly a 100% chance of limiting warming to 1.5°C with no overshoot.","It forecasts the energy mix that will result from policies governments have announced, without reaching net zero in any year.","It shows a pathway to net-zero energy-sector CO2 emissions by 2050 that gives roughly a 50% chance of limiting warming to 1.5°C with no or limited overshoot.","It shows a pathway that holds warming to 3°C with a 67% chance, with no net-zero target for the energy sector."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> NZEは、2050年のエネルギー部門CO2正味ゼロで、1.5℃を約50%の確率で達成する。<br><br><b>解説</b> IEAのNZEシナリオ（2021年に初公表、2023年に更新）は、2050年までにエネルギー部門のCO2排出を正味ゼロにする規範的な経路で、1.5℃以内に抑える確率が約50%（IEAは2021年の初版で『even chance』と表現）の経路である。IEAが「予測ではなく」目標から逆算するシナリオ。発表済みの政策を反映するのはSTEPS、公約の完全な実現を仮定するのはAPS。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 2070年・100%、既存政策の予測、3℃・67%などの記述は、NZEの内容と異なる。<br><br>【出典】IEA, Net Zero Roadmap: A Global Pathway to Keep the 1.5°C Goal in Reach, 2023 update, https://www.iea.org/reports/net-zero-roadmap-a-global-pathway-to-keep-the-15-0c-goal-in-reach"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch7 気候モデルとシナリオ分析","q":"[LO 7.4] The NGFS climate scenarios are produced using which set of models?","h":"複数の統合評価モデルが、共通の前提で使われています。","c":["A single in-house model of the European Central Bank, which is not available to any other central bank or supervisor, and has never been published by the ECB.","Three integrated assessment models (GCAM, MESSAGEix-GLOBIOM and REMIND-MAgPIE), with macroeconomic impacts computed by a separate macro model.","The IPCC's general circulation models alone, with no economic or energy-system model used at any stage.","A set of bank-specific credit models, supplied by each reporting bank for its own loan book."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> NGFSのシナリオは、GCAM、MESSAGEix-GLOBIOM、REMIND-MAgPIEの3つの統合評価モデルで作成される。<br><br><b>解説</b> NGFSシナリオは、3つの統合評価モデル（GCAM、MESSAGEix-GLOBIOM、REMIND-MAgPIE）で、エネルギー、土地利用、排出の経路を算出し、マクロ経済への影響は別のマクロ経済モデル（NiGEMなど）で推計する。結果は、IIASAが運営するNGFS Scenario Explorerで公開される。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> ECB単独のモデルや、気候モデルのみ、銀行ごとの信用モデル、という記述は誤り。<br><br>【出典】NGFS, NGFS Climate Scenarios for central banks and supervisors, https://www.ngfs.net/ngfs-scenarios-portal/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch7 気候モデルとシナリオ分析","q":"[LO 7.4] According to the IEA's 2021 'Net Zero by 2050' roadmap, which feature distinguishes its NZE pathway regarding new fossil-fuel supply?","h":"新規の化石燃料の開発は不要とされました。","c":["It requires several hundred new oil and gas fields by 2030, and it requires coal plants to be built in every region.","It requires no new oil and gas fields beyond those already approved for development, and no new unabated coal plants.","It requires a doubling of oil production by 2050, and it needs a high use of coal without carbon capture.","It requires no changes to the existing energy system, because demand for fossil fuels is assumed to be constant."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> NZEでは、すでに承認された案件を超える新規油ガス田や、排出削減対策のない新規石炭火力は不要。<br><br><b>解説</b> IEAの『Net Zero by 2050』（2021年）は、NZEの経路では、すでに承認済みの案件を超える新規の油・ガス田の開発や、排出削減対策のない新規の石炭火力は必要ないとした。需要の急減により、既存の油ガス田からの供給でも賄えるため。この結論は、エネルギー業界に大きな議論を呼んだ。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 油ガス田の新設、石油生産の倍増、現状維持は、NZEの内容と合わない。<br><br>【出典】IEA, Net Zero by 2050: A Roadmap for the Global Energy Sector, 2021, https://www.iea.org/reports/net-zero-by-2050"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch7 気候モデルとシナリオ分析","q":"[LO 7.5] In scenario analysis for a bank's loan book, what is the difference between a static and a dynamic balance sheet assumption?","h":"経営の対応を織り込むかどうかです。","c":["A static balance sheet allows the bank to change its portfolio freely, whereas a dynamic balance sheet freezes the book at its initial composition, throughout the entire analysis horizon.","A static balance sheet uses only the bank's equity, whereas a dynamic balance sheet uses only the bank's deposits.","A static balance sheet is used for physical risk only, whereas a dynamic balance sheet is used for transition risk only.","A static balance sheet keeps the size and composition of the book constant, whereas a dynamic balance sheet lets management actions and portfolio changes occur over the horizon."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 静的は構成を固定、動的は経営の対応や構成の変化を織り込む。<br><br><b>解説</b> 静的バランスシートでは、分析期間を通じて資産の規模・構成が一定とする。動的バランスシートでは、経営陣の対応（貸出の見直し、ポートフォリオの入替え）を織り込む。静的は、対応前のリスクの大きさを示し、動的は、現実的な対応を踏まえた影響を示す。どちらを使うかは、分析の目的に応じて選ぶ。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 静的と動的を入れ替えた記述や、物理・移行に割り当てる記述は誤り。<br><br>【出典】BoE, Results of the 2021 Climate Biennial Exploratory Scenario, https://www.bankofengland.co.uk/stress-testing/2022/results-of-the-2021-climate-biennial-exploratory-scenario"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch7 気候モデルとシナリオ分析","q":"[LO 7.5] Why does the choice of time horizon matter differently for transition and physical risk scenarios?","h":"物理リスクのシナリオ間の差は、後半の数十年に開きます。","c":["Physical outcomes across scenarios diverge mainly in later decades, so horizons to 2050 or beyond are needed, whereas transition effects can arise sooner.","Physical outcomes across scenarios diverge mainly in the first year, so a one-year horizon is sufficient, whereas transition effects arise only after 2100.","Time horizon never matters, because all scenarios give the same results in any year, whatever the policy and technology assumptions.","Time horizon matters only for transition risk, because physical risk is fully determined by past weather and does not depend on future emissions."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 物理リスクは後半の数十年で差が開き、移行リスクは早期にも生じる。<br><br><b>解説</b> シナリオ間の気温や物理的ハザードの差は、2050年以降に大きくなる（短期は過去の排出に左右される）。そのため、物理リスクは少なくとも2050年、可能なら2100年までの時間軸が必要。移行リスクは、政策・技術の変化が数年〜10年で影響するため、短中期も重要。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 1年のみ、時間軸は無関係、移行のみ、という記述は誤り。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, AR6 WGI Summary for Policymakers, 2021, https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg1/chapter/summary-for-policymakers/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch7 気候モデルとシナリオ分析","q":"[LO 7.5] Under the 2017 TCFD recommendations, which scenario choice should an organisation make when describing the resilience of its strategy?","h":"2℃以下のシナリオを含む、複数のシナリオを検討します。","c":["Consider different climate-related scenarios, including a 2°C or lower scenario.","Consider a single scenario of 4°C or higher, because lower scenarios do not affect business strategy.","Consider only the scenario that the entity expects to be the most likely, to avoid the cost of analysing the others.","Consider only scenarios published by the entity's own industry association, because other sources are not accepted."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> TCFDは、2℃以下を含む複数のシナリオでの戦略のレジリエンスの開示を提言した。<br><br><b>解説</b> TCFDの提言（戦略c）は、2℃以下のシナリオを含む、さまざまな気候関連シナリオを考慮した組織の戦略のレジリエンスの記述を求めた。単一のシナリオや、最も可能性の高いシナリオのみ、業界団体のシナリオのみ、といった選び方は推奨されない。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 4℃のみ、最も可能性の高いもののみ、業界団体のもののみ、は提言と異なる。<br><br>【出典】TCFD, Recommendations of the TCFD, 2017, https://www.fsb-tcfd.org/recommendations/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch7 気候モデルとシナリオ分析","q":"[LO 7.6] A company emits 500,000 tCO2e a year. Under a transition scenario with a carbon price of USD 80 per tonne, 30% of its emissions are covered by free allowances and it can pass 25% of the resulting cost on to customers. What is its net annual carbon cost?","h":"無償割当を除いた排出量に価格を掛け、転嫁分を引きます。","c":["USD 21.0 million.","USD 28.0 million.","USD 40.0 million.","USD 30.0 million."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> (1−0.3)×50万t×80ドル＝2,800万ドル、転嫁25%を引いて2,100万ドル。<br><br><b>解説</b> 課税対象の排出量＝500,000×(1−0.30)＝350,000t。コスト＝350,000×80＝28.0百万ドル。顧客への転嫁25%を引くと、純コスト＝28.0×0.75＝21.0百万ドル。28.0は転嫁を考慮していない値、40.0は無償割当・転嫁とも考慮していない値、30.0は無償割当を忘れて転嫁だけ引いた値(40×0.75)。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 28.0は転嫁なし、40.0は両方なし、30.0は無償割当を無視した値。<br><br><b>日本との対応</b> 日本のGX-ETSでは、2026年度から直接排出量が年10万tCO2以上の事業者に参加が義務づけられ、排出枠は一定の基準で無償割当される。<br><br>【出典】経済産業省, GX-ETS（排出量取引制度）リーフレット, https://www.meti.go.jp/policy/energy_environment/global_warming/ets_leaflet.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch7 気候モデルとシナリオ分析","q":"[LO 7.6] Which description of top-down versus bottom-up transition risk assessment is correct?","h":"マクロ・セクターの出力を使うか、企業ごとの財務モデルを使うかです。","c":["Top-down models each company's costs, revenues and balance sheet individually, whereas bottom-up applies sector- or macro-level scenario outputs to portfolios.","Top-down uses only physical hazard maps, whereas bottom-up uses only the carbon price series of an emissions trading system.","Top-down applies sector- or macro-level scenario outputs to portfolios, whereas bottom-up models each company's costs, revenues and balance sheet individually.","Top-down and bottom-up are identical, because both use only the name of the company's auditor and the year of its listing."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> トップダウンはセクター・マクロの出力、ボトムアップは企業ごとのモデル。<br><br><b>解説</b> 移行リスクの分析には、シナリオのセクター・マクロの出力（炭素価格、エネルギー構成、需要）をポートフォリオに適用するトップダウンと、個々の企業の費用・収益・バランスシートをモデル化するボトムアップがある。前者は、広い範囲を効率的に分析でき、後者は詳細で、データと工数が多い。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> トップダウンとボトムアップを入れ替えた記述、ハザードマップ・炭素価格のみ、同一、は誤り。<br><br>【出典】NGFS, Guide to climate scenario analysis for central banks and supervisors, https://www.ngfs.net/en/publications-and-statistics/publications/guide-climate-scenario-analysis-central-banks-and-supervisors"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch7 気候モデルとシナリオ分析","q":"[LO 7.6] What is the NGFS Scenario Explorer?","h":"NGFSシナリオの結果を、地域・年別に公開するプラットフォームです。","c":["A software tool that computes each bank's regulatory capital requirement from the bank's own accounting data under Basel rules.","A government register in which companies must file their annual emissions reports and receive a compliance certificate.","A trading venue in which allowances under a national emissions trading scheme are bought and sold between companies.","An online platform, hosted by IIASA, that provides NGFS scenario outputs such as carbon prices, energy mix and GDP by region and year."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> NGFS Scenario Explorerは、シナリオの出力（炭素価格・エネルギー構成・GDP）を公開する。<br><br><b>解説</b> NGFS Scenario Explorerは、IIASAが運営するオンラインのプラットフォームで、NGFSシナリオの結果（炭素価格、排出量、エネルギー構成、GDPなど）を、地域・年別に提供する。金融機関・当局が、移行リスクの分析の入力として利用する。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 資本要件の計算ソフト、排出報告の登録簿、取引所は、Scenario Explorerとは別のもの。<br><br>【出典】NGFS, NGFS Scenario Portal, https://www.ngfs.net/ngfs-scenarios-portal/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch7 気候モデルとシナリオ分析","q":"[LO 7.7] Why is downscaling used when assessing physical climate risk for a specific asset?","h":"全球モデルは粗い解像度のため、地域・地点の情報に詳細化します。","c":["Global climate models have a resolution of a few metres, so their output must be downscaled to remove excess detail from the output.","Global climate models cover only the ocean, so their output must be downscaled to produce estimates for land-based assets.","Global climate models are regulated by law, so their output must be downscaled to meet a national reporting format.","Global climate models have coarse resolution, so their output must be downscaled to represent local hazards at the asset's location."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 全球モデルは解像度が粗いため、資産の位置に合わせてダウンスケーリングする。<br><br><b>解説</b> 全球気候モデル（GCM）や地球システムモデル（ESM）の格子は、通常、数十〜数百kmで、地点の洪水・暴風・猛暑を直接表すには粗い。力学的または統計的なダウンスケーリングで、地域・地点の情報に詳細化する。ただし、ダウンスケーリングは不確実性を完全に取り除くわけではない。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 数メートルの解像度、海のみ、法的な形式、は誤り。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, AR6 WGI Chapter 10, https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg1/chapter/chapter-10/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch7 気候モデルとシナリオ分析","q":"[LO 7.7] In the catastrophe-model style chain used to estimate physical risk losses, which sequence of components is correct?","h":"ハザード→曝露→脆弱性→財務損失の順です。","c":["Financial loss, hazard, exposure, and vulnerability (damage function).","Hazard, exposure, vulnerability (damage function), and financial loss.","Exposure, financial loss, hazard, and vulnerability (damage function).","Vulnerability, financial loss, exposure, and hazard (damage function)."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> ハザード、曝露、脆弱性（損害関数）、財務損失の順。<br><br><b>解説</b> 物理リスクの評価やカタストロフィ・モデルは、(1)ハザード（洪水・暴風などの強度と頻度）、(2)曝露（資産の位置と価値）、(3)脆弱性（損害関数：ハザードの強度と損害の関係）、(4)財務（保険・免責などを考慮した損失）の順で構成される。気候シナリオは、ハザードの部分に反映される。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 財務損失を先に置く並びは、因果の順に合わない。<br><br>【出典】ECB, Results of the 2022 climate risk stress test (press release), 2022, https://www.bankingsupervision.europa.eu/press/pr/date/2022/html/ssm.pr220708~565c38d18a.en.html ／ NGFS, Guide to climate scenario analysis for central banks and supervisors, https://www.ngfs.net/en/publications-and-statistics/publications/guide-climate-scenario-analysis-central-banks-and-supervisors"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch7 気候モデルとシナリオ分析","q":"[LO 7.7] Which is a recognised limitation of using climate models for physical risk assessment?","h":"ティッピング・ポイントや複合事象を十分に表せない点です。","c":["Models represent every tipping point and compound event exactly, so tail losses are overstated relative to observations.","Models produce a single exact value for each location, so no uncertainty range needs to be reported with them.","Models are based only on future emissions, so they cannot be compared with any observation from the past.","Models may not fully capture tipping points and compound events, so tail losses from physical risk may be understated."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> ティッピング・ポイントや複合事象が十分に表現されず、損失の裾野を過小評価し得る。<br><br><b>解説</b> 気候モデルは、氷床の崩壊などのティッピング・ポイント、複数のハザードが重なる複合事象、局地的な極端現象（雹、対流性の嵐）を十分に表せず、物理リスクの損失の裾野を過小評価し得る。また、結果には幅があり、複数のモデル（アンサンブル）で不確実性を示す。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 全てを正確に表現する、単一の値で十分、過去の観測と比較できない、は誤り。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, AR6 WGI Chapter 4, https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg1/chapter/chapter-4/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch7 気候モデルとシナリオ分析","q":"[LO 7.8] How might an oil and gas company use climate scenario analysis in its strategy and financial planning?","h":"低需要・高炭素価格のシナリオで、投資案件の価値を検証します。","c":["Forecast next quarter's earnings per share with a single scenario, to guide the quarterly dividend for the next period, and to report it to the stock exchange.","Calculate the physical risk of its customers' homes, to set the premiums that it charges on their home insurance.","Test the value of its project portfolio and asset carrying amounts under lower-demand and higher-carbon-price scenarios, to guide capital allocation.","Determine the capital requirement of its lending book, to report the ratio to its banking supervisor each quarter."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 低需要・高炭素価格のシナリオで、投資案件と資産価値を検証する。<br><br><b>解説</b> 非金融企業（石油・ガスなど）は、シナリオ分析を、戦略のレジリエンスの確認、設備投資の優先順位、資産の減損テストの前提、サプライチェーン・拠点の立地などに使う。需要の減少、炭素価格、技術のコストといった前提を変えて、事業価値の変化を比較する。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 四半期の1株益予測、住宅保険の料率設定、銀行の資本要件は、石油・ガス会社の用途ではない。<br><br>【出典】TCFD, Guidance on Scenario Analysis for Non-Financial Companies, 2020, https://www.fsb.org/wp-content/uploads/P291020-3.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch7 気候モデルとシナリオ分析","q":"[LO 7.8] Under the Solvency II ORSA, which expectation did EIOPA set for insurers regarding climate scenarios (2021 Opinion)?","h":"ORSAに、気候変動シナリオを組み込むことが求められます。","c":["Insurers should include climate change risk scenarios in their Own Risk and Solvency Assessment, covering at least short-term and long-term time horizons.","Insurers should exclude climate change risk from their Own Risk and Solvency Assessment, since it falls outside the scope of Solvency II, and national supervisors confirmed this exclusion in 2022.","Insurers should run one climate scenario in the Own Risk and Solvency Assessment, and keep it separate from capital planning.","Insurers should replace the Own Risk and Solvency Assessment with the European Central Bank's climate stress test for banks."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> EIOPAは、ORSAに気候変動のシナリオ分析を含めることを求めた。<br><br><b>解説</b> EIOPAの2021年4月の意見書は、保険会社が、固有のリスクとソルベンシー評価（ORSA）に、気候変動リスクのシナリオを、短期・長期の時間軸で含めることを求め、長期では少なくとも、気温上昇が2℃未満の経路と2℃超の経路の2つのシナリオで重要な気候リスクを検証するよう求めた。保険会社は、資産・負債の両面で、物理リスクと移行リスクを分析する。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 除外、1シナリオのみ、ECBの銀行向けテストへの置換、は意見書と異なる。<br><br>【出典】EIOPA, Opinion on the supervision of the use of climate change risk scenarios in ORSA, 2021, https://www.eiopa.europa.eu/publications/opinion-supervision-use-climate-change-risk-scenarios-orsa_en"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch7 気候モデルとシナリオ分析","q":"[LO 7.8] How can an electric utility use scenario analysis in its integrated resource planning?","h":"需要・炭素価格・技術コストのシナリオで、発電設備の計画を検討します。","c":["Fix the fuel mix of all of its plants to its current level, since any change under scenarios would breach the supply license.","Compare generation and grid investment plans under scenarios for demand, carbon prices and technology costs, to choose a plan that remains robust across them.","Estimate the credit risk of its retail customers with a single scenario, in order to set the bank deposit rates for their savings, and to plan its staffing at each branch.","Forecast the weather of the next week at each plant location, to schedule the daily rotation of its employees."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 需要・炭素価格・技術コストのシナリオで、発電・送電の投資計画を比較する。<br><br><b>解説</b> 電力会社は、統合資源計画（IRP）で、電力需要、炭素価格、再エネ・蓄電池のコスト、政策などのシナリオを組み合わせ、発電・系統の投資計画が、複数のシナリオで頑健（robust）かを比較する。物理リスク（猛暑・洪水・渇水）も、設備や立地の計画に反映する。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 燃料構成の固定、預金金利の設定、翌週の天気予報は、シナリオ分析の用途ではない。<br><br>【出典】TCFD, Guidance on Scenario Analysis for Non-Financial Companies, 2020, https://www.fsb.org/wp-content/uploads/P291020-3.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch7 気候モデルとシナリオ分析","q":"[LO 7.9] Which statement correctly differentiates the inputs of transition and physical risk scenarios?","h":"移行は政策・技術・市場の前提、物理は気候の経路とハザードが中心です。","c":["Transition scenarios are built on hazard intensity and sea-level maps, whereas physical scenarios rely on policy, technology and market assumptions, as published in the IPCC's latest assessment report.","Transition scenarios and physical scenarios use the same inputs, because both depend only on the company's balance sheet.","Transition scenarios rely only on historical data, whereas physical scenarios rely only on the opinions of local residents.","Transition scenarios are built on policy, technology and market assumptions such as carbon prices, whereas physical scenarios rely on climate pathways and hazard intensity."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 移行は政策・技術・市場の前提、物理は気候の経路とハザードの強度が入力。<br><br><b>解説</b> 移行リスクのシナリオは、炭素価格、規制、技術コスト、需要の変化などの前提に基づく。物理リスクのシナリオは、RCP/SSPなどの気候の経路から導かれるハザード（洪水、熱波、海面上昇など）の強度と頻度に基づく。両者を並べて考えるが、入力は異なる。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 入力の入れ替えや、同一、過去データのみ、住民の意見のみ、という記述は誤り。<br><br>【出典】NGFS, Guide to climate scenario analysis for central banks and supervisors, https://www.ngfs.net/en/publications-and-statistics/publications/guide-climate-scenario-analysis-central-banks-and-supervisors"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch7 気候モデルとシナリオ分析","q":"[LO 7.9] Which statement about spatial granularity is correct when comparing physical and transition risk scenario analysis?","h":"物理リスクは、資産の位置まで見る必要があります。","c":["Physical risk analysis can be done using only the country of the company's headquarters, whereas transition risk requires the exact coordinates of each asset, because it varies sharply between neighbouring sites.","Physical risk analysis generally needs asset-level location data, whereas transition risk can often be assessed at sector or regional level using emissions and technology data.","Neither type of analysis needs any information on where the assets or activities are located, because risks are the same everywhere.","Both types of analysis require the home address of each shareholder, because risks depend on the owner's place of residence."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 物理リスクは資産の位置情報が必要で、移行リスクはセクター・地域の水準でも可能。<br><br><b>解説</b> 物理リスクは、同じ国でも洪水・熱波の曝露が地点ごとに大きく異なるため、資産（工場・店舗・担保物件）の位置情報が必要。移行リスクは、セクター・地域の排出量、技術、政策に基づき、セクターや地域の水準でも分析できる（ただし企業ごとの差は大きい）。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 本社所在地のみ、場所は不要、株主の住所、という記述は誤り。<br><br>【出典】NGFS, Guide to climate scenario analysis for central banks and supervisors, https://www.ngfs.net/en/publications-and-statistics/publications/guide-climate-scenario-analysis-central-banks-and-supervisors"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch7 気候モデルとシナリオ分析","q":"[LO 7.9] What trade-off between transition and physical risk is typically shown when comparing scenarios?","h":"緩和が弱いと移行は小さく物理は大、強いと逆になる傾向です。","c":["A scenario with limited mitigation shows high transition risk and low physical risk, whereas an ambitious scenario shows no transition risk and no physical risk, because it prevents any adjustment cost.","A scenario with limited mitigation shows low transition risk but high physical risk, whereas an ambitious scenario shows higher near-term transition risk but lower long-run physical risk.","Every scenario shows the same level of both transition and physical risk, because the risk depends only on the year of analysis.","A scenario with ambitious mitigation shows the highest physical risk, because lower emissions always cause faster warming in the long run."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 緩和が弱いと移行リスクは小さいが物理リスクが大きく、強いと移行は大きいが物理は小さい。<br><br><b>解説</b> シナリオの比較では、緩和が不十分な「ホットハウス」では、移行リスクは小さいが、長期の物理リスクが大きくなる。野心的な緩和のネットゼロ経路では、早期の移行リスク（特に無秩序な移行）が大きいが、長期の物理リスクは小さい。この両者のトレードオフを、NGFSのシナリオ（秩序ある移行、無秩序な移行、ホットハウス）が示す。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 緩和が弱い場合に移行リスクが大きい、全てのシナリオで同じ、緩和が強いと物理リスクが最大、は誤り。<br><br>【出典】NGFS, NGFS Climate Scenarios, https://www.ngfs.net/ngfs-scenarios-portal/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch7 気候モデルとシナリオ分析","q":"[LO 7.10] Which use of climate scenario analysis is characteristic of a bank rather than a non-financial company?","h":"貸出ポートフォリオの損失と資本への影響の分析です。","c":["Choosing the location of a new factory on the basis of the flood hazard at each candidate site.","Testing the net present value of its product line under a high carbon price and a low-demand scenario, before it decides on its next-year budget.","Reviewing its supply chain for concentration in regions that are prone to drought and heat waves.","Estimating climate-adjusted probabilities of default and losses across the loan book, and testing the bank's capital adequacy."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 貸出ポートフォリオのPD・損失と、資本の十分性の分析は、銀行に特徴的な用途。<br><br><b>解説</b> 銀行は、シナリオ分析で、貸出先の業種・地域別のPD/LGDの変化、貸出ポートフォリオの損失、資本の十分性、セクター別の与信方針を検討する。工場の立地、製品ラインのNPV、サプライチェーンの集中度の確認は、非金融企業の用途。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 他の3つは、非金融企業の事業・投資の判断。<br><br>【出典】ECB, Results of the 2022 climate risk stress test (press release), 2022, https://www.bankingsupervision.europa.eu/press/pr/date/2022/html/ssm.pr220708~565c38d18a.en.html ／ Bank of England, Results of the 2021 Climate Biennial Exploratory Scenario, https://www.bankofengland.co.uk/stress-testing/2022/results-of-the-2021-climate-biennial-exploratory-scenario"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch7 気候モデルとシナリオ分析","q":"[LO 7.10] Which use of scenario analysis is specific to a property and casualty insurer?","h":"自然災害の損失の期待値と再保険の必要量の見直しです。","c":["Choosing which fossil-fuel project to approve on the basis of its internal rate of return under different oil prices, as approved by its board of directors.","Testing whether a new bank branch should be located in a city centre or a suburb under different transit plans.","Assessing how expected annual catastrophe losses and reinsurance needs change for its property portfolio under different warming scenarios.","Determining the most profitable crop for a farm under different rainfall levels in the coming decades."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 温暖化シナリオ別に、期待年間損失と再保険の必要量を見直すのが、損保の用途。<br><br><b>解説</b> 損害保険会社は、気候シナリオに基づき、洪水・暴風などの期待年間損失の変化、引受方針、価格、再保険の設計、準備金や資本の要件を検討する。石油プロジェクトの承認、店舗の立地、農作物の選択は、保険会社の用途ではない。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 他の3つは、石油会社、小売、農家の意思決定。<br><br>【出典】EIOPA, Opinion on the supervision of the use of climate change risk scenarios in ORSA, 2021, https://www.eiopa.europa.eu/publications/opinion-supervision-use-climate-change-risk-scenarios-orsa_en"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch7 気候モデルとシナリオ分析","q":"[LO 7.10] How would an asset manager typically use climate scenario analysis?","h":"保有銘柄の評価がどう変わるかを調べ、配分や対話に活かします。","c":["Assess how the valuations of its holdings change under scenarios, to guide asset allocation and to prioritise engagement with the most exposed companies.","Set the premium for each policyholder in a home insurance book, to guide the reinsurance programme for its property exposures.","Determine the capital requirement of a bank's loan book, to report to its prudential supervisor under Basel rules each quarter, and publish the ratios in its annual report.","Plan the capacity of a power plant fleet over the next thirty years, to guide the construction of new transmission lines."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 保有銘柄の評価の変化を調べ、資産配分とエンゲージメントの優先順位づけに使う。<br><br><b>解説</b> 資産運用会社は、シナリオ別に、保有資産の価値の変化（移行リスクの高いセクター、物理リスクの高い地域）を分析し、資産配分、銘柄選定、エンゲージメントの優先順位づけ、顧客への報告に使う。保険料の設定、銀行の資本要件、発電設備の計画は、他の業種の用途。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 他の3つは、保険会社、銀行、電力会社の用途。<br><br>【出典】TCFD, Implementing the Recommendations of the TCFD, 2021, https://assets.bbhub.io/company/sites/60/2021/07/2021-TCFD-Implementing_Guidance.pdf"}
];
